E["item:alaric-s-remains"] = {t="item",n="Alaric's Remains",z="silverpine",s="Alaric's bones lie in a shallow grave in Silverpine Forest, far from Fenris Isle. His spirit asks travelers to carry them past the Rot Hide gnolls and directly into Fenris Keep.",h="Alaric's bones lie in a shallow grave in Silverpine Forest, far from Fenris Isle.",sec={{t="A Final Request",b="Alaric's bones were unearthed from a shallow grave in Silverpine Forest. He was once a resident of Fenris Isle, and his spirit longs for the place he cherished in life. He asks whoever finds his bones to leave his ill-fitting boots behind and carry his remains directly into Fenris Keep, far from the scavengers prowling the mainland.",sp=0},{t="The Alcove in the Keep",b="Alaric guides the carrier to the southwestern tower of Fenris Keep, past the infested lower grounds and into a quiet chamber. Behind a dusty shelf lies a hidden niche with an artifact once valued by Thule Ravenclaw and his fellow mages. In return for a quiet resting place beyond the Rot Hide gnolls, Alaric gives the hidden trinkets to those who carry his bones home.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Who was Alaric?",a="Alaric once lived in Fenris Keep, where he spent what he considered the finest days of his life. After his death, he was buried in a shallow grave in Silverpine Forest, and his spirit now asks a passerby to carry his bones home.",al={"who is alaric","alaric lore","who was this guy"},it="identity"},{q="Where are Alaric's remains supposed to go?",a="Alaric's remains belong in a concealed alcove behind a dusty shelf in the southwestern tower of Fenris Keep on Fenris Isle.",al={"where do i bring alaric","dusty shelf location","where is the niche"},it="target"},{q="Why does Alaric want his remains sealed behind a shelf?",a="Fenris Keep brought Alaric comfort in life, and he wants to rest within its stone walls instead of in a dirt ditch. He also wants the alcove sealed to protect his bones from the Rot Hide gnolls roaming the keep.",al={"why fenris keep","why the niche","why hide the body"},it="purpose"},{q="Why did he say to leave his boots behind?",a="Alaric said his boots never fit him in life, so he asked that they be left behind when his bones were carried from the shallow grave.",al={"leave the boots","alaric's boots","boots never fit"}},{q="What is inside the hidden alcove besides a resting place?",a="The hidden niche holds an item once treasured by Thule Ravenclaw and his former associates, along with magical belongings Alaric gives to anyone who carries his remains to rest.",al={"hidden niche treasure","what is behind the shelf","thule's item"}},{q="What are Alaric's Remains?",a="These are the physical bones and bodily remnants of Alaric, a former inhabitant of Fenris Keep who died and was hastily buried in Silverpine Forest. His lingering spirit retains consciousness within his bones, urging travelers to recover him from the dirt so he can find a final, peaceful resting place.",al={"what is alarics remains","alaric corpse","alarics remains item"},it="identity",add="7c652925"},{q="Where do Alaric's Remains come from?",a="You exhume them from a crude, shallow grave dug in the wilderness of Silverpine Forest, minus the ill-fitting boots he was buried in. Alaric perished out in the wilds away from his former home, leaving his unhallowed remains trapped in the earth until someone unearthed him.",al={"where did alaric die","shallow grave alaric","who made alarics remains"},it="origin",add="6447c1c8"},{q="Why does Alaric want his remains recovered?",a="Alaric spent the happiest years of his life inside Fenris Keep, and resting in the wilds brings him no peace. He wants his remains brought back to the keep and tucked securely inside a hidden alcove behind a dusty bookshelf, safe from the scavenging Rot Hide gnolls infesting the grounds.",al={"why take alarics remains","why does alaric want his body moved","why move alaric"},it="why_wanted",add="5f3dd52d"}},ang={["race:Undead"]="As a Forsaken traveler, you may understand a spirit whose mortal rest was disturbed. Alaric seeks peaceful seclusion, not service under the Dark Lady.",["class:Mage"]="As a mage, you may recognize the cache Alaric reveals as relics connected to Thule Ravenclaw and the Dalaran-trained arcanists who once studied and schemed inside Fenris Keep."},kw={"alaric","alaric's remains","fenris keep","rot hide","shallow grave","silverpine forest","the hidden niche","thule ravenclaw"},rel={"quest:461","quest:460","subzone:fenris-keep","zone:silverpine","quest:491"},src={"Alaric's Remains","The Hidden Niche"}}
E["item:ataeric-s-staff"] = {t="item",n="Ataeric's Staff",z="silverpine",s="At the Sepulcher, Ataeric's Staff marks the archmage's defeat. Archmage Ataeric, a senior Dalaran wizard in Silverpine Forest, wielded it to command local ley lines.",h="At the Sepulcher, Ataeric's Staff marks the archmage's defeat.",sec={{t="Trophy of the Sepulcher",b="Shadow Priest Allister feared Dalaran's growing reach in magic and ordered Ataeric killed. He also demanded the staff. Once Ataeric was slain and the staff recovered, the concentrated ley energies sank back into dormancy. Carrying the staff to the Sepulcher marked a clear victory over Dalaran's ambitions. Yet power still lies latent in the earth, and the Forsaken remain watchful.",sp=0},{t="A Conduit of Ley Magic",b="Archmage Ataeric carried the staff to direct ley energies in southern Silverpine Forest. Dalaran sent him to awaken an ancient ley node near the borders of its territory. The staff helped him weave the vast currents around him, making the archmage a grave threat to nearby Forsaken settlements.",sp=1,bt={"q477.3"}}},faq={{q="Who does Ataeric's Staff belong to?",a="Archmage Ataeric, a senior Dalaran wizard stationed in Silverpine Forest, owned the staff. He was there to oversee the awakening of a powerful ley node.",al={"who owns ataerics staff","ataeric owner","who dropped this staff"},sp=1,it="identity",bt={"q477.3"}},{q="Why does Shadow Priest Allister want Ataeric's Staff?",a="Shadow Priest Allister at the Sepulcher wants the staff as proof that Archmage Ataeric is dead. He also seeks to break Dalaran's efforts to command the region's ley lines.",al={"why allister want staff","staff purpose sepulcher","who takes the staff"},it="why_wanted"},{q="What happens once the staff is taken from Archmage Ataeric?",a="When Ataeric is slain and the staff taken, the ley energies Dalaran had woven dissipate and sink into dormancy. The immediate magical threat to the Forsaken ends.",al={"what happens to the ley line","after defeating ataeric"},sp=1,it="purpose"},{q="Where is Ataeric's Staff found?",a="Archmage Ataeric's body is found among other Dalaran mages and warders in southern Silverpine Forest, near Dalaran's presence. The staff is recovered from his body.",al={"where to get ataeric staff","ataeric location"},it="place",gp=true}},ang={["race:Undead"]="For the Forsaken, recovering the staff checks Dalaran's growing hold over Silverpine's magical reserves and secures their western borders.",["class:Mage"]="As a mage, you can see how Dalaran's archmagi use focused implements to reach ley nodes and stir them from dormancy."},kw={"archmage ataeric","ataeric's staff","dalaran","ley node","sepulcher","shadow priest allister","silverpine forest","the weaver"},rel={"quest:480","npc:shadow-priest-allister","subzone:sepulcher","zone:silverpine","subzone:dalaran","topic:mage","topic:priest"},src={"Ataeric's Staff","The Weaver (quest)"}}
E["item:bethor-s-scroll"] = {t="item",n="Bethor's Scroll",z="silverpine",s="Bethor Iceshard writes counter-incantations to help Apothecary Renferrel brew a protective draught against Thule Ravenclaw's dark sorcery. The scroll holds the key to facing the Scourge necromancy guarding Fenris Isle.",h="Bethor Iceshard writes counter-incantations to help Apothecary Renferrel brew a protective draught against...",sec={{t="Countering the Necromancer",b="Bethor Iceshard writes arcane formulas to guide the Royal Apothecary Society in brewing a restorative potion. Apothecary Renferrel receives the scroll at the Sepulcher. Its incantations counter the debilitating hexes Thule weaves around his fortress.",sp=1},{t="A Colleague's Betrayal",b="Bethor Iceshard recognizes Thule Ravenclaw's handiwork in tainted ichor recovered from Rot Hide gnolls. Thule was once a promising young mage of the Kirin Tor. When the Scourge rose to power, he betrayed his brethren and served the Lich King. Bethor learns Thule survived and directs Rot Hide attacks across Silverpine Forest from Fenris Isle. Knowing his former colleague's spellcraft well, Bethor writes the scroll.",sp=1,bt={"q437.6"}}},faq={{q="What is written on Bethor's Scroll?",a="Bethor Iceshard inscribes specialized arcane incantations on the scroll. He once studied alongside Thule Ravenclaw and knows the necromancer's preferred spells, so his formulas show how to brew an alchemical counter-potion.",al={"what does the scroll say","contents of bethors scroll","what is on the scroll"},it="identity"},{q="Who receives this scroll?",a="Apothecary Renferrel, stationed at the Sepulcher in Silverpine Forest, receives the scroll. He uses its magic to create a protective draught.",al={"who do i give the scroll to","bethors scroll turn in","who gets the scroll"},gp=true},{q="Why does Apothecary Renferrel need magical incantations for a potion?",a="Apothecary Renferrel practices alchemy rather than traditional sorcery, and admits he rarely weaves such overt forces into his concoctions. Ordinary anti-toxins cannot pierce the Scourge curses shielding Thule, so Bethor's arcane formulas are needed to make the brew effective.",al={"why does an apothecary need spells","magic potion renferrel"},it="purpose"},{q="Who was Thule Ravenclaw before turning to the Scourge?",a="Before the Third War, Thule Ravenclaw was a promising young human mage and an associate of Bethor Iceshard. When the Lich King marshaled his undead armies, Thule abandoned his fellow spellcasters and pledged loyalty to the Scourge.",al={"who is thule ravenclaw","thule backstory","thule and bethor"},it="history"},{q="Where does Bethor's Scroll come from, and who made it?",a="The scroll is penned by Bethor Iceshard, an undead mage serving the Forsaken from the Magic Quarter of the Undercity. Recognizing the magical signature on vile ichor recovered from Rot Hide gnolls, Bethor realized his former colleague Thule Ravenclaw had survived and turned to the Scourge. Drawing on his intimate knowledge of Thule's arcane techniques, Bethor transcribed counter-incantations onto this parchment to aid in defeating his rogue former peer.",al={"who wrote bethor's scroll","who made bethor's scroll","where did bethors scroll come from"},it="origin",add="31160c67"},{q="Why is Bethor's Scroll needed?",a="Apothecary Renferrel requires the magical incantations inscribed upon the scroll to brew a protective counter-agent. Thule Ravenclaw wields potent, debilitating hexes from his stronghold on Fenris Isle. By infusing Bethor's arcane formulae into an alchemical draught, the Royal Apothecary Society can produce a specialized potion that shields you against Thule's dark sorcery when you confront him.",al={"why want bethor's scroll","why is bethors scroll important","what is bethor's scroll used for"},it="why_wanted",add="64d2974c"}},ang={["class:Mage"]="As a mage, you can see how knowledge of a fellow spellcaster's signature magic can become a potent countermeasure. The scroll reflects the Kirin Tor's fractured past.",["race:Undead"]="As an undead, you can see Forsaken spellcasters and apothecaries bringing their talents together through this parchment. It joins Dalaran's old arcane training with the Sepulcher's alchemical craft."},kw={"apothecary renferrel","bethor iceshard","bethor's scroll","fenris isle","rot hide","silverpine","the sepulcher","thule ravenclaw"},rel={"quest:446","quest:442","subzone:fenris-isle","subzone:sepulcher","npc:apothecary-renferrel","topic:scourge","zone:silverpine"},src={"Bethor's Scroll","Thule Ravenclaw (quest)"}}
E["item:clarice-s-pendant"] = {t="item",n="Clarice's Pendant",z="silverpine",s="In the Pools of Vision in Thunder Bluff, Clarice Foster keeps a bitter reminder of the family she lost. Her pendant came from her former husband, Yuriv, whose devotion to the Light left Clarice and their children behind.",h="In the Pools of Vision in Thunder Bluff, Clarice Foster keeps a bitter reminder of the family she lost.",sec={{t="A Bitter Token",b="Clarice's Pendant recalls the life Clarice Foster lost before she became Forsaken. Before the Third War consumed Lordaeron, her husband Yuriv left her and their children to fight the undead. He believed devotion to the Holy Light came before all else. Yuriv died, and his family was left to fall to the very Scourge he had set out to fight. Clarice does not treasure the pendant he gave her. To her, it is an insult, a reminder that she and the children came second to his zeal and duty.",sp=0},{t="Resting upon Yuriv's Tomb",b="Clarice wants to sever her last ties to her former life and to Yuriv, the husband who neglected her. She sends an adventurer to lay the pendant on his grave at the Sepulcher. The neglected tomb lies beneath weeds and trash, and has been vandalized. When the pendant rests on the coffin's sculpted hands, its gemstone grows dull. The last warmth of Clarice's former life goes out.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Who owns Clarice's Pendant?",a="Clarice Foster, a Forsaken woman in the Pools of Vision in Thunder Bluff, owns the pendant. Her husband Yuriv gave it to her while she was alive, before he marched off to war.",al={"who does the pendant belong to","whose pendant is this","clarice foster"},it="identity"},{q="Who was Yuriv?",a="Yuriv was Clarice's husband while they were alive. He left Clarice and their children to fight the rising undead in the name of the Holy Light. He died and lies in a neglected grave at the Sepulcher.",al={"clarice husband","who is yuriv","yuriv tomb"},it="people"},{q="Why does Clarice want to get rid of the pendant?",a="Clarice wants to be rid of the pendant because she resents Yuriv for putting his crusade and devotion to the Light before her and their children. He died, and Clarice was left behind and raised in undeath, the very fate he sought to prevent.",al={"why throw away pendant","why does clarice hate yuriv","clarice pendant quest"},it="why_wanted"},{q="What happens when the pendant is placed on Yuriv's grave?",a="Laying the pendant on Yuriv's grave lets Clarice part with the keepsake and the painful attachment it carries.",al={"what happens at yuriv tomb","pendant on grave"},sp=1,it="power"}},ang={["race:Undead"]="As Forsaken, you may recognize the bitterness of loved ones who left to fight crusades that failed to protect anyone. Many of the Forsaken share that loss.",["class:Paladin"]="As a paladin, you may find Clarice's contempt for Yuriv's crusade hard to hear. His holy zeal left a broken home behind."},kw={"clarice foster","clarice's pendant","forsaken","sepulcher","silverpine forest","tomb","until death do us part","yuriv"},rel={"quest:264","subzone:sepulcher","zone:silverpine","topic:light"},src={"Clarice's Pendant","Until Death Do Us Part"}}
E["item:dalaran-pendant"] = {t="item",n="Dalaran Pendant",z="silverpine",s="In Ambermill, Dalaran Pendants focus the Kirin Tor's magic. The Forsaken seek them to hinder the wizards' work and trace the source of their power.",h="In Ambermill, Dalaran Pendants focus the Kirin Tor's magic.",sec={{t="Amulets of Ambermill",b="Kirin Tor sorcerers, conjurers, and protectors weave powerful spells in Ambermill, threatening Forsaken control of southern Silverpine Forest. Each carries an attuned Dalaran Pendant. At the Sepulcher, Shadow Priest Allister sends Forsaken operatives to recover the pendants, slowing the mages' efforts and uncovering who guides their magical weave.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What is the Dalaran Pendant?",a="A Dalaran Pendant is an arcane amulet carried by Kirin Tor conjurers, mages, and protectors in Ambermill. The Forsaken seek them to interrupt the wizards' workings and examine their magic.",al={"what is dalaran pendant","kirin tor necklace silverpine"},it="identity"},{q="Who carries these pendants?",a="Human mages, conjurers, and protectors of Dalaran carry the pendants in Ambermill, in Silverpine Forest.",al={"who drops dalaran pendant","where to get dalaran pendant"},it="people"},{q="Why does Shadow Priest Allister want them?",a="Shadow Priest Allister and his ally Dalar need the pendants to slow the wizards' spells and pinpoint the powerful mage directing Ambermill's magical weave.",al={"why allister wants pendants","ambermill investigations pendant"},it="why_wanted"},{q="Where is Ambermill located?",a="Ambermill lies in southern Silverpine Forest. From the Sepulcher, take the eastern fork off the main road heading south to reach the village.",al={"ambermill location","how to get to ambermill"},it="place",gp=true}},ang={["race:Undead"]="As an undead, taking these pendants from the Kirin Tor helps secure Silverpine Forest against human sorcerers trying to regain their foothold.",["class:Mage"]="As a mage, you can see how the Kirin Tor use these pendants to focus their magic and coordinate complex spells."},kw={"allister","ambermill","dalaran pendant","kirin tor","sepulcher","silverpine"},rel={"quest:479","subzone:ambermill","npc:shadow-priest-allister","subzone:sepulcher","zone:silverpine","subzone:dalaran","topic:mage","topic:priest"},src={"Dalaran Pendant","Ambermill Investigations"}}
E["item:darksoul-shackle"] = {t="item",n="Darksoul Shackle",z="silverpine",s="In Silverpine Forest, Moonrage Darksouls wear enchanted fetters forged under Archmage Arugal’s direction. Forsaken mages at the Sepulcher seek them to learn how the magic gripping the region can be undone.",h="In Silverpine Forest, Moonrage Darksouls wear enchanted fetters forged under Archmage Arugal’s direction.",sec={{t="A Crutch for Faltering Magic",b="Archmage Arugal’s magic could not fully command or sustain the worgen he unleashed upon Silverpine Forest. He bound enchanted implements such as Darksoul Shackles to the beasts to make up for that failing. The fetters channel outside sorcery into the Moonrage Darksouls, strengthening them and anchoring the curse that keeps them thrall to Shadowfang Keep.",sp=0},{t="Kirin Tor Scrutiny",b="At the Sepulcher, Forsaken mage Dalar Dawnweaver judges Arugal a dangerous incompetent. He believes Arugal’s meddling ruined the Kirin Tor’s defense against the Scourge. Forsaken researchers gather Darksoul Shackles and fetters torn from Moonrage Gluttons, then draw out the enchantments left in the metal. Studying them exposes flaws in Arugal’s spellcraft and gives the Forsaken arcane insight to shape a countermeasure against his lupine scourge.",sp=1}},faq={{q="What is a Darksoul Shackle?",a="Moonrage Darksoul worgen in Silverpine Forest wear enchanted metal fetters called Darksoul Shackles. Archmage Arugal crafted them to reinforce his spellcraft and bind the beasts to his control.",al={"what are darksoul shackles","darksoul shackle item lore","what is this shackle"},it="identity"},{q="Who wants Darksoul Shackles?",a="Dalar Dawnweaver, a Forsaken mage at the Sepulcher in Silverpine Forest, wants Darksoul Shackles. He studies their enchantments to find a solution to Arugal’s worgen outbreak.",al={"who needs darksoul shackles","who takes the shackles","dalar dawnweaver quest"},it="why_wanted"},{q="Where do these shackles come from?",a="Moonrage Darksouls, aggressive worgen haunting northern and eastern Silverpine Forest, bear these shackles.",al={"who drops darksoul shackles","darksoul shackle mob","where to get darksoul shackle"},it="origin"},{q="Why did Arugal put shackles on the worgen?",a="Dalar Dawnweaver says Arugal lacked the talent to command the beasts through sheer power alone. Arugal relied on enchanted objects like these shackles to channel and sustain the volatile magic holding the pack together.",al={"why do worgen wear shackles","arugal shackle purpose"}}},ang={["race:Undead"]="For the Forsaken, breaking Arugal’s hold on Silverpine Forest is essential to protecting their southern borders and proving Undercity’s arcane scholarship superior to Dalaran’s failures.",["class:Mage"]="As a mage, you can see how a desperate wizard used crude enchanted artifacts to shore up volatile summoning spells he could not properly control."},kw={"arugal","dalar dawnweaver","darksoul shackle","moonrage darksoul","sepulcher","silverpine forest","worgen"},rel={"npc:dalar-dawnweaver","quest:99","npc:arugal","item:glutton-shackle","subzone:sepulcher","zone:silverpine","subzone:dalaran"},src={"Darksoul Shackle","Arugal's Folly (2)"}}
E["item:deathstalker-report"] = {t="item",n="Deathstalker Report",z="silverpine",s="Deathstalker Rane Yorick sends word of Scourge resistance in Silverpine Forest to High Executor Hadrec.",h="Deathstalker Rane Yorick sends word of Scourge resistance in Silverpine Forest to High Executor Hadrec.",sec={{t="Frontline Intelligence",b="Deathstalkers Rane Yorick and Quinn Yorick faced a deadly ambush in northern Silverpine Forest. Pinned down by Scourge in the pine woods, they gathered their findings into a hurried dispatch. It describes stronger resistance than the Forsaken expected as they seek to claim the region. Quinn was grievously injured, so Rane entrusted the report to passing allies, who must carry it to High Executor Hadrec at the Sepulcher without delay.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What is the Deathstalker Report?",a="The report records Scourge activity, dangers, and the obstacles Forsaken scouts faced in Silverpine Forest.",al={"what is this report","deathstalker report lore","what is deathstalker report"},it="identity"},{q="Who wrote the report?",a="Deathstalker Rane Yorick wrote the report after tending to her injured brother, Deathstalker Quinn, following their encounter with the Scourge.",al={"who wrote deathstalker report","report author","who wrote it"},it="origin"},{q="Who is the report delivered to?",a="The report is addressed to High Executor Hadrec at the Sepulcher, where he commands Forsaken forces in Silverpine Forest.",al={"where does report go","who gets the report","hadrec report"}},{q="Why is the report so urgently needed?",a="Hadrec had underestimated the Scourge presence in Silverpine Forest. The report describes those hostile forces and gives him information to protect Forsaken efforts to occupy the region.",al={"why is it important","why does hadrec need it","what info is inside"},it="why_wanted"}},ang={["race:Undead"]="As an undead, you know the danger Deathstalkers face while gathering intelligence for Sylvanas along Lordaeron's frontiers.",["class:Rogue"]="As a rogue, you can see how Deathstalkers' covert reconnaissance helps keep the Forsaken military functioning."},kw={"deathstalker report","hadrec","quinn","rane yorick","scourge","sepulcher","silverpine forest"},rel={"quest:449","npc:high-executor-hadrec","subzone:sepulcher","zone:silverpine","quest:1886","topic:forsaken","topic:scourge"},src={"Deathstalker Report","The Deathstalkers' Report"}}
E["item:deliah-s-ring"] = {t="item",n="Deliah's Ring",z="silverpine",s="A grim trail begins with Deliah's Ring, found among the Rot Hide gnolls’ corpse piles in Silverpine Forest. Its inscription, “For Deliah,” points back to a plague victim taken from Tirisfal’s mass graves.",h="A grim trail begins with Deliah's Ring, found among the Rot Hide gnolls’ corpse piles in Silverpine Forest.",sec={{t="A Keepsake in the Mire",b="Among the gnoll mounds in Silverpine Forest, a ring rests on the pockmarked hand of a relatively fresh corpse. The band bears a simple inscription: “For Deliah.” The Rot Hide gnolls are doing more than scavenging battlefields. They raid the mass graves of Tirisfal Glades and carry human and Forsaken corpses south to Fenris Isle for their own purposes.",sp=0},{t="Ties to Brill",b="High Executor Hadrec sends the ring to Brill, where Magistrate Sevren keeps records of the recently deceased. Sevren confirms that Deliah lived in Brill and died of the plague. She was buried before body-snatchers exhumed her remains. The ring leads to the grief of those she left behind, and to the question of whether mortal devotion can endure undeath.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Where is Deliah's Ring found?",a="The ring is found among the Rot Hide gnoll mounds in northern Silverpine Forest, on the hand of an unwrapped plague victim among the scavenged dead.",al={"where to find deliahs ring","deliah ring location","how do you get deliahs ring"},it="place",gp=true},{q="Who was Deliah?",a="Deliah lived in Brill and died of the plague. She was buried in the local mass graves before Rot Hide gnolls stole her body and dragged it into Silverpine Forest.",al={"who is deliah","deliah lore","deliah of brill"},it="people"},{q="Why did the Rot Hide gnolls have her body?",a="The Rot Hide gnolls, aligned with the Scourge, pillage the communal graves in Tirisfal Glades. They stockpile corpses and carry them toward their stronghold on Fenris Isle.",al={"why gnolls stealing bodies","rot hide corpse stealing","what are gnolls doing with corpses"},it="motive"},{q="What is the inscription on the ring?",a="The ring bears the words “For Deliah” inside its band. It was a personal gift from a lover or husband before her death.",al={"ring engraving","what does the ring say","for deliah ring"}},{q="What is Deliah's Ring?",a="Deliah's Ring is an engraved piece of personal jewelry found on the hand of a deceased woman among the Rot Hide gnolls in Silverpine Forest. Inscribed simply with \"For Deliah,\" it is a rare, lingering token of affection and life from Lordaeron before the plague took hold.",al={"what is deliahs ring","deliah's ring lore","about deliahs ring"},it="identity",add="c1c1eafc"},{q="Why is Deliah's Ring wanted?",a="High Executor Hadrec values the ring as vital evidence that the Rot Hide gnolls are raiding mass plague graves in Tirisfal Glades for fresh corpses. Beyond that military clue, the ring serves to identify the dead woman through Brill's records, offering a chance to discover who once loved her and whether that mourner still exists.",al={"why keep deliahs ring","who wants deliahs ring","why turn in deliah's ring"},it="why_wanted",add="a38bd9ea"}},ang={["race:Undead"]="As an undead, you know that mortal attachments can fade alongside the flesh. A rare few still hold to the memory of those they loved in life."},kw={"brill","deliah","deliah's ring","engraved ring","fenris isle","hadrec","magistrate sevren","rot hide gnolls"},rel={"quest:439","quest:440","quest:441","quest:530","npc:high-executor-hadrec","npc:magistrate-sevren","subzone:fenris-isle","subzone:brill"},src={"Deliah's Ring","Rot Hide Clues","The Engraved Ring"}}
E["item:essence-of-nightlash"] = {t="item",n="Essence of Nightlash",z="silverpine",s="At the Dead Fields, Nightlash's defeat leaves a trace the Forsaken can carry away. High Executor Hadrec needs it as proof that the Scourge force behind the rot hide gnolls has been broken.",h="At the Dead Fields, Nightlash's defeat leaves a trace the Forsaken can carry away.",sec={{t="The Banshee of the Dead Fields",b="At the abandoned farmstead called the Dead Fields in northern Silverpine, packs of undead rot hide gnolls have dug in under Scourge command. Forsaken assaults have failed again and again, not because of the feral gnolls, but because their spectral commander, Nightlash, turns them back. Her wailing magic strengthens the gnoll lines and routs forces sent from the Sepulcher. When Nightlash is slain, her incorporeal form dissolves into dust, leaving a crystalline magical essence behind.",sp=0},{t="Proof of Scourge Defeat",b="Banshees leave no bodily corpse, so Nightlash's essence is the only physical proof that the spirit has been destroyed. High Executor Hadrec at the Sepulcher needs it to confirm that the Scourge foothold has fallen. With that proof, the Forsaken can secure their northern perimeter and suppress the rot hide threat.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What is the Essence of Nightlash?",a="The Essence of Nightlash is the crystalline dust left when the Scourge banshee Nightlash is defeated. Since spirits have no physical bodies, the residue proves her destruction.",al={"essence of nightlash","nightlash dust","what is nightlash essence"},it="identity"},{q="Who is Nightlash?",a="Nightlash is a Scourge banshee who commands and strengthens the rot hide gnolls at the Dead Fields in northern Silverpine.",al={"who is nightlash","nightlash lore","banshee nightlash"}},{q="Who wants this essence?",a="High Executor Hadrec at the Sepulcher wants the essence as proof that Nightlash, who routed his frontline assaults, has been defeated.",al={"who needs nightlash essence","who turn in essence","high executor hadrec"},it="why_wanted"},{q="Why are the gnolls working with a banshee?",a="The rot hide gnolls at the Dead Fields have succumbed to the undead plague and become Scourge thralls. Nightlash was sent to oversee them and lend magical support against Forsaken patrols.",al={"gnolls and scourge","rot hide scourge","why gnolls with banshee"}},{q="Where does the Essence of Nightlash come from?",a="The essence comes from the banshee Nightlash herself. When you confront and destroy her at the Dead Fields, her spectral form collapses and her essence turns into dust, leaving behind the remnant you collect.",al={"essence of nightlash origin","how to get essence of nightlash","where does essence of nightlash drop"},it="origin",add="13c624cf"}},ang={["race:Undead"]="As Forsaken, you know why soldiers see the destruction of banshees like Nightlash as vital work. Once victims of Scourge domination, the Forsaken fight the Lich King's agents to secure Lordaeron for their own people.",["class:Mage"]="As a mage, you may study the residue of destroyed banshees to learn how spectral undead tether necrotic magic to the physical world."},kw={"banshee","dead fields","dust","essence","hadrec","nightlash","rot hide","sepulcher"},rel={"quest:437","npc:high-executor-hadrec","subzone:dead-field","subzone:sepulcher","topic:scourge","topic:forsaken","topic:gnoll"},src={"Essence of Nightlash","The Dead Fields (quest)"}}
E["item:glutton-shackle"] = {t="item",n="Glutton Shackle",z="silverpine",s="In Silverpine Forest, Glutton Shackles lend strength to Arugal’s flawed sorcery. The mad archmage crafted these enchanted restraints for Moonrage Glutton worgen.",h="In Silverpine Forest, Glutton Shackles lend strength to Arugal’s flawed sorcery.",sec={{t="A Crutch for Weak Sorcery",b="Feral worgen infest Silverpine Forest, and the Forsaken’s trained mages see them as proof of poor arcane work. Dalar Dawnweaver, an accomplished arcanist stationed at the Sepulcher, holds Archmage Arugal in contempt and calls him an incompetent hack unworthy of the Kirin Tor. Dawnweaver found that Arugal relied on enchanted relics to shore up his fragile spells. The heavy Moonrage Gluttons that roam northern Silverpine wear Glutton Shackles, magical anchors that reinforce the curse binding the beasts.",sp=0},{t="Fuel for Forsaken Countermeasures",b="Arugal bound raw enchantments directly into heavy iron bands, leaving magical energy in the shackles even after their wearers are slain. Dawnweaver wants Forsaken agents to bring him the bands so he can study their construction and siphon their reserves. By examining the crude enchantments in the metal, the Forsaken hope to unravel the mysteries of the worgen curse and orchestrate the downfall of the beastmaster entrenched in Shadowfang Keep.",sp=1}},faq={{q="What is a Glutton Shackle?",a="A Glutton Shackle is an enchanted iron restraint worn by Moonrage Glutton worgen in Silverpine Forest. Archmage Arugal crafted these bands to reinforce their wearers with magic and shore up his flawed spells.",al={"what are glutton shackles","glutton shackle lore","worgen cuffs"},it="identity"},{q="Why does Dalar Dawnweaver want Glutton Shackles?",a="Dalar Dawnweaver wants the shackles to study Arugal’s crude enchantments and siphon their lingering magical energy. Understanding the items Arugal used to stabilize his beasts can help the Forsaken counter his magic.",al={"why collect shackles","dalar dawnweaver quest","shackles for sepulcher"},it="why_wanted"},{q="Who makes these shackles?",a="Archmage Arugal enchanted the shackles. He was a former wizard of Dalaran who summoned the worgen to fight the Scourge and eventually lost his mind, binding his creations to his will with magical trinkets.",al={"who made the shackles","arugal shackles","where did shackles come from"},it="origin"},{q="Where are the creatures wearing these shackles found?",a="Moonrage Gluttons roam the woods and abandoned farmsteads of central and northern Silverpine Forest, often in packs alongside other corrupted Moonrage worgen.",al={"where do gluttons spawn","moonrage glutton location","silverpine worgen shackles"},it="place",gp=true}},ang={["class:Mage"]="As a mage, you may recognize Dalar Dawnweaver’s biting critique of Arugal’s shoddy technique. Using physical enchanted crutches to stabilize simple transmutation and summoning spells marks a wizard as mediocre.",["race:Undead"]="As a Forsaken, you know that gathering these shackles is essential to neutralizing the worgen threat pressing directly on the borders of the Sepulcher."},kw={"arugal","dalar dawnweaver","glutton shackle","moonrage glutton","sepulcher","silverpine","worgen"},rel={"quest:99","item:darksoul-shackle","npc:dalar-dawnweaver","npc:arugal","zone:silverpine","subzone:sepulcher","subzone:dalaran","quest:421"},src={"Glutton Shackle","Arugal's Folly (2)"}}
E["item:head-of-grimson"] = {t="item",n="Head of Grimson",z="silverpine",s="At the Deep Elem Mine, Grimson the Pale's severed head proves the Forsaken have secured its riches. Dalar Dawnweaver receives the trophy at the Sepulcher, and the mine's minerals can supply Varimathras's military campaigns.",h="At the Deep Elem Mine, Grimson the Pale's severed head proves the Forsaken have secured its riches.",sec={{t="Securing the Deep Elem Mine",b="Forsaken scouts called Darkstalkers found a strategic threat brewing in the southeastern hills. Archmage Arugal's shadowy enchantments had corrupted workers in the Deep Elem Mine and driven its overseer, Grimson the Pale, mad. From the Sepulcher, Dalar Dawnweaver sent champions to kill Grimson and bring back his severed head. The trophy confirms the mine is free of rogue magic, leaving its underground wealth for Varimathras's forces.",sp=0},{t="A Trophy for the Dreadlord",b="The head of Grimson marks the end of his rule over the Deep Elem Mine. With the overseer gone, the Forsaken can work its rich mineral veins and turn the ore into weapons and armor. Those supplies sustain their advance across Silverpine Forest and the neighboring reaches of Lordaeron.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Who was Grimson the Pale?",a="Grimson the Pale was the overseer of the Deep Elem Mine in Silverpine Forest's southeastern hills. Arugal's spreading shadow magic corrupted him and the other miners, until the Forsaken intervened.",al={"who is grimson","grimson the pale lore","grimson background"},it="identity"},{q="Why does Dalar Dawnweaver want Grimson's head?",a="Dalar Dawnweaver wants Grimson's head as proof that the corrupted overseer has been eliminated. Varimathras wants the mine's mineral wealth for the Forsaken war effort, and Grimson's death breaks the corrupted miners' resistance in its tunnels.",al={"why dalar wants head","head of grimson purpose","why take head"},it="why_wanted"},{q="Where is the Deep Elem Mine located?",a="The Deep Elem Mine lies in the hills southeast of the Sepulcher in Silverpine Forest. The Forsaken contest its minerals with remnants corrupted by Arugal's magic.",al={"where is deep elem mine","grimson location","mine location silverpine"},it="place",gp=true},{q="What role does Varimathras play in this task?",a="Varimathras directs Forsaken expansion across Lordaeron from the Undercity. The mine's resources serve his strategic goals by providing raw materials for his war effort in Silverpine.",al={"varimathras role","why does varimathras want mine","varimathras silverpine"},it="motive"},{q="What is the Head of Grimson?",a="The Head of Grimson is the severed head of Grimson the Pale, taken as proof of his death. Once an ordinary overseer, Grimson was warped by the dark magical taint unleashed across Silverpine by Archmage Arugal. Claiming his head marks the end of his command over the Deep Elem Mine, securing undeniable evidence that the mine's corrupted leadership has fallen.",al={"head of grimson","grimson head","what is grimson's head"},it="item",add="f0354d96",nx={6}},{q="Where does the Head of Grimson come from?",a="This grim trophy comes directly from the Deep Elem Mine, located in the hills southeast of the Sepulcher. It is severed from the shoulders of Grimson the Pale, the mine's tainted foreman. Grimson succumbed to the wild magics leaking from Pyrewood and Shadowfang Keep, holding the mine until brought down on the orders of Dalar Dawnweaver.",al={"where to get head of grimson","who drops head of grimson","head of grimson origin"},it="origin",add="923cacb6"}},ang={["race:Undead"]="As Forsaken, claiming the mine fulfills Undercity high command's plans and proves your resolve to reclaim Lordaeron's vital infrastructure from maddened remnants.",["profession:Mining"]="Deep Elem Mine is one of Silverpine's prime mineral claims. Its overseer is gone, leaving raw ore available for Horde supply lines."},kw={"arugal","dalar dawnweaver","deep elem mine","grimson the pale","head of grimson","sepulcher","silverpine forest","varimathras"},rel={"quest:99","subzone:deep-elem-mine","npc:dalar-dawnweaver","subzone:sepulcher","npc:varimathras","npc:arugal","zone:silverpine","quest:421"},src={"Head of Grimson","Arugal's Folly (3)"}}
E["item:ivar-s-head"] = {t="item",n="Ivar's Head",z="silverpine",s="In northern Silverpine, Ivar's Head proves Ivar the Foul is dead. Rane Yorick seeks it so her wounded brother Quinn can recover safely.",h="In northern Silverpine, Ivar's Head proves Ivar the Foul is dead.",sec={{t="A Severed Threat",b="Rane and Quinn Yorick were scouting northern Silverpine Forest on High Executor Hadrec's orders when Ivar the Foul ambushed them at an abandoned farmstead. The Forsaken Deathstalkers drove the feral ghoul off, but Quinn was badly mauled. Rane stayed at the ruined farm to watch over him and could not safely leave to finish their mission. Ivar's severed head proves the ghoul will no longer threaten the estate, giving Quinn time to recover under Rane's care.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Whose head is this?",a="The head belonged to Ivar the Foul, a savage ghoul haunting the abandoned farmstead called the Ivar Patch in northern Silverpine Forest.",al={"who is ivar","ivar head identity","what is ivar"},it="identity"},{q="Why does Rane Yorick want Ivar's head?",a="Rane wants proof that Ivar is dead. The ghoul badly mauled her brother Quinn, who needs time to recover without fear of another ambush before they report back to High Executor Hadrec.",al={"why rane wants head","ivar head turn in","why kill ivar"},it="why_wanted"},{q="Where was Ivar the Foul found?",a="Ivar the Foul lurks inside the dilapidated barn at the Ivar Patch, waiting for the wounded Deathstalkers to let their guard down.",al={"ivar location","where is ivar"},it="place"},{q="Where does Ivar's Head come from?",a="This severed head is taken directly from the corpse of Ivar the Foul, a vicious ghoul lurking within the ruined barn at the Ivar Patch in Silverpine Forest. It is not an artifact or crafted item, but the physical trophy severed from an undead monster to guarantee he has truly been destroyed.",al={"origin of ivar's head","where did ivar's head come from","who made ivar's head"},it="origin",add="fce823f2"}},ang={["race:Undead"]="As a Forsaken scout, you know wild ghouls are mindless liabilities. They disrupt military reconnaissance and threaten Lordaeron's young security.",["faction:Horde"]="As a member of the Horde, you know removing Scourge remnants like Ivar protects Horde couriers traveling through northern Silverpine toward the Sepulcher."},kw={"deathstalkers","ivar patch","ivar the foul","ivar's head","quinn yorick","rane yorick","silverpine forest"},rel={"quest:425","subzone:ivar-patch","quest:430","quest:428","quest:429","npc:high-executor-hadrec","zone:silverpine","topic:forsaken"},src={"Ivar's Head","Ivar the Foul (quest)"}}
E["item:johaan-s-findings"] = {t="item",n="Johaan's Findings",z="silverpine",s="Apothecary Johaan sends his findings south from Brill to the Sepulcher. His research carries recent alchemical work from Tirisfal Glades to Apothecary Renferrel in Silverpine Forest.",h="Apothecary Johaan sends his findings south from Brill to the Sepulcher.",sec={{t="Apothecary Correspondence",b="Apothecary Johaan sends his research from Brill to Apothecary Renferrel at the Sepulcher. The Royal Apothecary Society works under Lady Sylvanas Windrunner's demand for a New Plague that can destroy both the living and the Scourge. Its researchers are scattered across Lordaeron's contested ruins, so they must share their findings between outposts. Renferrel directs the Society's efforts from Silverpine Forest, while Johaan records his local tests in Brill. His documents join the Society's wider work to refine its deadly brews.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What is Johaan's Findings?",a="Johaan's Findings are alchemical notes and research compiled by Apothecary Johaan in Brill. They record his recent tests and experiments in Tirisfal Glades.",al={"johaans findings","what are johaans findings","johaan research papers"},it="identity"},{q="Who is supposed to receive this item?",a="Apothecary Renferrel is meant to receive the findings. He is a senior member of the Royal Apothecary Society at the Sepulcher in northern Silverpine Forest.",al={"who gets johaans findings","where do i take johaans findings","renferrel delivery"},it="target"},{q="Why is this research being shared between apothecaries?",a="The Royal Apothecary Society shares knowledge among its scattered researchers to hasten their work. Sylvanas Windrunner demands swift progress on the New Plague, so researchers in Silverpine need to hear of discoveries made in Tirisfal.",al={"why share findings","purpose of johaans findings","royal apothecary society research"},it="why_wanted"},{q="Who wrote these documents?",a="Apothecary Johaan wrote the documents. He is a Royal Apothecary Society alchemist near the gallows in Brill, where he tests local specimens for Forsaken alchemical work.",al={"who is apothecary johaan","who wrote this","apothecary johaan"},it="origin"}},ang={["race:Undead"]="As an Undead, these findings speak to the Royal Apothecary Society's driving aim: delivering the New Plague promised to the Dark Lady.",["faction:Horde"]="As a member of the Horde, carrying research south takes you from familiar Tirisfal Glades into Silverpine Forest's darker conflicts."},kw={"apothecary johaan","apothecary renferrel","brill","johaan","johaan's findings","new plague","royal apothecary society","sepulcher"},rel={"quest:445","npc:apothecary-johaan","npc:apothecary-renferrel","subzone:sepulcher","subzone:brill","topic:royal-apothecary-society","zone:silverpine","zone:tirisfal"},src={"Johaan's Findings","Delivery to Silverpine Forest"}}
E["item:podrig-s-order"] = {t="item",n="Podrig's Order",z="silverpine",s="At the Sepulcher, Podrig's Order calls for fresh weapons from the Undercity.",h="At the Sepulcher, Podrig's Order calls for fresh weapons from the Undercity.",sec={{t="Arming the Sepulcher",b="Deathguard Podrig found the Sepulcher's stores mostly adequate after an inventory ordered by Executor Hadrec. Replacement weapons were running desperately low. His dispatch lists the blades and arms needed by the Deathguards holding the outpost in Silverpine Forest, a frontier threatened by the Scourge, feral beasts, and other dangers.",sp=0},{t="Dispatch via Bat Handler",b="The order goes to Gordon Wendham, a weapon dealer in the Undercity's Trade Quarter, because the damp crypts of Silverpine make forging weapons difficult. Couriers carry the document to bat master Karos Razok, using Forsaken flight paths to speed the shipment from the capital.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What is written in Podrig's Order?",a="Podrig's Order lists replacement weapons for the Deathguards at the Sepulcher, whose arms have been lost or broken in the field.",al={"what does the order say","contents of podrig's order","podrig order details"}},{q="Who wrote Podrig's Order?",a="Deathguard Podrig wrote the order at Executor Hadrec's direction, after an inventory of the Sepulcher's armory.",al={"who wrote it","author of podrig order"},it="origin"},{q="Who receives the order?",a="Gordon Wendham, a weapon dealer in the Undercity's Trade Quarter, is meant to receive the order.",al={"who gets the order","where does podrig order go","recipient of podrig order"},it="target"},{q="Why does the Sepulcher need new weapons?",a="The Deathguards need new weapons because skirmishes with the Scourge and other hostile forces in Silverpine often leave their equipment broken or lost.",al={"why need weapons","sepulcher weapon shortage"},it="motive"},{q="What is Podrig's Order?",a="Podrig's Order is an official Forsaken requisition document written to secure fresh armaments for the outpost at the Sepulcher. Penned by Podrig on behalf of Executor Hadrec, the scroll lists replacement weapons needed by the garrison's Deathguards to survive their ongoing clashes against the Scourge and other terrors lurking in Silverpine Forest.",al={"what is podrigs order","podrig order item","podrig requisition"},it="identity",add="92a3bbc0"},{q="Why does Gordon Wendham need Podrig's Order?",a="As a weapons vendor in the Trade Quarter of the Undercity, Gordon Wendham requires the formal requisition to verify and fulfill the garrison's supply request. Without this verified manifest, the Sepulcher cannot receive the necessary shipment of blades and gear to resupply its front-line Deathguards.",al={"why does gordon wendham want the order","why take podrigs order to undercity","why is podrig order needed"},it="why_wanted",add="6fc9fe58"}},ang={["race:Undead"]="As an Undead, you can see how the Undercity supplies outposts like the Sepulcher, keeping the Dark Lady's soldiers armed against the Scourge.",["profession:Blacksmithing"]="As a blacksmith, you know how vital forged weapons are on the front lines, where combat continually drains a garrison's supplies."},kw={"gordon wendham","hadrec","karos razok","podrig","podrig's order","sepulcher","silverpine"},rel={"quest:6321","quest:6323","subzone:sepulcher","npc:karos-razok","npc:gordon-wendham","zone:undercity","subzone:trade-quarter","zone:silverpine"},src={"Podrig's Order","Supplying the Sepulcher","Ride to the Undercity (Classic)"}}
E["item:pyrewood-shackle"] = {t="item",n="Pyrewood Shackle",z="silverpine",s="At Pyrewood Village, enchanted shackles bind its beleaguered inhabitants to Archmage Arugal's strange magic. The bands are tied to the dark fate that grips the townsfolk when night falls.",h="At Pyrewood Village, enchanted shackles bind its beleaguered inhabitants to Archmage Arugal's strange magic.",sec={{t="Arugal's Binding Magic",b="Pyrewood's residents live ordinary lives by day, appearing as humans, then become feral Moonrage worgen at sunset. Archmage Arugal bound the villagers in enchanted shackles as part of his experiments with worgen sorcery. At the Sepulcher, Forsaken arcane researcher Dalar Dawnweaver studies the bands to learn what their enchantments do. He gathers and examines the lingering energy on them, hoping to understand Arugal's magic and loosen the mad archmage's hold over the region.",sp=1,bt={"q421.5"}}},faq={{q="What are Pyrewood Shackles used for?",a="At the Sepulcher, Dalar Dawnweaver studies the shackles' enchantments. He hopes their magic will help him unravel Archmage Arugal's spells and dismantle the archmage's influence in Silverpine Forest.",al={"pyrewood shackles use","why gather shackles","dalar dawnweaver shackles"},it="why_wanted",gp=true},{q="Who carries these shackles?",a="The cursed residents of Pyrewood Village in southern Silverpine Forest carry the shackles. They wear them as humans by day and as Moonrage worgen by night.",al={"who drops pyrewood shackles","shackle source","where to find pyrewood shackles"},sp=1,it="origin",bt={"q421.5"}},{q="Why do the villagers transform at night?",a="Archmage Arugal's reckless experiments and enchantments made Pyrewood's residents change at night. The shackles hold an enchantment that lets them appear as ordinary humans in daylight, while darkness reveals their feral worgen forms.",al={"why pyrewood turns into worgen","pyrewood village curse","pyrewood werewolf secret"},sp=1,it="conflict",bt={"q421.5"}},{q="Who is Dalar Dawnweaver?",a="Dalar Dawnweaver is a Forsaken mage at the Sepulcher in Silverpine Forest. He studies arcane anomalies left by Archmage Arugal, seeking to break the archmage's curses.",al={"dalar dawnweaver","who is dalar"},it="people"},{q="What is a Pyrewood Shackle?",a="A Pyrewood Shackle is an enchanted fetter bound to the unfortunate residents of Pyrewood Village in southern Silverpine Forest. Imbued with the strange, reckless sorcery of the mad mage Archmage Arugal, these shackles play a direct role in binding the townsfolk to his will and masking the dark curse that afflicts them.",al={"pyrewood shackle","what are pyrewood shackles","pyrewood shackles"},it="identity",add="b92f5faa",nx={6}},{q="Where does a Pyrewood Shackle come from, and who made it?",a="These enchanted shackles were forged and placed upon the villagers by Archmage Arugal, the rogue Dalaran wizard who took residence in Shadowfang Keep. Arugal cast the shackles on Pyrewood's peasants as part of his twisted enchantments, keeping them under his sway while hiding their lupine transformation beneath a daylight illusion of ordinary human life.",al={"who made pyrewood shackles","pyrewood shackle origin","where do shackles come from"},it="origin",add="f6bcbb50"},{q="Why does anyone want Pyrewood Shackles?",a="Dalar Dawnweaver, an ambitious Forsaken mage conducting research at the Sepulcher, seeks these enchanted shackles to study Arugal's magic. By siphoning their residual energy, Dalar hopes to unravel the bizarre enchantment causing the villagers to appear human by day and turn into ravenous Moonrage worgen after dusk, seeking ultimately to dismantle Arugal's spells.",al={"why gather pyrewood shackles","who needs pyrewood shackles","pyrewood shackle purpose"},it="why_wanted",add="98d012f7"}},ang={["race:Undead"]="As Forsaken, you know Arugal's rampant sorcery threatens your borders. Collecting these enchanted bindings is vital to neutralizing Shadowfang Keep's influence.",["class:Mage"]="As a mage, you can recognize the reckless transmutation and binding magic woven into ordinary steel."},kw={"arugal","dawnweaver","moonrage","pyrewood","sepulcher","shackle","silverpine","worgen"},rel={"quest:99","subzone:pyrewood-village","npc:dalar-dawnweaver","npc:arugal","subzone:sepulcher","zone:silverpine","topic:worgen","topic:human"},src={"Pyrewood Shackle","Arugal's Folly (4)"}}
E["item:quinn-s-potion"] = {t="item",n="Quinn's Potion",z="silverpine",s="At the Sepulcher, Apothecary Renferrel brews Quinn's Potion to help an injured scout recover. Quinn Yorick needs it after a disastrous patrol in Silverpine Forest.",h="At the Sepulcher, Apothecary Renferrel brews Quinn's Potion to help an injured scout recover.",sec={{t="Renferrel's Cure",b="Apothecary Renferrel brews a remedy for Deathstalker Quinn Yorick. Word reached the Royal Apothecary Society at the Sepulcher after Quinn was badly hurt and left unable to move near the Ivar Patch. Renferrel made the draught to help him recover. Though minor field casualties rarely draw Renferrel from his darker research for Lady Sylvanas, he supplied the remedy so the scout could regain enough strength to travel.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What is Quinn's Potion used for?",a="Quinn's Potion helps Deathstalker Quinn Yorick recover from his injuries in northern Silverpine Forest. It restores enough of his strength for him to travel again.",al={"quinn potion purpose","what does quinn potion do","why brew quinn potion"},it="purpose"},{q="Who brewed this potion?",a="Apothecary Renferrel, an alchemist of the Royal Apothecary Society stationed in the Sepulcher's crypts, brewed the draught.",al={"who made quinn's potion","who brewed it","renferrel potion"},it="origin"},{q="Where does the potion need to be delivered?",a="Carry the potion north of the Sepulcher to Quinn Yorick, who is sheltering near the farmstead called the Ivar Patch.",al={"where do i take the potion","quinn location","quinn yorick spot"},it="place",gp=true},{q="Why was Quinn Yorick in need of a potion?",a="Quinn was scouting northern Silverpine with a Deathstalker patrol. At the Ivar Patch, the ghoul Ivar the Foul attacked the scouts and left Quinn badly hurt and stranded.",al={"why is quinn hurt","what happened to quinn yorick","quinn injured"},it="why_wanted"},{q="What is Quinn's Potion?",a="It is a restorative concoction brewed by Apothecary Renferrel at the Sepulcher. Formulated specifically to aid the injured scout Quinn Yorick, the draught provides the strength he needs to recover from his wounds and regain enough mobility to travel.",al={"quinns potion","what is this potion","what is quinn's draught"},it="identity",add="52098f03"}},ang={["race:Undead"]="As Forsaken, you know the Royal Apothecary Society rarely spends effort on simple field remedies unless they help preserve scouts who guard Silverpine's borders."},kw={"apothecary renferrel","deathstalker","ivar patch","quinn yorick","quinn's potion","sepulcher","silverpine"},rel={"quest:430","npc:quinn-yorick","npc:apothecary-renferrel","subzone:ivar-patch","subzone:sepulcher","quest:428","quest:429","quest:425"},src={"Quinn's Potion","Return to Quinn"}}
E["item:remedy-of-arugal"] = {t="item",n="Remedy of Arugal",z="silverpine",s="In Silverpine Forest, Dalar Dawnweaver seeks Arugal's spell to learn how his worgen magic works.",h="In Silverpine Forest, Dalar Dawnweaver seeks Arugal's spell to learn how his worgen magic works.",sec={{t="A Mage's Leftovers",b="Before taking Shadowfang Keep, Archmage Arugal sheltered at an abandoned wheat farm north of the river bridge in Silverpine Forest. He recorded his strange arts in spellbooks left among the farm tools and rotting floorboards. One scroll, the Remedy of Arugal, describes early methods and magical formulas from his experiments with the transmutations that cursed the local people.",sp=0},{t="Forsaken Scrutiny",b="Dalar Dawnweaver, a Forsaken spellcaster at the Sepulcher, thinks little of Arugal's standing and considers his intellect fragile and transparent. Still, Dawnweaver needs to understand the worgen curse's workings. Recovering the Remedy gives Forsaken agents the arcane knowledge Dawnweaver seeks to counter Arugal's spreading menace and secure Silverpine for Lady Sylvanas.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What is the Remedy of Arugal?",a="The Remedy of Arugal is a spell written by the renegade mage Arugal. It records the arcane methods he used in his first experiments with worgen magic in Silverpine Forest.",al={"what is remedy of arugal","arugal remedy item","remedy spell"},it="identity"},{q="Where was the Remedy left behind?",a="Arugal left the Remedy in dusty spellbooks on the upper floor of an abandoned wheat farm, just north of the river bridge in Silverpine Forest.",al={"where to find remedy of arugal","remedy of arugal location","farm spellbook"},it="place"},{q="Why does Dalar Dawnweaver want this spell?",a="Dalar Dawnweaver wants to study the magic Arugal used so the Forsaken can find ways to counter it and secure Silverpine.",al={"why does dalar want the remedy","dalar dawnweaver remedy"},it="why_wanted"},{q="Who guards the spellbooks at the farm?",a="Arugal's lupine thralls infest the farm. When someone disturbs the dusty spellbooks on the second floor, a Moonrage Darkrunner leaps out to defend its master's belongings.",al={"what attacks at the farm","spellbook ambush"},it="threat"},{q="Where does the Remedy of Arugal come from, and who made it?",a="The Remedy of Arugal is an incantation penned by Archmage Arugal himself during his early days in Silverpine Forest. After his schemes began to unfurl, he resided briefly at a wheat farm north of the main river bridge, leaving behind dusty spellbooks containing his research.",al={"who made remedy of arugal","remedy of arugal origin","where did remedy of arugal come from"},it="origin",add="157696b2"}},ang={["class:Mage"]="As a Forsaken mage, you may share Dalar Dawnweaver's disdain for Arugal's clumsy, reckless experiments, while seeing the danger in unchecked summoning magic.",["race:Undead"]="As Forsaken, you help secure this spell as an early, vital step against the feral worgen threatening Silverpine Forest's borders."},kw={"arugal","arugal's folly","dalar dawnweaver","dusty spellbooks","moonrage","remedy of arugal","sepulcher","silverpine forest"},rel={"quest:99","npc:dalar-dawnweaver","npc:arugal","subzone:sepulcher","zone:silverpine","topic:forsaken","quest:1886","quest:421"},src={"Remedy of Arugal","Arugal's Folly"}}
E["item:rot-hide-ichor"] = {t="item",n="Rot Hide Ichor",z="silverpine",s="On Fenris Isle, Rot Hide Ichor draws the Royal Apothecary Society’s attention. Apothecary Renferrel gathers it at the Sepulcher to learn what corrupted the gnolls and how to oppose them.",h="On Fenris Isle, Rot Hide Ichor draws the Royal Apothecary Society’s attention.",sec={{t="A Plague in the Blood",b="On Fenris Isle, Rot Hide gnolls are no ordinary beasts. Their bodies are decomposed and twisted by an unnatural blight, and a noxious ichor flows through their veins to sustain their animated flesh. The Royal Apothecary Society suspects the fluid may reveal how the pack was corrupted and who commands them from within the ruined keep.",sp=0},{t="Apothecary Research",b="At the Sepulcher, Apothecary Renferrel gathers vials of the ichor for study. The Forsaken hope to isolate the chemical and magical forces that fuel the gnolls, then find their weaknesses before sending troops across Lordamere Lake in a full assault.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Where does Rot Hide Ichor come from?",a="Rot Hide Ichor comes from the Rot Hide gnolls dwelling across Fenris Isle, in Lordamere Lake east of Silverpine Forest's mainland.",al={"where to get rot hide ichor","how to find rot hide ichor","gnoll ichor location"},it="origin"},{q="Why does Apothecary Renferrel want this ichor?",a="Apothecary Renferrel studies the fluid to learn what corrupted the gnolls and find physical or alchemical weaknesses the Forsaken can use before attacking the island.",al={"why does renferrel need ichor","renferrel quest reason","purpose of rot hide ichor"},it="why_wanted"},{q="Are the Rot Hide gnolls Scourge?",a="The Rot Hide gnolls are undead and warped by plague. The Forsaken are investigating who or what created them and commands them on Fenris Isle.",al={"are rot hides scourge","who controls rot hides","what are rot hide gnolls"},it="identity"},{q="Do all gnolls have this ichor?",a="No. The ichor belongs to the Rot Hide pack, whose flesh and blood are corrupted by foul necromantic blights.",al={"do all gnolls drop ichor","normal gnoll blood"}},{q="What is Rot Hide Ichor?",a="Rot Hide Ichor is a strange, unnatural fluid that courses through the bodies of the Rot Hide gnolls on Fenris Isle. It is not ordinary blood; the Royal Apothecary Society believes this tainted substance is directly responsible for the gnolls' twisted, undead-like nature and heightened resilience.",al={"what is rot hide ichor","rot hide fluid","what is the ichor"},it="identity",add="c332bd61"}},ang={["race:Undead"]="As Forsaken, you can see why studying the ichor matters: it offers military intelligence to secure Silverpine's eastern flank and advance the Royal Apothecary Society's mastery of plague science."},kw={"apothecary renferrel","fenris isle","lordamere lake","rot hide gnolls","rot hide ichor","sepulcher","silverpine forest"},rel={"quest:443","npc:apothecary-renferrel","subzone:fenris-isle","quest:442","subzone:sepulcher","subzone:decrepit-ferry","topic:gnoll","zone:silverpine"},src={"Rot Hide Ichor","Rot Hide Ichor (quest)"}}
E["item:rune-inscribed-pendant"] = {t="item",n="Rune-Inscribed Pendant",z="silverpine",s="In Silverpine Forest, a Rune-Inscribed Pendant arrives at the Sepulcher in a shipment bound for Ambermill. The Kirin Tor use pendants like it to channel arcane power.",h="In Silverpine Forest, a Rune-Inscribed Pendant arrives at the Sepulcher in a shipment bound for Ambermill.",sec={{t="Kirin Tor Relic",b="A Rune-Inscribed Pendant is found among cartographic supplies bound for the Dalaran enclave at Ambermill. Its fine arcane inscriptions reveal its purpose: to focus and strengthen a wizard’s spells. More channeling pendants are arriving in the region, and the Forsaken at the Sepulcher wonder what the Kirin Tor are preparing.",sp=0},{t="A Clue to Ambermill's Plans",b="At the Sepulcher, Shadow Priest Allister sees danger in the Dalaran wizards’ fortified position. He sends the pendant to Dalar Dawnweaver for closer study. Dawnweaver recognizes it as part of the mages’ operations. The Kirin Tor are gathering arcane focuses for powerful workings, defensive or offensive, behind Ambermill’s borders.",sp=1}},faq={{q="What is the Rune-Inscribed Pendant used for?",a="Kirin Tor wizards use the pendant to channel and direct powerful flows of magic. It focuses complex spellcraft.",al={"what does the pendant do","pendant purpose","rune pendant use"},it="purpose"},{q="Where did this pendant come from?",a="The pendant comes in a shipment bound for Ambermill in Silverpine Forest, where Kirin Tor remnants have fortified themselves.",al={"where do i find the pendant","pendant origin","where was it found"},it="origin"},{q="Who analyzes the pendant at the Sepulcher?",a="Shadow Priest Allister briefly inspects the pendant alongside captured maps. He sends it to Dalar Dawnweaver at the Sepulcher, who recognizes the Kirin Tor’s work.",al={"who studies the pendant","who wants the pendant","dalar pendant"},it="target"},{q="Why are the Forsaken concerned about it?",a="Large shipments of channeling pendants suggest the Kirin Tor at Ambermill are preparing a major magical undertaking. The Forsaken fear it could threaten their hold on Silverpine Forest.",al={"why do forsaken care","ambermill threat","why is the pendant dangerous"},it="why_wanted"},{q="What is the Rune-Inscribed Pendant?",a="It is an arcane artifact crafted and utilized by the powerful magi of Dalaran. Frequently used by the Kirin Tor to focus and channel tremendous magical energies, such pendants are conduits of potent arcane power rather than simple ornaments.",al={"what is rune inscribed pendant","rune pendant identity","what is this dalaran pendant"},it="identity",add="bf28d080"}},ang={["class:Mage"]="As a mage, you can recognize Kirin Tor craftsmanship in the runes. They steady volatile currents as powerful spells are channeled.",["race:Undead"]="As one of the Forsaken guarding Silverpine Forest, you know intercepted Dalaran focuses like this pendant offer clues to human resistance gathering behind Ambermill’s walls."},kw={"allister","ambermill","dalar dawnweaver","dalaran","kirin tor","pendant","rune-inscribed pendant","sepulcher"},rel={"quest:478","quest:481","npc:dalar-dawnweaver","npc:shadow-priest-allister","subzone:ambermill","subzone:sepulcher","subzone:dalaran","zone:silverpine"},src={"Rune-Inscribed Pendant","Maps and Runes","Dalar's Analysis"}}
E["item:thule-s-head"] = {t="item",n="Thule's Head",z="silverpine",s="At the Sepulcher, High Executor Hadrec demands proof that Thule Ravenclaw is dead. His severed head confirms the commander of the Scourge forces on Fenris Isle has fallen and helps the Forsaken hold Silverpine Forest.",h="At the Sepulcher, High Executor Hadrec demands proof that Thule Ravenclaw is dead.",sec={{t="Trophy of Fenris Isle",b="Fenris Isle is the Lich King's chief Scourge stronghold in Silverpine Forest. From Fenris Keep, the necromancer Thule Ravenclaw commands rot hides and undead minions that threaten Forsaken outposts, including the Sepulcher. High Executor Hadrec will accept no report of Thule's death without his severed head. When Thule dies, dark magic surges through the woods. His head gives Hadrec the proof he needs to declare Fenris Isle broken.",sp=1,bt={"q437.6"}}},faq={{q="Who wants Thule's Head?",a="High Executor Hadrec, who commands Forsaken forces from the Sepulcher in Silverpine Forest, demands Thule's Head as proof that the Scourge leader is dead.",al={"who needs thules head","who turned in thule head to","who takes thule head"},it="why_wanted"},{q="Who was Thule Ravenclaw?",a="Thule Ravenclaw is a powerful necromancer who commands the Scourge on Fenris Isle. From Fenris Keep, he directs attacks against the Forsaken and wields enchantments such as the Hex of the Ravenclaw.",al={"thule lore","who is thule","thule ravenclaw backstory"},it="identity"},{q="Why do the Forsaken demand his head specifically?",a="The Forsaken cannot leave Silverpine threatened by the Scourge. Necromancers are notorious for deceit and dark resurrections, so High Executor Hadrec demands physical proof that Thule is destroyed.",al={"why thule head","why do they want his head"},it="motive"},{q="What happens when Thule Ravenclaw is slain?",a="When Thule Ravenclaw is slain, necrotic energy bursts across the region. Forsaken scholars and apothecaries at the Sepulcher can sense the magical shockwave from afar.",al={"what happens after thule dies","energy released thule"},sp=1},{q="Where does Thule's Head come from?",a="This severed head is taken directly from the necromancer Thule Ravenclaw within the halls of Fenris Keep. Thule led the Scourge forces that seized Fenris Isle in northern Silverpine Forest, transforming the stronghold into a bastion of the undead until you cut him down.",al={"thules head origin","where do you get thules head","source of thules head"},it="origin",add="3fe7e40b"}},ang={["race:Undead"]="For the Forsaken, severing Thule's head is a military victory and personal vengeance against the Lich King's hold on Lordaeron.",["faction:Horde"]="Thule Ravenclaw's death secures Silverpine Forest's eastern borders and shields newly gained Horde territory from Scourge attacks."},kw={"fenris","hadrec","necromancer","ravenclaw","scourge","sepulcher","thule"},rel={"quest:442","quest:446","subzone:fenris-isle","npc:high-executor-hadrec","subzone:sepulcher","zone:silverpine","topic:forsaken","topic:scourge"},src={"Thule's Head","Assault on Fenris Isle"}}
E["npc:apothecary-renferrel"] = {t="npc",n="Apothecary Renferrel",z="silverpine",s="At the Sepulcher, Apothecary Renferrel advances Forsaken alchemy in Silverpine Forest. He studies the region’s corrupted wildlife and undead threats, and travelers help gather volatile reagents and investigate Scourge remnants.",h="At the Sepulcher, Apothecary Renferrel advances Forsaken alchemy in Silverpine Forest.",sec={{t="The Sepulcher's Alchemist",b="At the Sepulcher, Renferrel leads field research for the Royal Apothecary Society in Silverpine Forest. The society’s grand laboratories and high leadership are in Undercity, while he handles the work in the field. He secures native biological specimens, refines potent concoctions, and studies the grim ecology along Lordaeron’s western border.",sp=0},{t="Investigating Rot Hide and Scourge",b="Renferrel studies the Rot Hide gnolls and rogue undead in Silverpine. Blood and tissue samples help him examine the lingering touch of the plague and the necromantic forces binding local monsters. His investigations bring him into conflict with Thule Ravenclaw, a powerful Scourge necromancer near the ruins of Fenris Isle.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Who is Apothecary Renferrel?",a="Apothecary Renferrel works for the Royal Apothecary Society from the Sepulcher, the main Forsaken outpost in Silverpine Forest. He studies local beasts, plague variations, and enemy forces to brew concoctions and secure the region for Queen Sylvanas.",al={"renferrel","who is renferrel","apothecary renferrel lore"},it="identity"},{q="What does Renferrel research in Silverpine?",a="Renferrel develops new plagues and venomous mixtures, known broadly as a 'Recipe for Death'. He asks travelers to gather grizzly bear hearts, Rot Hide gnoll ichor, and other biological components so he can test and refine lethal concoctions.",al={"renferrel research","renferrel experiments","recipe for death"},it="wants"},{q="What is his connection to the Rot Hide gnolls?",a="Renferrel studies the corrupted ichor of the Rot Hide gnolls. His initial tests detect warlock and necromantic magic, so he sends a sample to Bethor Iceshard in Undercity for further study.",al={"rot hide ichor","rot hide origins","gnolls silverpine"},it="ties"},{q="Why does Renferrel target Thule Ravenclaw?",a="Renferrel investigates the magic behind the Rot Hide gnolls and seeks Bethor Iceshard’s help identifying its source. The investigation leads toward the threats on Fenris Isle.",al={"thule ravenclaw quest","who is thule ravenclaw","fenris keep necromancer"},sp=1,it="target",bt={"q437.6"}},{q="Where does Renferrel send adventurers after Silverpine?",a="After his initial research and the local threats are addressed, Renferrel sends seasoned travelers southeast to Hillsbrad Foothills. This connects the Sepulcher’s frontier efforts with broader Forsaken operations in Lordaeron.",al={"after sepulcher","hillsbrad delivery","journey to hillsbrad"},it="next_step"},{q="What is the Royal Apothecary Society?",a="The Royal Apothecary Society is the Forsaken’s scientific and alchemical branch, founded under Lady Sylvanas Windrunner. Based in Undercity, its researchers develop new poisons, seek to resist natural decay, and craft a plague capable of eradicating the Scourge.",al={"royal apothecary society","ras","forsaken apothecaries"}},{q="Whose side is Apothecary Renferrel on?",a="Apothecary Renferrel serves the Forsaken and Lady Sylvanas Windrunner as a sworn member of the Royal Apothecary Society. Operating under the broader banner of the Horde, his loyalty lies with Undercity's alchemical orders, dedicating his efforts to advancing the Forsaken's survival and dominance against common enemies like the Scourge and the living.",al={"renferrel faction","who does renferrel serve","is apothecary renferrel horde"},it="side",add="703d1213"},{q="Why is Apothecary Renferrel here in Silverpine Forest?",a="Stationed at the Sepulcher, Renferrel carries out vital alchemical field research for the Royal Apothecary Society. Silverpine Forest provides him access to feral beasts, dangerous Scourge activity, and tainted local threats like the Rot Hide gnolls—all vital subjects for harvesting potent ingredients and brewing new toxins.",al={"why is renferrel in the sepulcher","renferrel location why","why is apothecary renferrel here"},it="why_here",add="dbc0ae2b"}},ang={["race:Undead"]="As an undead, you know the Forsaken’s ruthless drive to survive. Renferrel turns Lordaeron’s native flora and fauna into weapons to secure a future for the freed undead.",["faction:Horde"]="As a member of the Horde, you may find Renferrel’s biological experiments gruesome. His intelligence gathering against the Scourge helps protect Horde territories from northern incursions."},kw={"apothecary","recipe for death","renferrel","rot hide","royal apothecary society","sepulcher","silverpine","thule ravenclaw"},rel={"subzone:sepulcher","zone:silverpine","topic:royal-apothecary-society","topic:forsaken","quest:446","quest:447","quest:443","quest:493"},src={"Apothecary Renferrel"}}
E["npc:clarice-foster"] = {t="npc",n="Clarice Foster",z="silverpine",s="In the Pools of Vision, Clarice Foster lives among tauren seers and mystics. Far from Lordaeron, the Forsaken woman spends her days in contemplation beneath the bluffs of Mulgore.",h="In the Pools of Vision, Clarice Foster lives among tauren seers and mystics.",sec={{t="A Forsaken in the Pools of Vision",b="Most Forsaken remain in Lordaeron, rebuilding their kingdom beneath the Undercity. Clarice Foster has traveled to the heart of tauren lands in Kalimdor. She lives in the cavernous Pools of Vision beneath the mesa of Thunder Bluff, among Forsaken apothecaries and tauren shamans who study the spiritual and elemental mysteries of the earth.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who is Clarice Foster?",a="Clarice Foster is a Forsaken woman in the Pools of Vision beneath Thunder Bluff. She is an envoy among the tauren of Mulgore, and one of the few undead visitors dwelling with them.",al={"who is clarice","clarice foster npc","clarice foster backstory"},it="identity"},{q="Where can I find Clarice Foster?",a="You can find Clarice Foster in the Pools of Vision, a cave complex beneath Spirit Rise in Thunder Bluff.",al={"clarice foster location","where is clarice foster","find clarice foster"},it="place",gp=true},{q="What quests does she offer?",a="Clarice Foster offers Until Death Do Us Part. Bitter that her late husband left her to fight the undead and died, she sends travelers to lay his pendant on his tomb at the Sepulcher in Silverpine Forest.",al={"clarice foster quests","until death do us part quest"},it="purpose",gp=true},{q="Whose side is Clarice Foster on?",a="Clarice Foster is aligned with the Forsaken and the broader Horde. Though her duties keep her far from Lordaeron within the subterranean Pools of Vision in Thunder Bluff, she remains loyal to Queen Sylvanas and the Forsaken cause.",al={"clarice foster faction","clarice foster allegiance","who does clarice foster serve"},it="side",add="4e89059e"}},ang={["race:Undead"]="As Forsaken, Clarice Foster reflects your people's ties to their tauren allies in Kalimdor, far from the blight-stained soil of Tirisfal and Silverpine.",["race:Tauren"]="As a tauren, you see Clarice Foster welcomed into the sacred Pools of Vision beneath Spirit Rise, a sign of your people's willingness to host unconventional newcomers to the Horde."},kw={"clarice foster","forsaken","pools of vision","spirit rise","thunder bluff","until death do us part"},rel={"subzone:pools-of-vision","zone:thunderbluff","quest:264","topic:forsaken","zone:silverpine"},src={"Clarice Foster"}}
E["npc:dalar-dawnweaver"] = {t="npc",n="Dalar Dawnweaver",z="silverpine",s="At the Sepulcher, Dalar Dawnweaver turns his arcane learning toward the Forsaken’s enemies. Once an archmage of Dalaran, he died when the Scourge destroyed the city and later broke free of the Lich King’s control. Now he studies Dalaran’s lingering presence and seeks to end the madness of Archmage Arugal.",h="At the Sepulcher, Dalar Dawnweaver turns his arcane learning toward the Forsaken’s enemies.",sec={{t="A Fallen Archmage",b="Dalar Dawnweaver once held high rank among the Kirin Tor, walking the Violet Citadel’s halls when Dalaran stood at the height of arcane mastery. His mortal life ended when the Scourge sacked the city to prepare for Archimonde’s summoning. Raised as a mindless thrall of the Lich King, Dalar broke free alongside Lady Sylvanas Windrunner when the Scourge’s grip faltered. Now at the Sepulcher, he keeps an archmage’s keen intellect and devotes it to protecting the Forsaken realm.",sp=0},{t="Eyes on Ambermill and Shadowfang",b="Silverpine Forest faces many dangers, and Dalar directs the Sepulcher’s arcane strategy. To the south, Dalaran wizards occupy Ambermill, where they pursue matters he aims to uncover and disrupt. Shadowfang Keep lies closer, its feral worgen prowling the woods. Dalar knows his former colleague, Archmage Arugal, well. He carefully directs efforts to stop Arugal’s beastly creations before they overrun the region.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who is Dalar Dawnweaver?",a="Dalar Dawnweaver is a Forsaken mage at the Sepulcher in Silverpine Forest. He was once an archmage of the Kirin Tor in Dalaran. After dying during the Third War and being raised by the Scourge, he broke free of the Lich King’s control and joined the Dark Lady.",al={"who is dalar","dalar dawnweaver lore","dalar background"},it="identity"},{q="What happened to him during the Third War?",a="Dalar was in Dalaran when Arthas Menethil and the Scourge invaded to recover the Book of Medivh. He died in the assault as Kel’Thuzad summoned Archimonde into Azeroth, then was raised as a servant of the Scourge until Sylvanas freed him.",al={"how did dalar die","dalar death","dalar third war"},it="history"},{q="Why is Dalar stationed at the Sepulcher?",a="Dalar is the Forsaken’s local arcane authority in Silverpine Forest. He knows the Kirin Tor forces occupying Ambermill and his former peer, Archmage Arugal, making him well placed to counter both threats.",al={"why is dalar in sepulcher","dalar role in silverpine"},it="why_here"},{q="What is Dalar's connection to Archmage Arugal?",a="Dalar and Archmage Arugal were both Kirin Tor mages in Dalaran before its fall. Dalar understands the tragic course and deadly danger of Arugal’s summoning experiments in Shadowfang Keep. He sends adventurers to gather relics of Arugal’s folly and ultimately demands the mad mage’s death.",al={"dalar and arugal","did dalar know arugal"},it="ties"},{q="What does Dalar want with Dalaran's remnants?",a="Dalar watches his former homeland and the surviving Kirin Tor forces at Ambermill. He directs agents to intercept their messages and study their intentions, so they cannot threaten the Forsaken in Silverpine.",al={"dalar and dalaran","dalar ambermill"},it="wants"},{q="Is Dalar aligned with the Kirin Tor?",a="No. Dalar was once an archmage among the Kirin Tor, but his loyalty now belongs to the Forsaken and the Horde. He actively opposes the surviving Kirin Tor forces in Silverpine Forest.",al={"is dalar kirin tor","is dalar loyal to dalaran"},it="side"}},ang={["class:Mage"]="As a Forsaken mage, you can see in Dalar a dark reflection of Dalaran’s former grandeur. His Kirin Tor training now serves the Dark Lady.",["race:Undead"]="As an undead, you can see Dalar reclaiming his agency as a Forsaken. He turns the knowledge he gained in life against Dalaran’s remnants and rogue wizards who threaten their sovereignty.",["faction:Horde"]="At the Sepulcher, Dalar helps secure the Horde’s western frontier. He coordinates strikes against the worgen of Shadowfang Keep and hostile Kirin Tor enclaves."},kw={"archmage","arugal","dalar","dalaran","dawnweaver","forsaken","kirin tor","sepulcher","silverpine"},rel={"subzone:sepulcher","zone:silverpine","npc:arugal","quest:99","quest:1014","quest:481","quest:482","topic:forsaken"},src={"Dalar Dawnweaver"}}
E["npc:deathstalker-faerleia"] = {t="npc",n="Deathstalker Faerleia",z="silverpine",s="Deep inside Pyrewood Village, Deathstalker Faerleia works against its leaders. From the town hall, she directs covert strikes against the Pyrewood Council, the puppets Arugal uses to rule the village.",h="Deep inside Pyrewood Village, Deathstalker Faerleia works against its leaders.",sec={{t="Behind Enemy Lines",b="Deathstalker Faerleia works from the upper levels of Pyrewood Village's town hall. As an agent of the Deathstalkers, the Undercity's covert intelligence and assassin branch, she has infiltrated the isolated human enclave in southern Silverpine Forest. The village holds dark secrets, including a curse that transforms its people beneath the night sky. From inside the settlement, Faerleia coordinates operations to disrupt it and calls on Horde operatives to eliminate influential members of the Pyrewood Council.",sp=1,bt={"q421.5"}}},faq={{q="Who is Deathstalker Faerleia?",a="Faerleia serves in the Deathstalkers, Queen Sylvanas Windrunner's stealth and intelligence division. She has slipped into Pyrewood Village to wage a covert war against its leadership.",al={"faerleia","who is faerleia","deathstalker faerleia"},it="identity"},{q="Where can Deathstalker Faerleia be found?",a="Faerleia can be found inside Pyrewood Village's town hall, in southern Silverpine Forest just north of the Greymane Wall.",al={"where is faerleia","faerleia location","find faerleia"},it="place",gp=true},{q="What mission does she give?",a="Faerleia directs adventurers in the Pyrewood Ambush, an operation to assassinate the councilmen who govern Pyrewood Village and weaken the enclave's resistance to the Forsaken.",al={"faerleia quest","pyrewood ambush quest"},it="purpose"},{q="Why are the Deathstalkers targeting Pyrewood Village?",a="Arugal uses the Pyrewood Council as puppets to keep the cursed villagers under his control. Faerleia believes that if the council dies, the sons of Arugal will turn against their master, helping the Forsaken take the town and drive Arugal from Shadowfang Keep.",al={"why attack pyrewood","deathstalkers in pyrewood"},it="motive"},{q="Whose side is Deathstalker Faerleia on?",a="Faerleia is an operative of the Deathstalkers, the intelligence and assassin order serving Lady Sylvanas Windrunner and the Forsaken. Her loyalty lies with the Undercity and the Horde, advancing their hold over Silverpine Forest against hostile enclaves.",al={"faerleia faction","who does faerleia serve","faerleia loyalty"},it="side",add="72e51f96"},{q="What does Deathstalker Faerleia want?",a="She seeks the destruction of Pyrewood Village's leadership. Deep within hostile territory, Faerleia coordinates an ambush against the Pyrewood Council to break the village's organized resistance and eliminate the local threat.",al={"what does faerleia want","faerleia goal","faerleia objective"},it="wants",add="7830562d"},{q="Why is Deathstalker Faerleia in Pyrewood Village?",a="Faerleia has slipped past Pyrewood's defenders into the town hall itself. Positioned directly in the seat of power, she lies in wait to stage a decisive strike against the village leaders from within their own walls.",al={"why is faerleia here","why is faerleia in pyrewood","faerleia silverpine town hall"},it="why_here",add="fcf28179"},{q="Who is Deathstalker Faerleia tied to?",a="Faerleia answers to the Deathstalkers of the Forsaken, answering up the chain of command to Queen Sylvanas Windrunner. In the field, she depends on trusted Horde scouts and adventurers bold enough to infiltrate the cursed settlement to carry out her ambush.",al={"faerleia ties","faerleia connections","who is faerleia working with"},it="ties",add="e3ddcd8c"}},ang={["race:Undead"]="As an Undead, you can see how Faerleia uses infiltration and cold calculation to dismantle enemies of the Dark Lady without committing an entire army.",["class:Rogue"]="As a Rogue serving the Forsaken, you can look to Faerleia's field craft: she slips into the enemy's seat of power unnoticed and orchestrates ambushes."},kw={"ambush","council","deathstalker","faerleia","forsaken","pyrewood","silverpine"},rel={"subzone:pyrewood-village","quest:452","zone:silverpine","topic:forsaken"},src={"Deathstalker Faerleia"}}
E["npc:deathstalker-rane-yorick"] = {t="npc",n="Rane Yorick",z="silverpine",s="At a farmhouse in Silverpine, Deathstalker Rane Yorick and her brother Quinn are cut off from the Sepulcher. Sent to scout the northern farms, they must get word to High Executor Hadrec.",h="At a farmhouse in Silverpine, Deathstalker Rane Yorick and her brother Quinn are cut off from the Sepulcher.",sec={{t="Eyes in the Woods",b="Across Lordaeron, the Deathstalkers are Lady Sylvanas Windrunner's eyes, ears, and blades. Agents like Rane Yorick watch the wilds from hidden posts for threats to Forsaken rule. Rane and her brother Quinn were sent to scout northern Silverpine Forest. Feral dangers closed around them, turning their covert work into a fight to survive.",sp=0},{t="Trapped at Ivar Patch",b="At the Ivar Patch, Rane Yorick shelters in a ruined farmhouse. The ghoul Ivar the Foul has badly mauled her brother Quinn, and worgs prowl the fields between them and the Sepulcher. Rane holds to her assignment. She calls on passing Horde travelers to gather worg hearts for a healing potion, slay Ivar, and carry her report to command.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Who is Deathstalker Rane Yorick?",a="Rane Yorick serves with the Deathstalkers, the Forsaken order of rogues who gather intelligence and kill in secret. She is stationed at a ruined farmhouse in the Ivar Patch of Silverpine Forest.",al={"who is rane yorick","rane yorick lore","who is deathstalker yorick"},it="identity"},{q="What are the Deathstalkers?",a="The Deathstalkers are the Forsaken's covert rogue guild, answering to Lady Sylvanas Windrunner. They scout, spy, and carry out targeted killings across Lordaeron.",al={"what are deathstalkers","deathstalker faction","who are the deathstalkers"}},{q="Why is she trapped in a farmhouse?",a="Rane and her brother Quinn were sent to scout the farms of northern Silverpine Forest. At the Ivar Patch, the ghoul Ivar the Foul attacked them and badly mauled Quinn, so they took shelter in a farmhouse while he heals.",al={"why is rane trapped","ivar patch farmhouse","why is she hiding"},it="why_here"},{q="Who is her brother?",a="Quinn Yorick is Rane's brother and a fellow Deathstalker on the same scouting mission. Ivar the Foul badly mauled him at the Ivar Patch.",al={"rane yorick brother","who is erland","deathstalker erland"},it="ties"},{q="What threats are they tracking in Silverpine?",a="Rane and Quinn were sent to scout northern Silverpine's farms for threats to Forsaken rule. They found more Scourge than expected, along with prowling worgs and the ghoul Ivar the Foul.",al={"what are they scouting","what is rane investigating"},it="threat"},{q="Where does she report her findings?",a="Rane reports her findings to High Executor Hadrec at the Sepulcher. Hadrec oversees the Forsaken occupation of Silverpine Forest.",al={"where do reports go","who is rane's superior"}},{q="Whose side is Deathstalker Rane Yorick on?",a="Deathstalker Rane Yorick is fully loyal to the Forsaken and the Dark Lady. As a member of the Deathstalkers, the Forsaken's covert espionage and assassination order, she carries out dangerous reconnaissance missions across Lordaeron to protect their fledgling realm from lurking enemies.",al={"rane yorick faction","who does rane yorick serve","is rane yorick forsaken"},it="side",add="bafbf2b7"},{q="What does Deathstalker Rane Yorick want?",a="Rane wants to complete her scouting mission and ensure her findings make it back to Forsaken command. With herself and her companion cornered and beleaguered in Silverpine, she desperately needs reliable allies to assist them, neutralize nearby perils, and convey her intelligence safely.",al={"what does rane yorick need","rane yorick motive","why does rane yorick want help"},it="wants",add="a4a724f9"}},ang={["class:Rogue"]="As a Forsaken rogue, you see the dangerous fieldwork of the Deathstalkers in Rane Yorick's efforts to gather intelligence under enemy pressure.",["race:Undead"]="As a Forsaken champion, you meet Rane as a scout guarding Silverpine Forest's frontier from hostile hands.",["faction:Horde"]="As a member of the Horde, you benefit from Rane's intelligence work, which helps keep Horde supply routes through Silverpine clear of worgen and local ambushes."},kw={"deathstalker","erland","forsaken","ivar patch","rane","rogue","scout","silverpine","yorick"},rel={"quest:428","quest:435","quest:449","subzone:ivar-patch","quest:425","topic:worgen","zone:silverpine","topic:forsaken"},src={"Deathstalker Rane Yorick"}}
E["npc:elder-obsidian"] = {t="npc",n="Elder Obsidian",z="silverpine",s="At the Sepulcher in Silverpine Forest, Elder Obsidian appears for the Lunar Festival. The ancestral earthen spirit greets travelers among the graves claimed by the Forsaken, offering ancient wisdom and blessings.",h="At the Sepulcher in Silverpine Forest, Elder Obsidian appears for the Lunar Festival.",sec={{t="A Spirit at the Sepulcher",b="Elder Obsidian greets travelers at the Sepulcher during the Lunar Festival. His earthen spirit brings the ancient heritage of Azeroth to Silverpine Forest. The surrounding crypts are held by the Forsaken, and feral worgen menace the forest. Yet Obsidian welcomes wayfarers of every allegiance in peace, offering a Coin of Ancestry and ancient blessings to those who seek his wisdom.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who is Elder Obsidian?",a="Elder Obsidian is an ancient earthen spirit who appears in Silverpine Forest during the Lunar Festival. He greets travelers who honor Azeroth's ancestral heritage.",al={"elder obsidian lore","who is obsidian","sepulcher elder"},it="identity"},{q="Where can Elder Obsidian be found?",a="Elder Obsidian can be found in the graveyard at the Sepulcher, a Forsaken hamlet along the road in central Silverpine Forest.",al={"elder obsidian location","where is obsidian","find elder obsidian"},it="place",gp=true},{q="Why does an earthen elder appear in Silverpine Forest?",a="During the Lunar Festival, ancient elder spirits appear across Azeroth to share ancestral wisdom. Elder Obsidian meets travelers among the old graves, beyond local territorial conflicts.",al={"why is obsidian in silverpine","earthen in silverpine"},it="why_here"},{q="Can Alliance adventurers speak with Elder Obsidian?",a="Yes. Festival elders welcome travelers of every faction. The Sepulcher is held by the Forsaken, so Alliance adventurers must pass the hostile guards nearby to reach Elder Obsidian.",al={"can alliance visit elder obsidian","elder obsidian alliance friendly"},it="side",gp=true},{q="Whose side is Elder Obsidian on?",a="Elder Obsidian stands apart from the mortal conflicts between the Alliance and Horde. As an ancient earthen spirit returning for the Lunar Festival, he offers his wisdom and ancestral blessing to any adventurer who comes to honor the elders, regardless of allegiance, even though he manifests near the Forsaken settlement of the Sepulcher.",al={"is elder obsidian alliance or horde","elder obsidian faction","elder obsidian side"},it="side",add="cd669d85"},{q="What does Elder Obsidian want?",a="Elder Obsidian wishes to be remembered and honored by the mortals of Azeroth. During the celebration of the Lunar Festival, he welcomes travelers who seek out his ancient presence, bestowing his blessing and a token of ancestral luck upon those who pay their respects to the past.",al={"what does elder obsidian need","elder obsidian goal","why visit elder obsidian"},it="wants",add="5cd08f2c"}},ang={["race:Dwarf"]="As a dwarf, you can glimpse the primordial past of your stone-hewn ancestors by speaking with an earthen spirit like Elder Obsidian.",["faction:Alliance"]="As an Alliance pilgrim, you must tread carefully to reach Elder Obsidian at the Sepulcher, a Forsaken settlement."},kw={"ancestor","coin of ancestry","earthen","elder obsidian","lunar festival","sepulcher","silverpine"},rel={"subzone:sepulcher","zone:silverpine"},src={"Elder Obsidian"}}
E["npc:high-executor-hadrec"] = {t="npc",n="High Executor Hadrec",z="silverpine",s="At the Sepulcher, High Executor Hadrec directs the Forsaken garrison in Silverpine Forest. From this crypt, he oversees defense against threats such as the Rot Hide gnolls and investigates scouts who have gone missing across the zone.",h="At the Sepulcher, High Executor Hadrec directs the Forsaken garrison in Silverpine Forest.",sec={{t="Commander at the Sepulcher",b="High Executor Hadrec directs Forsaken military operations from the Sepulcher in Silverpine Forest. Tirisfal Glades is secure under the Dark Lady’s forces, but Silverpine faces hostile Dalaran mages, feral worgen, and encroaching gnolls. Hadrec must strengthen Forsaken control and suppress threats to Undercity authority south of the capital.",sp=0},{t="The Rot Hide Scourge",b="The Rot Hide gnolls and Fenris Isle occupy much of Hadrec’s attention. Tainted by undeath, the beasts have overrun the Dead Fields and Lake Lordamere’s shores, threatening Forsaken patrols. Hadrec sends agents to search the ruined ferries and farmsteads for clues, learn what empowers the gnolls, and prepare a strike against their island stronghold.",sp=0},{t="Eye on Shadowfang",b="Hadrec also watches reports from the Deathstalkers, the Forsaken’s secretive intelligence arm. When covert operatives vanish near Shadowfang Keep, Hadrec sends agents to learn their fate and keep the Dark Lady informed about the archmage Arugal and his cursed worgen.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Who is High Executor Hadrec?",a="Hadrec is a Forsaken military officer with the rank of High Executor. He commands the garrison at the Sepulcher and directs Forsaken operations across Silverpine Forest.",al={"hadrec lore","who is hadrec","sepulcher commander"},it="identity"},{q="Where can High Executor Hadrec be found?",a="You can find Hadrec inside the Sepulcher, the Forsaken settlement in central Silverpine Forest along the main north-south road.",al={"hadrec location","where is hadrec","find hadrec"},it="place",gp=true},{q="What threats does Hadrec direct players against?",a="Hadrec directs soldiers and adventurers against Rot Hide gnolls in the Dead Fields and on Fenris Isle. He also oversees efforts to find missing Deathstalker spies and learn what is happening inside Shadowfang Keep.",al={"hadrec quests","what does hadrec do","silverpine missions"},it="threat"},{q="What does a High Executor do in Forsaken military structure?",a="A High Executor is a senior Forsaken field commander, responsible for strategic oversight of a regional outpost or front under Lady Sylvanas Windrunner.",al={"forsaken high executor","high executor rank","hadrec rank"},it="power"},{q="Why is Hadrec interested in Fenris Isle?",a="Hadrec is interested in Fenris Isle because it has become the Rot Hide gnolls’ main den. He coordinates reconnaissance and a planned assault to break their leadership and secure Lake Lordamere and nearby waterways for Forsaken supply lines.",al={"fenris isle hadrec","why assault fenris isle","rot hide fenris"},it="target"},{q="What is Hadrec's connection to Shadowfang Keep?",a="Hadrec works with the Deathstalkers, the Forsaken espionage order. When scouts sent toward Shadowfang Keep fail to report back, he sends trusted agents to investigate and learn what happened to them.",al={"shadowfang keep hadrec","hadrec arugal","deathstalkers in shadowfang"},it="conflict"},{q="Whose side is High Executor Hadrec on?",a="High Executor Hadrec serves the Forsaken and the Dark Lady, Queen Sylvanas Windrunner, as part of the Horde. From his post at the Sepulcher, he commands Forsaken military operations across Silverpine Forest, acting directly in the interests of the Undercity.",al={"hadrec faction","who does hadrec serve","hadrec horde"},it="side",add="82ec3fb8"},{q="What does High Executor Hadrec want?",a="Hadrec aims to secure Silverpine Forest for the Forsaken and protect the Undercity's southern flank. He coordinates efforts to gather intelligence on enemy movements, eradicate the Rot Hide gnoll scourge infesting the region, and eliminate rival threats lurking across the forest from Fenris Isle to the outskirts of Shadowfang Keep.",al={"what is hadrec's goal","hadrec motives","hadrec silverpine goals"},it="wants",add="3524c842"},{q="Why is High Executor Hadrec here at the Sepulcher?",a="Hadrec is stationed at the Sepulcher because it serves as the Forsaken's central military and operational stronghold in Silverpine Forest. As High Executor, he oversees regional operations, coordinates field reports from the Deathstalkers, and dispatches champions to neutralize encroaching threats to ensure Forsaken dominion over the territory.",al={"why is hadrec at sepulcher","hadrec location silverpine","why is hadrec in silverpine"},it="why_here",add="ed357496"},{q="Who is High Executor Hadrec tied to?",a="Hadrec works in close concert with the Forsaken's covert intelligence wing, the Deathstalkers, receiving field reports and sending reinforcements to uncover hidden perils. He also collaborates with local specialists like Apothecary Renferrel to study regional threats such as the Rot Hide gnolls.",al={"hadrec allies","hadrec connections","who does hadrec work with"},it="ties",add="4117c6ac"}},ang={["race:Undead"]="As a Forsaken traveling south from Deathknell, you find in Hadrec the voice of Undercity’s high command, organizing newly risen undead to defend Lordaeron.",["faction:Horde"]="As a Horde ally arriving from Kalimdor, you can report to Hadrec and help steady Silverpine, where the Horde’s hold in northern Lordaeron remains tenuous.",["class:Rogue"]="As a rogue, you may work with the Deathstalkers under Hadrec’s command, recovering missing comrades and gathering enemy ichor and documents."},kw={"deathstalker","fenris isle","hadrec","high executor","rot hide","sepulcher","shadowfang","silverpine"},rel={"subzone:sepulcher","zone:silverpine","quest:442","quest:1098","quest:449","quest:437","subzone:fenris-isle","topic:forsaken"},src={"High Executor Hadrec"}}
E["npc:karos-razok"] = {t="npc",n="Karos Razok",z="silverpine",s="At the Sepulcher in Silverpine Forest, Karos Razok keeps the Forsaken bat roost ready.",h="At the Sepulcher in Silverpine Forest, Karos Razok keeps the Forsaken bat roost ready.",sec={{t="Keeper of the Sepulcher's Wings",b="Karos Razok tends the skeletal bats from the wooden platform above the Sepulcher's crypts. Moonrage worgen, rogue Dalaran magi, and the human remnants of Ambermill make the northern road through Silverpine Forest treacherous. Razok keeps messengers, fresh recruits, and vital supplies moving above the haunted canopy, linking the frontier outpost to the capital in Tirisfal Glades.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who is Karos Razok?",a="Karos Razok tends the Forsaken bat roost at the Sepulcher in Silverpine Forest. Horde travelers and messengers use the trained vampiric bats to cross Lordaeron.",al={"karos razok role","who is the flight master in the sepulcher","sepulcher bat handler"},it="identity"},{q="Where can Karos Razok send travelers?",a="Karos Razok sends travelers from the Sepulcher to the Undercity in Tirisfal Glades and to Tarren Mill in the Hillsbrad Foothills. His routes connect the outpost with northern Lordaeron.",al={"sepulcher flight paths","where does the sepulcher bat fly","flight routes from sepulcher"},gp=true},{q="What creatures does Karos handle?",a="Karos Razok tends large, skeletal flight bats. These undead fliers are hardy and tireless, and the Forsaken favor them for their silence and endurance in Lordaeron's blighted skies.",al={"what mounts does razok have","forsaken flight beasts","what are the flying mounts at sepulcher"}},{q="Why is a flight master important at the Sepulcher?",a="Hostile forces make Silverpine's roads dangerous, from Pyrewood's worgen curse to the human wizards at Ambermill. Karos Razok gives the Forsaken an aerial route to supply the forward base without risking ambushes on the highway.",al={"why is sepulcher bat master needed","sepulcher travel importance"},it="why_here"},{q="Whose side is Karos Razok on?",a="Karos Razok serves the Forsaken and the Horde. Stationed in Silverpine Forest, he pledges his allegiance to Lady Sylvanas Windrunner and the Undercity, aiding Forsaken couriers, scouts, and adventurers traveling across the region.",al={"karos razok faction","who does karos razok serve","karos razok horde"},it="side",add="db08745b"},{q="What does Karos Razok want?",a="Karos simply wants to keep the skies open and aerial transit running smoothly for the Forsaken. Managing the roost at the Sepulcher ensures that supplies, messages, and reinforcements can flow reliably between Silverpine and other Horde bastions.",al={"karos razok goal","what does karos razok do","karos razok motives"},it="wants",add="6a9fc34a"}},ang={["race:Undead"]="As an Undead, you can use Karos Razok's bat roost to travel back to the Undercity, Lady Sylvanas's capital, from the Silverpine front.",["faction:Horde"]="As a Horde traveler heading south toward Hillsbrad Foothills, you can use Karos Razok's bat roost as a waypoint on Lordaeron's western edge."},kw={"bat handler","flight master","karos razok","sepulcher","silverpine forest","undercity"},rel={"subzone:sepulcher","zone:silverpine","zone:undercity","subzone:tarren-mill","topic:forsaken","quest:6323","quest:6321","zone:hillsbrad"},src={"Karos Razok"}}
E["npc:minor-manifestation-of-water"] = {t="npc",n="Minor Manifestation of Water",z="silverpine",s="Along North Tide's Run, the Minor Manifestation of Water awaits shamans on Silverpine Forest's coast. Its corrupted counterpart must be cleansed before the peaceful spirit can be consulted.",h="Along North Tide's Run, the Minor Manifestation of Water awaits shamans on Silverpine Forest's coast.",sec={{t="A Spirit of the Western Tides",b="The Minor Manifestation of Water waits west of the Sepulcher, along North Tide's Run. For developing shamans, meeting the spirit is an essential rite. Water elementals embody life, renewal, and fluidity, yet malevolent blight can corrupt them. An initiate must face and defeat a corrupted manifestation before the pure spirit reveals itself. Once cleansed, the Minor Manifestation of Water guides shamans on their sacred journey to fashion a Water Totem.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Where can I find the Minor Manifestation of Water?",a="Find the Minor Manifestation of Water along North Tide's Run, on Silverpine Forest's western coast, just west of the Sepulcher.",al={"minor manifestation of water location","where is manifestation of water","north tides run elemental"},it="place",gp=true},{q="Why is the elemental hostile when I first approach?",a="A shaman must first summon and destroy the Corrupt Minor Manifestation of Water. After its defeat, the peaceful manifestation appears and speaks with you.",al={"corrupt minor manifestation","why is water manifestation angry","manifestation attacking me"},it="hostile"},{q="What quest involves this elemental?",a="The Minor Manifestation of Water guides shamans in the Call of Water chain, which ultimately teaches them to cast their Water Totem.",al={"call of water quest","water totem quest silverpine","what quest is this for"},it="purpose",gp=true},{q="Can non-shamans interact with this spirit?",a="The Minor Manifestation of Water guides shamans through their spiritual trials. Other adventurers have little reason to seek the spirit.",al={"is this shaman only","can anyone talk to manifestation","who talks to minor manifestation"},gp=true},{q="Who is the Minor Manifestation of Water?",a="The Minor Manifestation of Water is a spirit of the elemental waters called forth to test and guide aspiring shamans. Once cleansed of corruption, this elemental serves as a conduit of water's natural flow and wisdom, assisting those learning to heed the call of the elements.",al={"minor manifestation of water who","what is minor manifestation of water","who is this elemental"},it="identity",add="8e58f5e5"},{q="Whose side is the Minor Manifestation of Water on?",a="The manifestation belongs neither to the Horde nor the Alliance. It serves the balance of the elements itself, answering the summons of shamans who seek communion with water and demonstrating whether a supplicant possesses the strength and purity of spirit to wield its powers.",al={"minor manifestation of water faction","who does the manifestation of water serve","is minor manifestation of water horde"},it="side",add="c7703042"},{q="What does the Minor Manifestation of Water want?",a="This spirit seeks to test any shaman seeking mastery over water. It demands that you prove yourself capable of overcoming corrupting forces before it will share its pure essence and grant its blessing.",al={"minor manifestation of water goal","what does the water manifestation desire","manifestation of water purpose"},it="wants",add="9e575f56"},{q="Why is the Minor Manifestation of Water here?",a="The manifestation is drawn to places where water's power collects and awaits the rituals of shamans answering the Call of Water. It manifests specifically to commune with those guided to its presence by their elemental mentors.",al={"why is manifestation of water here","manifestation of water location reason"},it="why_here",add="05f89621"}},ang={["class:Shaman"]="As a shaman, cleanse the corruption from this elemental and receive its blessing to attune to the tides and forge your Water Totem.",["faction:Horde"]="As a troll, orc, or tauren shaman, you travel from Kalimdor to Lordaeron's shores to commune with this spirit."},kw={"call of water","elemental","minor manifestation of water","north tide's run","shaman quest","silverpine forest","water totem"},rel={"quest:63","subzone:north-tide-s-run","zone:silverpine","subzone:sepulcher","zone:barrens"},src={"Minor Manifestation of Water"}}
E["npc:quinn-yorick"] = {t="npc",n="Quinn Yorick",z="silverpine",s="At the Ivar Patch, Quinn Yorick hides from the ghoul that wounded him. The Forsaken scout waits in a ruined farmhouse, unable to finish his mission or retreat alone.",h="At the Ivar Patch, Quinn Yorick hides from the ghoul that wounded him.",sec={{t="A Precarious Refuge",b="Quinn Yorick lies gravely injured upstairs in a ruined farmhouse at the Ivar Patch. Ivar the Foul, a ghoul lurking in the farm’s barn in northern Silverpine Forest, wounded him in a vicious clash. Quinn and his sister Rane were sent to scout Silverpine and report to High Executor Hadrec. Too hurt to finish the mission or make a safe retreat alone, he remains in hiding. Passing travelers working for the Forsaken bring him healing and deal with the creature that nearly tore him apart.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Where is Quinn Yorick located?",a="Quinn Yorick hides on the upper floor of a ruined farmhouse in the Ivar Patch, north of the Sepulcher in Silverpine Forest.",al={"quinn yorick location","where is quinn","quinn yorick house"},it="place",gp=true},{q="Who injured Quinn Yorick?",a="Ivar the Foul, a ghoul lurking in the farm’s barn, severely wounded Quinn Yorick.",al={"who attacked quinn","what happened to quinn yorick","quinn injured"},it="conflict"},{q="What role does Quinn serve for Horde adventurers?",a="Quinn’s sister, the Deathstalker Rane Yorick, sends travelers to bring him a healing potion. After he takes it, she asks them to kill Ivar the Foul so Quinn has time to recover.",al={"quinn yorick quest","quinn quest giver"},it="purpose",gp=true},{q="Who is Quinn Yorick?",a="Quinn Yorick is a Forsaken Deathstalker sheltering upstairs in a decrepit farmhouse within the Ivar Patch. Severely wounded by the ghoul Ivar the Foul while scouting Silverpine Forest with his sister Rane, he hides in the shadows, relying on travelers of the Horde to assist him while he recovers from his injuries.",al={"who is quinn","quinn yorick lore","who quinn yorick"},it="identity",add="63631c13"},{q="Whose side is Quinn Yorick on?",a="Quinn is loyal to Lady Sylvanas Windrunner and the Forsaken, and by extension the Horde. He welcomes Horde champions who wander into the isolated farmstead, seeking their aid against the feral threats lurking just outside his refuge.",al={"quinn yorick faction","is quinn yorick horde","quinn yorick allegiance"},it="side",add="f58f2509"},{q="Why is Quinn Yorick here?",a="Quinn and his sister Rane were sent to scout Silverpine Forest and report to High Executor Hadrec, but at this farm they were attacked by Ivar the Foul, who grievously mauled Quinn. Unable to easily escape or press forward on his own, he holed up on the second floor of the abandoned farmhouse to survive.",al={"why is quinn yorick at ivar patch","quinn yorick purpose here","why quinn upstairs"},it="why_here",add="cd20af14"},{q="What does Quinn Yorick want?",a="Stuck nursing grave wounds, Quinn wants time to heal so he can travel again. A healing potion brought by adventurers starts his recovery, and his sister Rane asks them to kill Ivar the Foul before the ghoul can return for him.",al={"what does quinn want","quinn yorick goal","quinn yorick objectives"},it="wants",add="e4d12614"}},ang={["race:Undead"]="As an Undead, Quinn’s plight shows the danger ghouls and beasts pose to Forsaken forces trying to secure northern Silverpine."},kw={"forsaken scout","ghoul","ivar patch","ivar the foul","quinn yorick","silverpine forest"},rel={"subzone:ivar-patch","quest:425","quest:430","zone:silverpine","topic:forsaken"},src={"Quinn Yorick"}}
E["npc:shadow-priest-allister"] = {t="npc",n="Shadow Priest Allister",z="silverpine",s="At the Sepulcher, Shadow Priest Allister directs Forsaken efforts across Silverpine Forest. He watches nearby threats and helps secure Lordaeron's borders for the Dark Lady.",h="At the Sepulcher, Shadow Priest Allister directs Forsaken efforts across Silverpine Forest.",sec={{t="Watcher at the Sepulcher",b="Shadow Priest Allister directs Forsaken scouts from the Sepulcher in Silverpine Forest. From this settlement, he keeps watch for renegade humans, beasts, and the arcane activity around Dalaran.",sp=0},{t="Eyes on Ambermill and Dalaran",b="Allister's chief concern is the surviving mages of Dalaran, especially those at Ambermill who probe across the borders. He will not let the Kirin Tor gain a foothold in Forsaken lands. His agents intercept messengers, decipher arcane runes, and seek the wizards' long-term aims.",sp=0},{t="Heretical Musings",b="Allister's duties as a strategist share his attention with the study of shadow. He wrote 'Holy Bologna: What the Light Won't Tell You', a sharp attack on traditional holy doctrine. The book considers undeath's harsh realities and the Holy Light's failure to aid those cast aside by life. Somehow, copies have reached the ruins of Dire Maul in Kalimdor.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who is Shadow Priest Allister?",a="Shadow Priest Allister is a Forsaken priest at the Sepulcher in Silverpine Forest. He coordinates surveillance and strikes against nearby threats, especially Dalaran's forces.",al={"allister","shadow priest allister","who is allister silverpine"},it="identity"},{q="Where can I find Shadow Priest Allister?",a="You can find Shadow Priest Allister at the Sepulcher, the main Forsaken settlement on the road through Silverpine Forest.",al={"allister location","where is shadow priest allister","find allister"},it="place",gp=true},{q="Why is Allister focused on Dalaran and Ambermill?",a="The Kirin Tor mages at Ambermill threaten Forsaken territory. Allister works to decipher their communications, learn their intentions, and contain their influence.",al={"allister dalaran","why attack ambermill","dalaran threat silverpine"},it="wants"},{q="What book did Allister write?",a="Allister wrote 'Holy Bologna: What the Light Won't Tell You', a sharp critique of the Holy Light that reached the ancient libraries of Dire Maul across the sea.",al={"allister book","holy bologna","what the light wont tell you"}},{q="What quests does Allister offer?",a="Allister offers several intelligence-gathering missions in Silverpine Forest, including Border Crossings, Maps and Runes, Ambermill Investigations, and work against Dalaran agents.",al={"allister quests","sepulcher shadow priest quests"},gp=true},{q="Why does Allister practice Shadow magic instead of the Holy Light?",a="Like many Forsaken priests who felt abandoned by the Holy Light after death, Allister turned to shadow. He found power and resolve in a discipline that embraces undeath.",al={"why shadow priest","forsaken shadow magic allister"},it="motive"},{q="Whose side is Shadow Priest Allister on?",a="Allister is utterly loyal to the Forsaken and the Dark Lady. Stationed in the crypts of the Sepulcher, he turns his dark arts and calculating mind entirely toward securing Lordaeron for the undead and neutralizing any regional threats that challenge their fragile new domain.",al={"allister faction","who does shadow priest allister serve","is allister forsaken"},it="side",add="bfa3e4a4"},{q="Why is Shadow Priest Allister here in Silverpine Forest?",a="Operating from the Sepulcher, Allister keeps a watchful eye on hostile enclaves lingering along the southern borders. Between the surviving Dalaran wizards entrenched in Ambermill and strange magics stirring nearby, his role is to direct Forsaken operatives to probe enemy defenses and uncover their true intentions.",al={"why is allister at the sepulcher","allister silverpine purpose","why is shadow priest allister here"},it="why_here",add="9415cd7f"}},ang={["race:Undead"]="As an Undead, you share Allister's ruthless pragmatism as he protects his people from the living.",["class:Priest"]="As a Priest, you can see the Forsaken priesthood's disillusionment with the Light in Allister, author of 'Holy Bologna'.",["faction:Horde"]="As a member of the Horde, you share Allister's work to secure Silverpine Forest and keep the route between Tirisfal Glades and lands to the south safe for Horde allies."},kw={"allister","ambermill","dalaran","forsaken","holy bologna","sepulcher","shadow priest","silverpine"},rel={"subzone:sepulcher","zone:silverpine","subzone:ambermill","quest:479","quest:482","subzone:dalaran","subzone:dire-maul","topic:forsaken"},src={"Shadow Priest Allister"}}
E["quest:100"] = {t="quest",n="Call of Water",z="silverpine",s="At Silverpine's coast, the shaman completes the Call of Water at the Brazier of Everfount. The rite clears nearby corruption, and a spirit of pure water appears.",h="At Silverpine's coast, the shaman completes the Call of Water at the Brazier of Everfount.",sec={{t="A Burst of Cleansing Light",b="At the Brazier of Everfount, your final words call forth a burst of light. It scatters the minor spirits that threaten the spring, and the shore falls quiet.",sp=0},{t="The Water's Gratitude",b="A Minor Manifestation of Water appears beside the brazier after the spirits are gone. The spirit thanks you for the rite and says the taint here has ebbed. Yet life across Silverpine's decaying lands continues to wane, and the Horde's shamans must stay watchful to preserve it.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What happens when the brazier ritual finishes?",a="The final incantation at the Brazier of Everfount releases a burst of light that destroys the nearby corrupted spirits and purifies the surrounding flow of water.",al={"brazier ritual light","everfount explosion"},it="purpose"},{q="Who is the Minor Manifestation of Water?",a="The Minor Manifestation of Water is a small elemental of pure water that appears after the corrupted elementals near the Brazier of Everfount are destroyed.",al={"water spirit silverpine","manifestation of water"},it="identity"},{q="What does the water spirit say about Silverpine?",a="The spirit thanks the shamans and says that although the local corruption has ebbed, life across Silverpine continues to wane and needs constant care.",al={"water spirit warning","silverpine corruption"},it="place"},{q="Where does this ritual take place?",a="The ritual takes place at the Brazier of Everfount, along the coast of Silverpine Forest.",al={"brazier location","call of water location"},it="place"},{q="Why must shamans intervene in Silverpine?",a="Shamans must defend distant, embattled waters from blight and lingering corruption as part of their elemental trials to earn the Water Totem and prove their commitment to balance.",al={"why shamans here","shaman duty silverpine"},it="motive"},{q="What comes next in the trials?",a="After meeting the Minor Manifestation of Water, the shaman receives elemental remains or guidance to finish the journey and forge the Water Totem.",al={"next step call of water","after water manifestation"},it="next_step"}},ang={["class:Shaman"]="As a shaman, you prove your resolve by healing suffering waters far from home and earning communion with the spirit of water.",["faction:Horde"]="As a member of the Horde, you help cleanse corrupted waterways in Forsaken-controlled Silverpine and preserve elemental harmony."},kw={"brazier of everfount","call of water","elemental","minor manifestation of water","shaman trial","silverpine forest","water totem"},rel={"npc:minor-manifestation-of-water","zone:silverpine","quest:63","topic:light"},m={start="Brazier of Everfount",["end"]="Minor Manifestation of Water",level="23",faction="Horde",id=100},src={"Call of Water (8)"}}
E["quest:1103"] = {t="quest",n="Call of Water",z="silverpine",s="Along Silverpine Forest's coast, shamans can renew their communion with water through Call of Water. Tiev Mordune offers another Water Sapta to those whose spirit-sight fades before they speak with the purified water spirit.",h="Along Silverpine Forest's coast, shamans can renew their communion with water through Call of Water.",sec={{t="A Helping Hand in the Mist",b="Shamans drink a Water Sapta to see spirits near the elemental shrines. If its magic fades before they speak with the Minor Manifestation of Water, they can no longer enter the spirit realm to finish the trial. On Silverpine Forest's fog-shrouded shore, fellow shaman Tiev Mordune helps those whose visions end too soon.",sp=0},{t="Renewing the Ritual",b="Tiev Mordune has already defeated the corrupt water spirit off the coast and waits with the ritual remnants he gathered. To show you are ready, bring a fresh Water Sapta from Islen Waterseer in the Barrens. Tiev casts his gathered bracers and droplets into the shrine's brazier, summoning the pure manifestation again so you can speak with it and seal your bond with the element.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who is Tiev Mordune?",a="Tiev Mordune is a fellow Horde shaman on the coast of Silverpine Forest. He has defeated the corrupt water spirit there and stays by the shore to help shamans whose spirit-sight fades before they finish their communion.",al={"tiev mordune","who is tiev","tiev silverpine"},it="identity"},{q="Why do I need a Water Sapta for this quest?",a="A Water Sapta lets your mind cross into the spirit world. Tiev needs a fresh draught from Islen Waterseer so you can see the elemental when he summons it again.",al={"why need sapta","water sapta tiev","where to get sapta"},it="item"},{q="What happens if I missed speaking to the water spirit?",a="If the Water Sapta fades or the Minor Manifestation of Water vanishes before you speak with it, you cannot finish the trial alone. Tiev Mordune rekindles the brazier with the trophies he gathered, so you can commune with the spirit.",al={"missed the water spirit","failed water manifestation","manifestation despawned"},gp=true},{q="Where does this ritual take place?",a="The trial takes place on Silverpine Forest's western coast, by an elemental shrine facing the Great Sea.",al={"where is water shrine","silverpine water shrine location"},it="place"},{q="Who sent shamans on this pilgrimage?",a="Islen Waterseer, a tauren shaman, guides initiates through their Call of Water trials and brews the needed saptas. She lives by a fishing hut on the Barrens' eastern coast.",al={"who gave the call of water","islen waterstrider"},it="origin"},{q="What is the Minor Manifestation of Water?",a="The Minor Manifestation of Water is a purified elemental spirit summoned at the shrine after the corruption in the local waters has been cleansed. Communing with it completes this part of a shaman's elemental trials.",al={"what is the water spirit","minor manifestation"},it="target"},{q="Why is Tiev Mordune helping other shamans here?",a="Tiev Mordune is a fellow shaman who has already conquered the corrupt water spirit and prepared his offerings. Having seen other pilgrims lose their chance when the spirit realm faded too quickly, he chose to delay his own ritual so he could assist any brother or sister who stumbled during the trial. By offering his ritual parts and knowledge of sapta magic, he ensures no worthy shaman is left behind on their path to understanding.",al={"why does tiev help","tiev mordune motive","why is tiev waiting"},it="motive",add="890785ae"}},ang={["class:Shaman"]="As a shaman, you walk a hard path toward earning your Water Totem. This rite shows how shamans help one another so no initiate is left behind when a trance fades.",["faction:Horde"]="As a member of the Horde, you follow shamanic traditions of mutual aid and respect for natural spirits, even in Lordaeron's haunted lands."},kw={"call of water","islen waterseer","minor manifestation of water","shaman","silverpine forest","tiev mordune","water sapta"},rel={"quest:63","quest:972","npc:minor-manifestation-of-water","zone:silverpine"},m={start="Tiev Mordune",level="23",faction="Horde",id=1103,ri={"Water Sapta"}},src={"Call of Water (Silverpine)"}}
E["quest:264"] = {t="quest",n="Until Death Do Us Part",z="silverpine",s="In Silverpine Forest, Until Death Do Us Part brings Clarice Foster’s old grief to Yuriv’s grave. From the Pools of Vision beneath Thunder Bluff, the Forsaken asks you to leave her keepsake pendant on the tomb of the husband who abandoned her and their children.",h="In Silverpine Forest, Until Death Do Us Part brings Clarice Foster’s old grief to Yuriv’s grave.",sec={{t="A Bitter Keepsake",b="Clarice Foster remembers her mortal marriage without fondness. As Lordaeron crumbled, Yuriv left her and their children to join a crusade against the rising undead, declaring service to the Holy Light paramount. His devotion saved neither his family nor himself. Clarice was raised into undeath, while Yuriv lies beneath a defaced stone. She wants the last tangible reminder of his broken promises cast away.",sp=0},{t="The Neglected Grave",b="Yuriv’s tomb lies in the graveyard around the Sepulcher, marked by gashes, rubbish, and weeds. Set Clarice’s pendant on the relief of his sculpted hands, and no grand magic or spiritual closure follows. The gem grows dull, and a cold, silent gust passes over the tombs, leaving the old resentments of Lordaeron’s fallen people.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who was Yuriv?",a="Yuriv was Clarice Foster’s mortal husband. He left her and their children to fight the Scourge in the name of the Holy Light, putting his crusade before his family.",al={"who is yuriv","yuriv lore","clarice husband"},it="identity"},{q="Why does Clarice hate her late husband so much?",a="Clarice waited night after night while Yuriv put his religious duties first. His crusade failed to protect them; he died in a neglected grave, and she was raised as the undead kind he fought.",al={"why is clarice mad","clarice foster backstory"},it="motive"},{q="What happens when you return the pendant?",a="On the stone hands carved into Yuriv’s tomb, the pendant’s gem grows noticeably dull. A stiff, cool breeze sweeps over the Sepulcher, where the defaced grave lies in silence.",al={"pendant on grave","ending of until death do us part"},sp=1,it="next_step"},{q="Where is Yuriv's tomb located?",a="Yuriv’s tomb is in the cemetery at the Sepulcher, a Forsaken stronghold in northern Silverpine Forest.",al={"where is yuriv tomb","yuriv grave location"},it="place",gp=true},{q="Why is Yuriv's grave so damaged?",a="The grave is gashed, littered with garbage, and overgrown with weeds. The Forsaken at the Sepulcher feel no sympathy or reverence for a crusader who died fighting their kind.",al={"why is grave defaced","tomb abused"}},{q="Did Clarice's children survive?",a="Clarice says Yuriv abandoned his children along with her, but gives no word of their fate. With Lordaeron devastated, they may have met a tragic end.",al={"what happened to the kids","clarice children"}}},ang={["race:Undead"]="As Forsaken, you can see Clarice’s plight as the hypocrisy of the living: holy warriors left their families to perish in holy fervor, while their transformed survivors bear the burden of memory.",["class:Priest"]="As a priest, you can see how devotion to the Light can tear families apart and leave lasting bitterness in those left behind.",["faction:Horde"]="As Horde, you gain a glimpse of the personal tragedies and enduring spite that bind the Forsaken in Silverpine Forest."},kw={"clarice foster","crusade","forsaken","pendant","sepulcher","silverpine","tomb","yuriv"},rel={"npc:clarice-foster","subzone:sepulcher","zone:silverpine","topic:light"},m={start="Clarice Foster",["end"]="Yuriv's Tombstone",faction="Horde",id=264},src={"Until Death Do Us Part"}}
E["quest:3221"] = {t="quest",n="Speak with Renferrel",z="silverpine",s="At the Sepulcher, Apothecary Renferrel needs to discuss the tainted wolf hearts. High Executor Hadrec sends you back to the Royal Apothecary Society researcher with your findings.",h="At the Sepulcher, Apothecary Renferrel needs to discuss the tainted wolf hearts.",sec={{t="Summons from the Society",b="After you help the Deathstalkers across Silverpine Forest, High Executor Hadrec gives you an urgent message from Apothecary Renferrel. Renferrel has studied the discolored wolf hearts gathered from local wildlife and needs you at once.",sp=0},{t="Alchemical Curiosities",b="Apothecary Renferrel works for the Royal Apothecary Society in a laboratory inside the Sepulcher crypt. He studies how dark magic and disease are changing Silverpine's beasts, bringing alchemical research together with military reports from the front.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Where is Apothecary Renferrel located?",a="Apothecary Renferrel is in the Sepulcher crypt in central Silverpine Forest, beside his alchemy equipment and a short walk from High Executor Hadrec.",al={"renferrel location","where is renferrel","find renferrel"},it="place",gp=true},{q="Why does Apothecary Renferrel want to speak with me?",a="Renferrel has studied discolored hearts from Silverpine wolves and found strange signs in their corruption. He needs to investigate further and report to the Undercity.",al={"why does renferrel want me","renferrel wolf hearts"},it="purpose"},{q="Who sends you to Renferrel?",a="High Executor Hadrec, the Forsaken commander at the Sepulcher, gives you Renferrel's summons after you return from helping the Deathstalkers.",al={"who gives speak with renferrel","quest giver"},it="identity"},{q="What follows this conversation?",a="Your conversation with Renferrel leads to further work linking the Sepulcher's alchemical research with senior figures in the Undercity, including Apothecary Zinge.",al={"next quest after speak with renferrel","renferrel follow up"},it="next_step"},{q="Why does High Executor Hadrec send you to Renferrel?",a="High Executor Hadrec is simply passing along a formal summons on behalf of the Royal Apothecary Society. While you were scouting the Silverpine front lines for the Deathstalkers, Apothecary Renferrel requested your return to discuss the wolf hearts you previously gathered for his alchemical research. Hadrec ensures that vital business between the military post and the Society continues smoothly.",al={"hadrec motive","why does hadrec want me to speak with renferrel","why send me to apothecary renferrel"},it="motive",add="1f8d2902"}},ang={["race:Undead"]="As an Undead, you may hear of the Royal Apothecary Society's work alongside military command at the Sepulcher, where researchers study unusual creatures in Silverpine.",["faction:Horde"]="As a member of the Horde, you can learn how taint is changing the beasts of Silverpine."},kw={"hadrec","renferrel","royal apothecary society","sepulcher","silverpine","wolf hearts"},rel={"npc:high-executor-hadrec","npc:apothecary-renferrel","subzone:sepulcher","quest:449","quest:1359","zone:silverpine"},m={start="High Executor Hadrec",["end"]="Apothecary Renferrel",level="12",faction="Horde",id=3221},src={"Speak with Renferrel"}}
E["quest:421"] = {t="quest",n="Prove Your Worth",z="silverpine",s="At the Sepulcher, Prove Your Worth begins Dalar Dawnweaver's campaign against the worgen of Silverpine. The Forsaken seek a path south through human and dwarven lands, but feral worgen threaten the road. Their presence leads back to Archmage Arugal.",h="At the Sepulcher, Prove Your Worth begins Dalar Dawnweaver's campaign against the worgen of Silverpine.",sec={{t="Securing the Southern Corridor",b="Lady Sylvanas Windrunner and her dreadlord lieutenant, Varimathras, seek to secure the lands south of Tirisfal Glades, including human and dwarven enclaves. Silverpine Forest lies in their path, but the route is dangerous. Feral Moonrage worgen prowl the pine-covered hills, threatening Forsaken supply lines and forward bases.",sp=0},{t="Arugal's Blight",b="Dalar Dawnweaver says the worgen came through the work of Arugal, a disgraced former mage of Dalaran. During the Scourge invasion, Arugal unleashed otherworldly worgen upon Silverpine. He has since claimed Shadowfang Keep, while his feral creations roam the forest. Before Dalar trusts soldiers with a deeper inquiry into Arugal's sorcery, recruits must prove their fighting skill against the nearest Moonrage Whitescalps.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who is Dalar Dawnweaver?",a="Dalar Dawnweaver is a Forsaken mage at the Sepulcher. He leads efforts against magical threats in Silverpine, especially Archmage Arugal and his feral worgen pack.",al={"dalar dawnweaver","who gives prove your worth","sepulcher questgiver"},it="identity"},{q="Where are the Moonrage Whitescalps located?",a="The Moonrage Whitescalps prowl the woods and ruined homesteads of central Silverpine, just off the main road down the hill from the Sepulcher.",al={"where are whitescalps","moonrage whitescalps location","whitescalp farm"},it="place",gp=true},{q="Why does the Horde care about worgen in Silverpine?",a="The Horde needs Silverpine Forest as a route from the Undercity to the southern lands. Lady Sylvanas and Varimathras seek safe passage south, and the worgen packs threaten that route.",al={"why kill worgen","forsaken worgen problem","why clear silverpine"},it="purpose"},{q="What is Arugal's connection to these creatures?",a="Archmage Arugal summoned the extradimensional worgen to fight the Scourge while he served Dalaran. The beasts turned wild, and guilt drove Arugal mad before he withdrew to Shadowfang Keep to foster the curse.",al={"how did worgen get here","arugal worgen connection","who summoned worgen"},it="ties"},{q="What happens after proving your worth to Dalar?",a="After you prove your combat skill by slaying the Whitescalps, Dalar Dawnweaver enlists you in his campaign against Arugal's influence through the multi-part chain called Arugal's Folly.",al={"next quest","what follows prove your worth","arugal's folly start"},it="next_step"},{q="Is the Alliance involved in this quest?",a="No. Dalar Dawnweaver gives this to the Horde at the Forsaken outpost of the Sepulcher.",al={"can alliance do prove your worth","alliance silverpine"},it="side"},{q="Why does Dalar Dawnweaver want this done?",a="Lady Sylvanas tasked Varimathras with conquering the human and dwarven territories to the south, making Silverpine Forest an essential strategic corridor for the Forsaken. However, the mage Arugal's reckless conjurations have overrun the woods with feral worgen. Before Dalar can commit to a campaign against Arugal's curse and secure the region, he needs capable fighters who can clear the surrounding wilderness and handle the feral beasts.",al={"dalar dawnweaver motive","why prove your worth","why does dalar want whitescalps killed"},it="motive",add="8fc519da"},{q="What are Moonrage Whitescalps?",a="Moonrage Whitescalps are feral worgen roaming the hills and woods near the Sepulcher. Unleashed upon Silverpine by Archmage Arugal's reckless magic, they are vicious, predatory beasts that threaten Forsaken expansion and control across the forest. ",al={"moonrage whitescalps","who are the whitescalps","what are we killing"},it="target",add="dab3177e"}},ang={["race:Undead"]="As Forsaken, you help clear Silverpine to secure the Undercity's borders and remove threats left by Dalaran's failures.",["class:Mage"]="As a mage, you can see the danger of reckless conjuration in Dalar Dawnweaver's mission and Arugal's calamity.",["faction:Horde"]="As Horde, you help secure a clear military road through Silverpine toward southern Lordaeron."},kw={"arugal","dalar dawnweaver","moonrage whitescalps","prove your worth","sepulcher","shadowfang keep","silverpine forest","worgen"},rel={"npc:dalar-dawnweaver","quest:99","subzone:sepulcher","zone:silverpine","npc:arugal","zone:shadowfang","npc:varimathras","subzone:dalaran"},m={start="Dalar Dawnweaver",level="10",faction="Horde",id=421},src={"Prove Your Worth (Classic)"}}
E["quest:422"] = {t="quest",n="Arugal's Folly",z="silverpine",s="At the Sepulcher, Dalar Dawnweaver sends Forsaken agents to a nearby farmstead for Arugal's earliest spellbooks. The Forsaken need to understand the magic behind the worgen curse if they are to turn it against Arugal and secure Silverpine Forest. The Remedy of Arugal is the first step in unraveling the threat from Shadowfang Keep.",h="At the Sepulcher, Dalar Dawnweaver sends Forsaken agents to a nearby farmstead for Arugal's earliest...",sec={{t="A Mage's Derision",b="In the Sepulcher's crypts, ambitious Forsaken mage Dalar Dawnweaver holds Archmage Arugal in contempt. He sees him as an ordinary practitioner whose place in the Kirin Tor makes no sense, and whose grasp of magic seems amateurish. Yet the monstrous beasts roaming Silverpine cannot be ignored. To break Arugal's hold on the region, Dawnweaver means to take apart the spells that unleashed the worgen upon Lordaeron.",sp=0},{t="Remnants on the Farmstead",b="Before claiming Shadowfang Keep, Arugal lived at a secluded wheat farm just north of the river bridge. Deathstalker scouts found discarded spellbooks on the farmhouse's upper floor, but lingering beasts kept them from retrieving the texts. Search the dusty grimoires to uncover the Remedy of Arugal, an incantation that offers crucial insight into the unnatural curse afflicting Silverpine Forest.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Who is Dalar Dawnweaver?",a="Dalar Dawnweaver is an ambitious Forsaken mage in the Sepulcher in Silverpine Forest. Dedicated to Sylvanas Windrunner, he seeks to dissect and counter Arugal's magic so the Forsaken can claim the territory.",al={"dalar dawnweaver","who gives arugal's folly","sepulcher mage"},it="identity"},{q="What is the Remedy of Arugal?",a="The Remedy of Arugal is a spell written in Arugal's discarded books from the time he lived on the farm north of the bridge. Dalar Dawnweaver needs the incantation to study the arcane foundations of Arugal's work.",al={"remedy of arugal","arugal's remedy","what is the book"},it="item"},{q="Where are Arugal's old spellbooks located?",a="Arugal's dusty spellbooks lie on the upper floor of an abandoned farmhouse at the wheat farm just north of the bridge crossing in northern Silverpine.",al={"where are the books","dusty spellbooks location","farmhouse books"},gp=true},{q="Why does Dawnweaver look down on Arugal?",a="Dawnweaver considers Arugal an inferior wizard with a shallow grasp of the arcane. He cannot understand why the Kirin Tor accepted Arugal into its ranks in Dalaran.",al={"why dawnweaver hate arugal","dawnweaver opinion on arugal"}},{q="Why is this task important to the Forsaken?",a="Arugal's worgen slaughter Forsaken forces and threaten their hold on Silverpine Forest. By studying his spells, the Forsaken hope to stop the threat and secure the region for the Dark Lady.",al={"forsaken interest in arugal","why do forsaken care about arugal"},it="motive"},{q="What happens when you touch the dusty spellbooks?",a="Touching the dusty grimoires alerts a Moonrage worgen hiding in the farmhouse. It attacks anyone who disturbs Arugal's abandoned research.",al={"spellbook trap","moonrage darkrunner attack"},gp=true}},ang={["class:Mage"]="As a Forsaken mage, you can study Arugal's work as a warning of the danger magic brings when wielded without discipline or foresight.",["race:Undead"]="As an undead, you know Silverpine is the western shield of the Undercity. Reclaiming it from feral worgen is vital to securing the Dark Lady's borders.",["faction:Horde"]="As a member of the Horde, you face feral beasts contesting your presence in Silverpine. Neutralizing Arugal is vital to establishing stable supply lines out of Lordaeron."},kw={"arugal","dalar dawnweaver","dusty spellbooks","kirin tor","remedy of arugal","sepulcher","silverpine","worgen"},rel={"npc:dalar-dawnweaver","npc:arugal","zone:silverpine","subzone:sepulcher","quest:421","quest:99","topic:forsaken","quest:1886"},m={start="Dalar Dawnweaver",level="11",faction="Horde",id=422,ri={"Remedy of Arugal"}},src={"Arugal's Folly"}}
E["quest:423"] = {t="quest",n="Arugal's Folly",z="silverpine",s="In Silverpine, Forsaken agents seek shackles worn by Moonrage worgen. Dalar Dawnweaver studies Arugal's notes to learn how the renegade mage strengthened his unstable magic. The bindings may help the Forsaken break the worgen threat.",h="In Silverpine, Forsaken agents seek shackles worn by Moonrage worgen.",sec={{t="A Hack's Shortcut",b="Dalar Dawnweaver studies Arugal's recovered research with open contempt for his former peer. He says Arugal was never fit to serve Dalaran, much less wield high sorcery in the kingdom's darkest hour. Lacking talent, Arugal turned to enchanted relics and devices to strengthen and bind the worgen he summoned. Dalar needs samples of those objects to study the magic tethering the beasts.",sp=0},{t="The Moonrage Bindings",b="Moonrage worgen roam Silverpine with shackles that carry Arugal's binding enchantments. Moonrage Gluttons and Moonrage Darksouls prowl north and east of the Sepulcher. Their heavy metal shackles hold residual arcane energy, making them useful to Dawnweaver as he searches for a way to counter Shadowfang Keep.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Why does Dalar Dawnweaver want worgen shackles?",a="Dalar wants the shackles to study how Arugal used enchanted objects to make up for his weak magical talent. He hopes their magic will show how Arugal commands his beasts.",al={"why collect shackles","purpose of worgen shackles","dalar dawnweaver plan"},it="motive"},{q="Who was Arugal before he went mad in Silverpine?",a="Arugal was a mage of Dalaran. Dalar Dawnweaver calls him a mediocre talent in the Kirin Tor, but during the Third War Arugal used forbidden summoning from beyond this world to unleash worgen against the Scourge.",al={"arugal backstory","who is arugal","arugal dalaran"},it="identity"},{q="Where are the Moonrage Gluttons and Darksouls found?",a="Moonrage Gluttons and Moonrage Darksouls roam Silverpine Forest north and east of the Sepulcher, near old ruins and wooded trails.",al={"where to find gluttons","darksoul location","worgen locations silverpine"},it="place",gp=true},{q="Why are the Forsaken so concerned with Arugal?",a="Arugal's worgen threaten the Sepulcher and Forsaken control south of Tirisfal Glades. The Forsaken seek to break his magic and secure the northern kingdom.",al={"forsaken worgen threat","why fight arugal"},it="conflict"},{q="What does Dalar Dawnweaver think of Dalaran?",a="Dalar bitterly despises his former peers in Dalaran. He believes they were fools to trust Arugal with duties beyond his abilities.",al={"dalar dalaran opinion","dalar on kirin tor"},it="history"},{q="Is Arugal working with the Scourge?",a="No. Arugal summoned the worgen to defend Dalaran from the Scourge. The beasts became wild and drove him mad, and he claimed Shadowfang Keep as his own domain.",al={"arugal scourge alliance","is arugal scourge"},it="side"},{q="What are the Glutton and Darksoul Shackles used for?",a="These enchanted metal bands are forged by Archmage Arugal to reinforce his otherwise weak spellcraft and anchor his command over the worgen. Because Arugal lacked the innate power to control the feral beasts summoned to Silverpine, he bound them with these magical fetters. Dalar Dawnweaver requires them to study their enchantments and extract their residual energies, hoping to unravel Arugal's crude magic and devise a way to neutralize the worgen threat.",al={"glutton shackle","darksoul shackle","arugal shackles use"},it="item",add="044c53be"},{q="What are Moonrage Gluttons and Darksouls?",a="They are vicious worgen prowling the woods of northern and eastern Silverpine Forest. Once summoned into this world by Arugal to repel the Scourge, the monstrous beasts quickly slipped from his control and overran the local lands. Bound by enchanted shackles that channel Arugal's crude magic, these corrupted predators now stalk the forest, terrorizing both surviving locals and Forsaken scouts traveling through the region.",al={"moonrage worgen","who are moonrage gluttons","moonrage darksouls"},it="target",add="1eff7283"}},ang={["race:Undead"]="As Forsaken, you need to secure Silverpine from feral worgen to protect Tirisfal Glades' southern border and strengthen Queen Sylvanas's domain.",["class:Mage"]="As a Forsaken mage, you can recognize Dalar's harsh professional judgment: Arugal made up for poor arcane skill by channeling power through enchanted bindings.",["faction:Horde"]="As a member of the Horde, you need clear woods in Silverpine for safe travel along the high road from Tirisfal to lands farther south."},kw={"arugal","dalar dawnweaver","dalaran","darksoul","glutton","kirin tor","sepulcher","shackles","silverpine","worgen"},rel={"npc:dalar-dawnweaver","quest:99","npc:arugal","subzone:sepulcher","zone:silverpine","quest:421","subzone:dalaran"},m={start="Dalar Dawnweaver",level="14",faction="Horde",id=423,ri={"Darksoul Shackle","Glutton Shackle"}},src={"Arugal's Folly (2)"}}
E["quest:424"] = {t="quest",n="Arugal's Folly",z="silverpine",s="Worgen hold Deep Elem Mine in Silverpine's southeastern hills, keeping the Forsaken from ore needed by Varimathras's forces. Dalar Dawnweaver sends you to slay their corrupted foreman, Grimson the Pale, and carry his head to the Sepulcher.",h="Worgen hold Deep Elem Mine in Silverpine's southeastern hills, keeping the Forsaken from ore needed by...",sec={{t="Securing the Depths",b="Dalar Dawnweaver learns from the Forsaken Darkstalkers that worgen have reached Deep Elem Mine in Silverpine's southeastern hills. Their feral sorcery spread from Shadowfang Keep, where Archmage Arugal unleashed dark enchantments across the forest. Ore from the mine is needed to arm the Undercity. But worgen now make their lair in its shafts, and the mine lies unusable.",sp=0},{t="The Severed Head",b="Grimson the Pale leads the worgen through the mine's infested shafts. Dalar Dawnweaver orders you to slay the corrupted foreman and bring his head to the Sepulcher. With Grimson gone, the worgen will lose their leader, and Forsaken laborers can claim the mine for Lord Varimathras.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who is Grimson the Pale?",a="Grimson the Pale is the foreman of Deep Elem Mine. Like many laborers and residents in southern Silverpine, he was corrupted by magic from Archmage Arugal's experiments. Now he oversees a den overrun by worgen.",al={"grimson","who is grimson","deep elem foreman"},it="target"},{q="Where is the Deep Elem Mine located?",a="Deep Elem Mine lies in the craggy hills southeast of the Sepulcher in Silverpine Forest. Its tunnels run deep into the hillside and teem with worgen.",al={"deep elem mine location","where is deep elem","where to find grimson"},it="place",gp=true},{q="Why does Varimathras care about a mining operation?",a="Varimathras oversees the strategic expansion of Forsaken power. The mine's high-yield iron and stone are vital to arming troops and reinforcing fortresses throughout Lordaeron.",al={"why varimathras want mine","varimathras interest"}},{q="What happens after Grimson is slain?",a="Dalar Dawnweaver takes Grimson's head as proof of victory. Then he turns his attention to Arugal's spreading influence and prepares to strike at its heart.",al={"after arugals folly 3","what next","next quest"},it="next_step"},{q="What kind of magic corrupted the mine?",a="Archmage Arugal unleashed wild otherworldly magic and worgen curses across Silverpine. That magic reached Deep Elem Mine, corrupting its foreman, Grimson the Pale, and leaving the shafts overrun by worgen.",al={"arugals magic in mine","what corrupted deep elem","mine curse"}},{q="Who are the Darkstalkers mentioned by Dalar Dawnweaver?",a="The Darkstalkers are the Forsaken military's covert intelligence and scouting branch. From outposts like the Sepulcher, they watch enemy troop movements and regional anomalies.",al={"darkstalkers","who are darkstalkers"},it="allies"},{q="Why does Dalar Dawnweaver want Grimson the Pale killed?",a="While Dalar studies Arugal's dark enchantments, he must also answer to Varimathras, who demands the Deep Elem Mine to fuel the Forsaken's military advance across Silverpine. Arugal's spreading magic tainted the mine and corrupted its foreman, Grimson the Pale. Slain, Grimson's hold over the site will break, securing a critical source of ore and metal for the Forsaken while keeping Dalar in good standing with the dreadlord.",al={"why kill grimson","dalar dawnweaver motive","why does dalar want the mine"},it="motive",add="8e7515d1"},{q="What is the Head of Grimson for?",a="Dalar Dawnweaver requires Grimson's severed head as undeniable proof that the tainted foreman is dead. With Varimathras demanding swift results for his campaign, Dalar cannot afford any doubt that the Deep Elem Mine has been cleared of its corrupted overseer and is ready to be claimed.",al={"why take grimson's head","head of grimson purpose","grimson head quest"},it="item",add="49f6b035"}},ang={["race:Undead"]="As an undead, you help secure metal for the Forsaken to fortify their young nation against the living and the Scourge.",["profession:Mining"]="As a miner, you can seek Deep Elem Mine's rich ore veins once its tainted workers are cleared out.",["class:Mage"]="As a mage, you can see the danger in Arugal's runaway conjurations and transmutations seeping into the mines."},kw={"arugal's folly","dalar dawnweaver","deep elem mine","grimson the pale","sepulcher","silverpine forest","varimathras"},rel={"npc:dalar-dawnweaver","subzone:deep-elem-mine","npc:arugal","npc:varimathras","subzone:sepulcher","zone:silverpine","quest:421"},m={start="Dalar Dawnweaver",level="15",faction="Horde",id=424,ri={"Head of Grimson"}},src={"Arugal's Folly (3)"}}
E["quest:425"] = {t="quest",n="Ivar the Foul",z="silverpine",s="At the Ivar Patch in northern Silverpine, Ivar the Foul has trapped two Deathstalkers. Rane asks Horde travelers to kill the savage ghoul so Quinn can recover and they can finish their report to High Executor Hadrec.",h="At the Ivar Patch in northern Silverpine, Ivar the Foul has trapped two Deathstalkers.",sec={{t="A Mission Derailed",b="Rane and Quinn Yorick, siblings and Deathstalkers, were sent to survey Silverpine Forest for High Executor Hadrec at the Sepulcher. Their work ended in violence at a farmstead in the northern forest, where Ivar the Foul ambushed them.",sp=0},{t="The Threat in the Barn",b="Rane and Quinn escaped, but Quinn was badly mauled. An alchemical remedy made from forest beasts has not made him strong enough to travel. Ivar prowls the nearby barn, waiting for Rane's guard to fail. She asks Horde travelers to enter the barn and kill him, so the homestead can be secured.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who is Ivar the Foul?",a="Ivar the Foul is a Scourge ghoul lurking in northern Silverpine Forest. The Ivar Patch was once his farm, and he and most of his family and workers fell to the Scourge. He now ambushes passersby and attacks Forsaken scouts there.",al={"who is ivar","ivar the foul lore","what is ivar the foul"},it="target"},{q="Where can Ivar the Foul be found?",a="Ivar lurks in the barn at the Ivar Patch, just north of the ruined farmhouse where Rane and Quinn Yorick have taken shelter.",al={"ivar location","where is ivar","ivar the foul barn"},it="place",gp=true},{q="Who are Rane and Quinn Yorick?",a="Rane and Quinn Yorick are Forsaken siblings, a sister and brother, and Deathstalkers. High Executor Hadrec sent them to survey enemy activity in Silverpine Forest, where Ivar ambushed them.",al={"who is rane yorick","yorick brothers","who is quinn yorick"},it="people"},{q="Why does Rane ask an adventurer to kill Ivar?",a="Quinn was badly mauled in their first encounter and is still recovering. Rane must guard her brother against sudden Scourge attacks, so she cannot hunt Ivar herself.",al={"why kill ivar","why doesn't rane fight"},it="motive"},{q="Who receives the report on Ivar's death?",a="High Executor Hadrec, the military commander at the Sepulcher in Silverpine Forest, receives the scouts' reconnaissance logs. Rane promises to commend the adventurer's help in them.",al={"who is hadrec","who sent the yoricks"}},{q="What happens after Ivar is slain?",a="Killing Ivar the Foul ends the siblings' ordeal at the Ivar Patch. With the immediate danger gone, Quinn has time to heal before they finish their survey of the forest.",al={"what next after ivar","quest after ivar"},sp=1,it="next_step"},{q="What is Ivar's Head for?",a="Bringing severed heads back to your commander or patron is standard protocol in Lordaeron's wild frontier. Rane Yorick demands Ivar's head as indisputable proof that the vicious ghoul has been permanently destroyed. With Quinn incapacitated and vulnerable in their makeshift shelter, Rane cannot afford to take anyone's word on faith: only the creature's decapitated head guarantees his brother has the time he needs to recover safely.",al={"ivar head","why ivar head","what is ivars head for"},it="item",add="494849b1"},{q="Why does Rane Yorick need an adventurer to kill Ivar?",a="Rane cannot leave her brother's side. The ghoul savagely mauled Quinn during their initial scout, leaving him bedridden and reliant on healing draughts to mend his broken frame. With Ivar lurking in the nearby barn waiting for Rane's vigilance to slip, abandoning Quinn even briefly would leave him completely defenseless against a second strike. Far from Undercity reinforcements or The Sepulcher's patrols, an outside mercenary is their only lifeline.",al={"why rane cant kill ivar","why me ivar the foul","why not kill ivar himself"},it="why_me",add="2febd219"}},ang={["race:Undead"]="As an Undead, you know the danger faced by the Deathstalkers. Forsaken scouts caught behind enemy lines must rely on champions who come their way.",["faction:Horde"]="As a member of the Horde, you help protect Forsaken supply lines and strategic ground in Lordaeron by clearing away Scourge remnants like Ivar.",["class:Rogue"]="As a Rogue, you know the danger of stealth reconnaissance when ravenous Scourge horrors catch you unaware."},kw={"deathstalkers","ghoul","hadrec","ivar","ivar patch","ivar the foul","quinn yorick","rane yorick","sepulcher"},rel={"quest:430","quest:429","quest:428","subzone:ivar-patch","zone:silverpine","npc:high-executor-hadrec","topic:forsaken"},m={start="Rane Yorick",level="12",faction="Horde",id=425,ri={"Ivar's Head"}},src={"Ivar the Foul (quest)"}}
E["quest:428"] = {t="quest",n="Lost Deathstalkers",z="silverpine",s="In northern Silverpine, two Forsaken scouts have been missing for weeks. High Executor Hadrec sent Rane and Quinn Yorick to survey haunted farmsteads, and now you must learn what became of them.",h="In northern Silverpine, two Forsaken scouts have been missing for weeks.",sec={{t="A Silence from the North",b="High Executor Hadrec at the Sepulcher has heard nothing from Rane and Quinn Yorick for weeks. He sent the two Deathstalkers into northern Silverpine Forest to watch the abandoned farms and track enemy movements. Deathstalkers are the Forsaken’s hidden scouts and killers, serving Lady Sylvanas. Hadrec fears the Scourge or another threat has cut the scouts down.",sp=0},{t="The Northern Peril",b="Northern Silverpine lies between Lordaeron’s ruined estates and the shadowed borders of Tirisfal Glades. Undead roam there, beasts prowl, and feral worgen make travel perilous even for seasoned rogues. You must search the decaying farmsteads where Rane and Quinn Yorick began their survey, and recover any intelligence they gathered before danger overtook them.",sp=0},{t="Trapped in the Shadows",b="Rane and Quinn Yorick are alive, but trapped at a farm and struggling to stay free. They escaped an attack by the ghoul Ivar the Foul, though Quinn was badly mauled. Ivar lurks nearby, leaving the two Deathstalkers cornered. Their rescue draws the Forsaken into a deeper struggle with the feral threats beyond the road.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Who are Rane and Quinn Yorick?",a="Rane and Quinn Yorick are Forsaken scouts in the Deathstalkers, the Forsaken’s intelligence and assassination wing. They were sent to survey Silverpine Forest’s farmsteads and then disappeared.",al={"who are the yoricks","who are the lost deathstalkers","rane and quinn lore"},it="people"},{q="Why is High Executor Hadrec concerned about them?",a="High Executor Hadrec oversees Forsaken military operations from the Sepulcher. With two scouts missing, the Forsaken lack reports on hostile activity along their northern borders, where the Scourge still lingers.",al={"why hadrec care","who sent the yoricks","hadrec lost scouts"},it="motive"},{q="Where did the Yoricks disappear?",a="The Yoricks disappeared while scouting northern Silverpine Forest. Their route took them through the decaying farmsteads north of the Sepulcher.",al={"where are the deathstalkers","yorick location","where to find rane and quinn"},it="place"},{q="What threats do the Deathstalkers face in northern Silverpine?",a="Scourge remnants, aggressive predators, and feral worgen threaten scouts in northern Silverpine. Any of them can kill those who travel alone.",al={"what happened to them","silverpine dangers","why did they go missing"},it="threat"},{q="What happens after finding the missing Deathstalkers?",a="Finding Rane Yorick leads to helping the injured scouts recover through Wild Hearts, which brings you against local threats such as Ivar the Foul.",al={"what is the next quest","after lost deathstalkers","quest chain after yorick"},sp=1,it="next_step"},{q="Who are the Deathstalkers as an organization?",a="The Deathstalkers are the Forsaken’s corps of spies, scouts, and assassins. They serve the Dark Lady as her secretive vanguard across Lordaeron.",al={"what are deathstalkers","deathstalker order","forsaken assassins"},it="history"}},ang={["race:Undead"]="As a Forsaken, you know each missing agent could leave a gap in Silverpine’s fragile defenses. Finding your kin helps keep the Sepulcher safe from sudden attack.",["class:Rogue"]="As a rogue, you know the Yoricks as fellow operatives of the shadows. Their plight shows that stealth cannot always protect even seasoned Deathstalkers from northern dangers.",["faction:Horde"]="As a member of the Horde, you know Silverpine Forest guards a safe corridor between Undercity and southern Lordaeron. Reconnaissance helps protect that route."},kw={"deathstalkers","hadrec","quinn yorick","rane yorick","reconnaissance","scourge","sepulcher","silverpine"},rel={"npc:high-executor-hadrec","npc:quinn-yorick","quest:429","quest:430","quest:425","quest:1886","zone:silverpine","topic:scourge"},m={start="High Executor Hadrec",["end"]="Rane Yorick",level="12",faction="Horde",id=428},src={"Lost Deathstalkers"}}
E["quest:429"] = {t="quest",n="Wild Hearts",z="silverpine",s="Rane Yorick seeks help in Silverpine Forest as her brother Quinn lies badly wounded. She needs discolored worg hearts for Apothecary Renferrel at the Sepulcher, whose alchemy may help Quinn recover.",h="Rane Yorick seeks help in Silverpine Forest as her brother Quinn lies badly wounded.",sec={{t="A Brother's Desperation",b="Rane Yorick stays beside her severely wounded brother, Quinn, after the Deathstalkers' disastrous mission left them pinned down at a farm in northern Silverpine. The feral ghoul Ivar the Foul mauled Quinn, and he is failing to recover. Ordinary rest cannot mend an undead body torn by such savagery. Rane turns to the Royal Apothecary Society and its grim arts for a way to put her brother back together.",sp=0},{t="Alchemy of the Scourge-Tainted Wilds",b="The worgs of Silverpine carry the corruption spreading through northern Lordaeron. Their hearts are discolored and hold potent essences. The Royal Apothecaries can distill these blighted organs into concoctions that restore withered Forsaken flesh.",sp=0},{t="Renferrel's Cold Duty",b="Apothecary Renferrel works at the Sepulcher and greets the request with frustration, not sympathy. Lady Sylvanas Windrunner has charged him with pressing research, and he resents the Royal Apothecary Society being treated as field medics for blundering scouts. Still, he takes the gruesome ingredients and prepares a draught to keep the Dark Lady's agents operational.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Why does Quinn Yorick need worg hearts to heal?",a="Forsaken bodies need special alchemical aid to heal. Quinn was grievously wounded by Ivar the Foul, and the Royal Apothecary Society uses tainted, discolored Silverpine worg hearts to brew tonics for undead tissue.",al={"why worg hearts","quinn healing","healing potion recipe"},it="item"},{q="Where can the discolored worg hearts be found?",a="Discolored worg hearts can be found among the worgs roaming central Silverpine Forest, especially between the road where the Yorick siblings are stranded and Malden's Orchard to the east.",al={"where are the worgs","worg locations silverpine","worg heart farming"},it="place",gp=true},{q="Who is Ivar the Foul?",a="Ivar the Foul is a dangerous ghoul at the farm where the Yoricks took shelter. He attacked Rane and Quinn as they scouted there; both escaped, but Quinn was badly mauled.",al={"who is ivar","ivar the foul lore","ghoul ivar"},it="identity"},{q="Why is Apothecary Renferrel annoyed by the task?",a="Apothecary Renferrel works at the Sepulcher and says the Dark Lady charged him with grave work. He sees failed Deathstalker scouting as an embarrassment and a distraction from his greater alchemical experiments.",al={"why is renferrel mad","renferrel dialogue","renferrel's attitude"},it="conflict"},{q="What happens after giving the hearts to Renferrel?",a="After processing the discolored hearts, Renferrel sends you back to Rane and Quinn Yorick with a restorative potion. It can help Quinn recover enough to seek vengeance.",al={"next quest after wild hearts","what to do with the potion"},sp=1,it="next_step"},{q="Why do the Deathstalkers need help from an adventurer?",a="Rane Yorick cannot leave Quinn's side while he is so badly injured, and roaming Scourge and beasts threaten another ambush. She depends on passing Horde travelers to gather the organs and carry her plea to the Sepulcher.",al={"why can't rane get the hearts","deathstalker failure"},it="why_me"},{q="Why does Rane Yorick need you to gather worg hearts?",a="Rane Yorick is desperate to save her brother, Quinn, who was gravely injured in a disastrous skirmish against the powerful ghoul Ivar the Foul. Knowing ordinary rest will not suffice to mend Quinn's damaged undead frame, Rane seeks an apothecary's concoction made from local worg hearts to restore him before he succumbs to his wounds.",al={"why does rane want worg hearts","rane yorick motive","why help quinn yorick"},it="motive",add="a9c32125"}},ang={["race:Undead"]="As an Undead, you know the Forsaken survive through ruthless pragmatism. Even brotherhood may depend on scavenged organs and cold alchemy rather than divine grace.",["class:Rogue"]="As a Rogue, you see seasoned Deathstalkers laid low by a feral ghoul. Their fate warns how much stealth and skill it takes to survive the Lordaeron wilderness."},kw={"apothecary renferrel","discolored worg heart","ivar the foul","maldens orchard","quinn yorick","rane yorick","sepulcher","silverpine forest","wild hearts"},rel={"quest:428","quest:430","quest:425","npc:apothecary-renferrel","subzone:sepulcher","subzone:malden-s-orchard","zone:silverpine"},m={start="Rane Yorick",["end"]="Apothecary Renferrel",level="11",faction="Horde",id=429,ri={"Discolored Worg Heart"}},src={"Wild Hearts"}}
E["quest:430"] = {t="quest",n="Return to Quinn",z="silverpine",s="At the Ivar Patch, Quinn Yorick waits for a draught that may let him travel again. Apothecary Renferrel sends you from the Sepulcher with the mixture, while Quinn remains wounded in dangerous country.",h="At the Ivar Patch, Quinn Yorick waits for a draught that may let him travel again.",sec={{t="A Bitter Draught",b="After you gather wild beast hearts for the Royal Apothecary Society, Apothecary Renferrel brews a restorative draught for Quinn Yorick at the Sepulcher. He hands it over without ceremony and returns to his secret alchemical research. You carry the mixture back into the wilderness.",sp=0},{t="Respite at the Ivar Patch",b="At the ruined Ivar Patch, Quinn Yorick hides beside his sister, Deathstalker Rane Yorick. The ghoul Ivar the Foul wounded him so badly he cannot cross hostile ground. Quinn drinks the draught as soon as you arrive. It restores enough strength for him to travel in time, though danger still surrounds the farmstead, with Ivar lurking nearby.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Where is Quinn Yorick located?",a="Quinn Yorick is sheltering at the abandoned Ivar Patch in northern Silverpine Forest, well north of the Sepulcher.",al={"where is quinn","quinn yorick location","ivar patch location"},it="place",gp=true},{q="Who made the potion for Quinn?",a="Apothecary Renferrel brewed Quinn's potion at the Sepulcher for the Royal Apothecary Society, using wild beast hearts gathered in the forest.",al={"who brewed the potion","apothecary renferrel potion"},it="origin"},{q="Why was Quinn unable to move on his own?",a="Quinn was badly mauled by the ghoul Ivar the Foul while scouting with his sister, leaving him unable to move without Rane's help and medicine.",al={"why is quinn stuck","quinn yorick injured"},it="why_here"},{q="What happens after giving Quinn the potion?",a="The draught restores Quinn's strength enough for him to travel, and he can prepare to strike back at Ivar the Foul, who threatens their position.",al={"what next after return to quinn","next quest after quinn"},sp=1,it="next_step"},{q="Who is Quinn's sister?",a="Quinn's sister is Deathstalker Rane Yorick. She stayed beside him at the Ivar Patch to protect him and help them survive.",al={"quinn yorick sister","quinn sister"},it="ties"},{q="Does Apothecary Renferrel care about Quinn's fate?",a="Renferrel shows little personal concern for Quinn. He gives you the draught, then returns to his secret research for the Royal Apothecary Society.",al={"does renferrel care","renferrel attitude"},it="motive"},{q="Why does Apothecary Renferrel send you back to Quinn instead of going himself?",a="Apothecary Renferrel views Quinn Yorick's plight as little more than an inconvenience that interrupts his true research for the Royal Apothecary Society. Having concocted the restorative draught from the wolf hearts you supplied, Renferrel is eager to return immediately to his alchemical experiments and considers courier work beneath him. Entrusting the delivery to an adventurer lets him resume his studies without wasting further time.",al={"why send me","why renounce quinn delivery","renferrel why me"},it="why_me",add="fec360eb"}},ang={["race:Undead"]="As an Undead, you see how the Royal Apothecary Society's restorative mixtures help the Dark Lady's scouts keep working in hostile terrain.",["faction:Horde"]="As a member of the Horde, you know stranded scouts need help to secure the Horde's foothold in Silverpine Forest against feral worgen packs.",["class:Rogue"]="As a Rogue, you know how dangerous reconnaissance can be when pack predators catch operatives of the Deathstalkers off guard."},kw={"apothecary renferrel","deathstalker erland","deathstalkers","ivar patch","quinn yorick","quinn's potion","sepulcher","silverpine forest"},rel={"quest:429","quest:425","quest:428","npc:quinn-yorick","npc:apothecary-renferrel","subzone:ivar-patch","subzone:sepulcher","zone:silverpine"},m={start="Apothecary Renferrel",["end"]="Quinn Yorick",level="11",faction="Horde",id=430},src={"Return to Quinn"}}
E["quest:435"] = {t="quest",n="Escorting Erland",z="silverpine",s="In Silverpine, Deathstalker Erland needs help reaching his partner. Wolves have trapped him in a shelter, and he must cross their hunting ground to reach Rane Yorick.",h="In Silverpine, Deathstalker Erland needs help reaching his partner.",sec={{t="Cornered by Wolves",b="Deathstalker Erland is trapped in a shelter by hungry wolves. Even seasoned Forsaken scouts can be outmatched by Silverpine's wilds. The wolves circle the ruined refuge, drawn to the little flesh left on Erland's withered frame. Alone, he cannot break through their pack.",sp=0},{t="A Treacherous Crossing",b="Deathstalker Erland needs to reach his partner, Rane Yorick, near the Ivar Patch. The way crosses ground prowled by wolves. Once you guide him past them, Erland runs the last stretch to Rane Yorick's outpost. There, the scouts can bring their intelligence together for the Undercity.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Why are the wolves hunting an undead scout?",a="The wolves may be so hungry that they see a desiccated Forsaken corpse as food. Silverpine's feral wildlife attacks anything that crosses its territory.",al={"why wolves attack undead","why eat undead","erland wolves"},it="conflict"},{q="Who is Deathstalker Erland reporting to?",a="Deathstalker Erland reports to his scouting partner, Deathstalker Rane Yorick, who keeps watch at a nearby farmhouse near the Ivar Patch. Together, they monitor threats in the woods for the Forsaken.",al={"who is rane yorick","who does erland report to","erland partner"},it="people"},{q="Where does the escort lead?",a="The escort leads Erland from his refuge to the farm near the Ivar Patch, where he reports to Rane Yorick. After speaking with Rane, Erland goes inside and upstairs to check on the injured Quinn Yorick.",al={"escort destination","where does erland go","erland route"},it="place",gp=true},{q="What happens after Erland is rescued?",a="Once Erland is safely reunited with Rane Yorick, the two scouts prepare their findings. Rane then entrusts you with carrying their compiled dispatch back to the Sepulcher, as described in The Deathstalkers' Report.",al={"what next after escorting erland","the deathstalkers report quest","what follows erland escort"},sp=1,it="next_step"},{q="Are there other threats encountered during the escort?",a="Wolves patrolling the open ground between Erland's refuge and the farm near the Ivar Patch are the main danger.",al={"escort enemies","what attacks erland","what is on the road"},it="threat"},{q="What role do Deathstalkers play in Silverpine?",a="Deathstalkers are Forsaken rogues, scouts, and assassins. In Silverpine Forest, they go ahead of the main garrisons to track Scourge stragglers, Worgen incursions, feral beasts, and Alliance movements.",al={"what are deathstalkers","deathstalker role","deathstalker lore"},it="people"},{q="Why does Deathstalker Erland want an escort?",a="Erland is trapped inside his shelter by a pack of ravenous Silverpine wolves prowling right outside the doorway. Cut off from his fellow scout, Rane Yorick, he cannot deliver his scouting observations or fulfill his mission for the Forsaken while cornered alone. To break through the surrounding beasts and reach safety, he desperately requires your armed protection.",al={"why does erland need an escort","erland escort why","why does deathstalker erland need help"},it="motive",add="ef1632bd"},{q="Why does Erland need your help rather than other Deathstalkers?",a="Deathstalkers operate as isolated reconnaissance agents in hostile frontier territory rather than marching in large battalions. Erland and Rane Yorick are stationed far from the safety of Undercity reinforcements, leaving Erland pinned down with no guards or fellow agents nearby to relieve him. You are the only capable ally within reach to break the siege.",al={"why erland need me","why can't guards help erland","why does erland ask me"},it="why_me",add="fbccd737"}},ang={["race:Undead"]="As a Forsaken, you know Deathstalkers rely on teamwork and stealth. Erland pinned down by beasts shows the danger Silverpine's wilds pose to the newly risen.",["faction:Horde"]="As a member of the Horde, you help isolated Deathstalkers gather crucial reconnaissance for forces pushing outward from the Sepulcher."},kw={"deathstalker erland","deathstalkers report","ivar patch","rane yorick","silverpine forest","wolves"},rel={"npc:deathstalker-rane-yorick","quest:449","subzone:ivar-patch","zone:silverpine"},m={start="Deathstalker Erland",["end"]="Rane Yorick",level="11",faction="Horde",id=435,ri={"Deathstalker Shortsword"}},src={"Escorting Erland"}}
E["quest:437"] = {t="quest",n="The Dead Fields",z="silverpine",s="At the Dead Fields, Forsaken forces face a Scourge threat in northern Silverpine. High Executor Hadrec sends champions from the Sepulcher against the Rot Hide gnolls and the banshee who shields them.",h="At the Dead Fields, Forsaken forces face a Scourge threat in northern Silverpine.",sec={{t="A Plague upon the Fields",b="North of the Sepulcher, an abandoned farmstead lies overrun by Rot Hide gnolls. The fields once held ordinary farms, but now these plague ridden scavengers infest the Silverpine countryside. High Executor Hadrec sent small raiding parties to drive them out. Each attack stalled under a strange magical resistance.",sp=0},{t="The Banshee's Grasp",b="Nightlash, a Scourge banshee, directs the Rot Hide gnolls and scatters Forsaken skirmishers with dark sorcery when the gnolls face defeat. Hadrec sends Horde champions to cut down the gnolls and draw Nightlash into the open. He asks for her spectral essence as proof that she is destroyed.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Where are the Dead Fields located?",a="The Dead Fields lie north of the Sepulcher in Silverpine Forest. Rot Hide gnolls overrun the abandoned, decaying farmstead.",al={"dead fields location","where is dead field","where to find dead fields"},it="place",gp=true},{q="Who is Nightlash?",a="Nightlash is a Scourge banshee who commands and shields the Rot Hide gnolls at the Dead Fields. Her dark magic has driven off Forsaken assault parties.",al={"who is nightlash","nightlash lore","banshee nightlash"},it="target"},{q="Why are gnolls working with a banshee?",a="The Rot Hide gnolls of Silverpine Forest are tainted by the plague of undeath. The Scourge directs these rabid creatures as vanguard foot soldiers against the Forsaken through figures like Nightlash.",al={"why rot hides with scourge","gnoll scourge connection","rot hide gnolls lore"},it="conflict"},{q="How do you draw out Nightlash?",a="Nightlash stays hidden while the gnolls under her protection remain in force. Slay enough Rot Hides, and she appears in the field to defend her domain.",al={"how to spawn nightlash","where is nightlash","nightlash not there"},gp=true},{q="Who gives the quest The Dead Fields?",a="High Executor Hadrec, the Forsaken military commander at the Sepulcher, sends you against the Scourge threat as he seeks to secure the region.",al={"who gives the dead fields","dead fields quest giver","hadrec quest"},it="in_charge"},{q="What happens after Nightlash is destroyed?",a="Nightlash's essence proves to High Executor Hadrec that the Scourge has lost a vital presence in northern Silverpine. He then directs you toward the Decrepit Ferry east of the Sepulcher.",al={"dead fields followup","what comes after dead fields"},sp=1,it="next_step"},{q="Why does High Executor Hadrec want Nightlash destroyed?",a="The rot hide gnolls have entrenched themselves at an old farm known as the Dead Fields, threatening Forsaken operations across Silverpine Forest. Previous assaults sent by High Executor Hadrec failed because the banshee Nightlash intervened, using her dark sorcery to turn the tide and rout his forces. Until Nightlash is eliminated, Hadrec cannot break the rot hide encampment or secure the region for the Dark Lady.",al={"why kill nightlash","hadrec motive dead fields","why attack dead fields"},it="motive",add="1fb911a7"},{q="What is the Essence of Nightlash used for?",a="Upon her defeat, Nightlash dissolves into lingering dust. You collect this residue not as a magical ingredient, but as indisputable physical proof for High Executor Hadrec that the banshee has truly been destroyed and can no longer reinforce the rot hides.",al={"essence of nightlash purpose","why collect nightlash essence","essence of nightlash"},it="item",add="4cfc66ca"}},ang={["race:Undead"]="As Forsaken, destroying Nightlash strikes at the Scourge and recalls the spectral torment Sylvanas and her banshees escaped.",["faction:Horde"]="As Horde, breaking the Scourge's hold over northern Silverpine helps protect the travel corridor between the Undercity and Lordaeron's southern territories."},kw={"banshee","dead fields","hadrec","nightlash","rot hide","scourge","sepulcher","silverpine"},rel={"subzone:dead-field","npc:high-executor-hadrec","subzone:sepulcher","topic:scourge","topic:gnoll","topic:forsaken","zone:silverpine"},m={start="High Executor Hadrec",level="14",faction="Horde",id=437,ri={"Essence of Nightlash"}},src={"The Dead Fields (quest)"}}
E["quest:438"] = {t="quest",n="The Decrepit Ferry",z="silverpine",s="At the Decrepit Ferry, rot hides swarm the dock east of The Sepulcher. High Executor Hadrec sends Forsaken champions to learn why the Scourge has gathered along Lordamere Lake's shore.",h="At the Decrepit Ferry, rot hides swarm the dock east of The Sepulcher.",sec={{t="Eyes Across the Lake",b="High Executor Hadrec turns east after the Scourge presence in the Dead Fields is suppressed. The Decrepit Ferry lies among Silverpine Forest's eastern waterways, where mainland Lordaeron once connected to the island estates of Lordamere Lake. Now undead gather around its rotted piers. Hadrec sends scouts to find out what draws the Lich King's servants there.",sp=0},{t="A Grim Cargo",b="At the ferry, rot hides patrol the marshy banks. A waterlogged skiff rests beside the dock, carrying carefully wrapped, preserved corpses. Across the mist of Lordamere Lake, docks on Fenris Isle reveal where the bodies are headed: toward the island keep.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Who sends you to the Decrepit Ferry?",a="High Executor Hadrec, the Forsaken military commander at The Sepulcher in Silverpine Forest, sends you after you help clear the Dead Fields.",al={"who gives the decrepit ferry quest","hadrec quest ferry","quest giver decrepit ferry"},gp=true},{q="Where is the Decrepit Ferry located?",a="The Decrepit Ferry lies east of The Sepulcher, along Lordamere Lake's western bank where inland creeks meet open water.",al={"decrepit ferry location","where is the ferry silverpine","how to find decrepit ferry"},it="place",gp=true},{q="What creatures occupy the Decrepit Ferry?",a="Scourge undead occupy the area, mainly rot hide gnolls and reanimated skeletons that patrol the shore and docks.",al={"mobs at decrepit ferry","what enemies are at the ferry","decrepit ferry monsters"},it="threat"},{q="What do you discover at the ferry?",a="You find a corpse-laden boat pulled halfway out of the water, with wrapped bodies ready to be shipped across the lake toward Fenris Isle.",al={"what is at the ferry","ferry turn in object","what is in the boat"},it="purpose"},{q="Why does the Scourge care about the ferry?",a="The ferry gives the Scourge a crossing over Lordamere Lake, carrying fresh corpses directly to its stronghold on Fenris Isle.",al={"why are scourge at decrepit ferry","ferry scourge purpose"},it="purpose"},{q="What quest follows The Decrepit Ferry?",a="Inspecting the corpse-laden boat leads to Rot Hide Clues, where you investigate the gnoll operations and their link to Fenris Isle.",al={"next quest after decrepit ferry","decrepit ferry follow up"},it="next_step",gp=true},{q="Why does High Executor Hadrec want you to investigate the Decrepit Ferry?",a="The Forsaken keep a precarious hold over Silverpine Forest, and the sudden emergence of a new Scourge hive so close to the Sepulcher threatens their security. High Executor Hadrec cannot ignore an organized enemy concentration directly east of his base. He needs to uncover what purpose brings the rot hides and undead to the shore of Lordamere Lake before they mount an assault against the Forsaken.",al={"hadrec motive decrepit ferry","why send to decrepit ferry","why investigate decrepit ferry"},it="motive",add="2d3f81d3"},{q="Who are you sent against at the Decrepit Ferry?",a="The Decrepit Ferry has been overtaken by the Scourge, specifically packs of rot hide gnolls and walking dead. They are not merely wandering; they actively patrol the ruined docks, securing the site to load wrapped corpses aboard boats bound across Lordamere Lake for Fenris Isle.",al={"decrepit ferry enemies","who controls decrepit ferry","decrepit ferry targets"},it="target",add="e09d24e5"}},ang={["race:Undead"]="As Forsaken, you face a direct threat to Tirisfal's borders and the Undercity whenever the Scourge gains a foothold in Silverpine.",["faction:Horde"]="As Horde, you help protect supply lines through Silverpine by securing the perimeter around Lordamere Lake from northern Scourge incursions."},kw={"corpse laden boat","decrepit ferry","fenris isle","high executor hadrec","lordamere lake","rot hide","sepulcher","silverpine"},rel={"subzone:decrepit-ferry","npc:high-executor-hadrec","quest:439","subzone:fenris-isle","subzone:lordamere-lake","subzone:sepulcher","topic:scourge","zone:silverpine"},m={start="High Executor Hadrec",["end"]="Corpse Laden Boat",level="16",faction="Horde",id=438},src={"The Decrepit Ferry (quest)"}}
E["quest:439"] = {t="quest",n="Rot Hide Clues",z="silverpine",s="At Lordamere Lake, the Rot Hide Clues begin with an engraved ring on a recently deceased woman's hand. Reporting the grim find to High Executor Hadrec at the Sepulcher reveals that Rot Hide gnolls are taking bodies from Tirisfal's mass graves and carrying them to Fenris Isle.",h="At Lordamere Lake, the Rot Hide Clues begin with an engraved ring on a recently deceased woman's hand.",sec={{t="A Gruesome Cargo",b="Forsaken scouts find a corpse-laden ferry on the shore of Lordamere Lake. Among the dead is the unwrapped, plague-marked hand of a recently slain woman, with a simple band engraved “For Deliah.” The ferry points to organized transport, not scavengers feeding at random.",sp=0},{t="Raiders of the Graves",b="High Executor Hadrec fits the clues together when Deliah's ring reaches him at the Sepulcher. He concludes that a body so recently buried came from the mass graves across the border in Tirisfal Glades. Rot Hide gnolls in Silverpine are methodically exhuming human corpses and shipping them across the water to Fenris Isle for purposes no one knows.",sp=1}},faq={{q="What is the Corpse Laden Boat?",a="It is an old ferry moored along the shore of Lordamere Lake in Silverpine Forest. Rot Hide gnolls use it to carry exhumed human corpses across the water to their stronghold on Fenris Isle.",al={"corpse boat","decrepit ferry boat","lake boat"},it="identity"},{q="Who was Deliah?",a="Deliah was a human plague victim recently buried in the mass graves of Tirisfal Glades. Rot Hide gnolls stole her body, leaving her engraved ring as a clue.",al={"deliah lore","who is deliah","for deliah ring"},it="history"},{q="Why are gnolls gathering dead bodies?",a="The Rot Hides are undead gnolls serving the Scourge. They rob Tirisfal's mass graves and ship the corpses to the Scourge stronghold on Fenris Isle instead of eating them.",al={"why do gnolls want corpses","rot hide corpses","fenris isle dead bodies"},sp=1,it="threat"},{q="Who is High Executor Hadrec?",a="High Executor Hadrec is the military commander of the Forsaken stationed at the Sepulcher in Silverpine Forest. He oversees defense against regional threats, including feral Rot Hide gnolls, Dalaran wizards, and the Worgen.",al={"hadrec","sepulcher commander","executor hadrec"},it="in_charge"},{q="Where did the corpses on the boat come from?",a="Hadrec concludes that the bodies were dug up from the mass graves in nearby Tirisfal Glades, where victims of the Scourge and plague were hastily buried.",al={"boat corpses origin","tirisfal graves boat"},it="origin"},{q="What happens after reporting this clue to Hadrec?",a="Hadrec dispatches agents to counter the Rot Hide threat directly on Fenris Isle and retrieve samples of the putrid ichor they are refining. His actions also prompt an investigation into Deliah's identity and the return of her ring.",al={"after rot hide clues","deliah ring follow up"},sp=1,it="next_step"}},ang={["race:Undead"]="The desecration of Tirisfal's mass graves strikes close to home for the Forsaken, whose fallen kin and unrisen brethren are being carried away as raw material for gnoll alchemical horrors.",["faction:Horde"]="Hadrec coordinates Horde operations from the Sepulcher to secure Silverpine against growing monster encampments, including the Rot Hide pack occupying Fenris Isle."},kw={"corpse laden boat","deliah","deliah's ring","fenris isle","hadrec","rot hide clues","rot hide gnolls","sepulcher"},rel={"npc:high-executor-hadrec","subzone:sepulcher","quest:440","quest:443","subzone:fenris-isle","topic:gnoll","zone:silverpine"},m={start="Corpse Laden Boat",["end"]="High Executor Hadrec",level="16",faction="Horde",id=439},src={"Rot Hide Clues"}}
E["quest:440"] = {t="quest",n="The Engraved Ring",z="silverpine",s="High Executor Hadrec sends you across the border to Brill with a ring bearing Deliah's name. Magistrate Sevren searches the town records to learn who she was and where the ring came from.",h="High Executor Hadrec sends you across the border to Brill with a ring bearing Deliah's name.",sec={{t="A Keepsake in Silverpine",b="Scouts found a ring engraved with Deliah's name while investigating Rot Hide gnolls in northern Silverpine Forest. High Executor Hadrec sends you across the border to Brill with the ring. Magistrate Sevren keeps Tirisfal's civic records and burial registers, so he may identify Deliah. Hadrec doubts anyone among the Forsaken still cares about such keepsakes.",sp=0},{t="Stolen from the Soil",b="Magistrate Sevren confirms Deliah lived in Brill and was buried in the town's mass grave. Her ring among the Rot Hides points to a grim theft: the plague-warped gnolls have been raiding mass graves and carrying corpses south for Scourge experiments. Sevren wants the gnolls wiped out.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Who was Deliah?",a="Deliah is the name engraved on the recovered ring. Hadrec sends you to Magistrate Sevren's records in Brill to learn who she was.",al={"who is deliah","deliah lore","deliah ring"},it="identity"},{q="Why was Deliah's ring found in Silverpine Forest?",a="The ring turned up during the investigation of the Rot Hide gnolls. Sevren's records may reveal whose keepsake it was and how it reached Silverpine.",al={"why do gnolls have the ring","rot hide ring","how did ring get to silverpine"},sp=1,it="why_here"},{q="Why does High Executor Hadrec doubt the ring matters?",a="Hadrec says undeath often strips away mortal attachments. He assumes Deliah's lover is dead or, if risen as Forsaken, indifferent to mortal vows and memories.",al={"hadrec dialogue","why hadrec cynical","forsaken feelings"},it="motive"},{q="What role does Magistrate Sevren play in this quest?",a="Magistrate Sevren keeps Brill's municipal records and registers of the dead. He can confirm Deliah's identity and burial place.",al={"sevren brill","magistrate sevren role","who is sevren"},sp=1,it="purpose"},{q="Are the Rot Hide gnolls allied with the Scourge?",a="Yes. The Scourge plague infected the Rot Hide gnolls in Silverpine Forest. Dark influences guide them as they gather corpses for necromantic purposes.",al={"are rot hides scourge","gnoll scourge","silverpine gnolls"},sp=1,it="threat"},{q="Where does this investigation lead next?",a="Magistrate Sevren searches Brill's records for Deliah's identity. What he learns gives the investigation its next lead.",al={"what next after engraved ring","next quest","deliah continuation"},sp=1,it="next_step"}},ang={["race:Undead"]="As Forsaken, you can see Deliah's ring as a quiet link between a living past and Lordaeron's grim, cold present.",["faction:Horde"]="As Horde, you have reason to stop Rot Hide gnolls from desecrating graves in Horde-controlled Tirisfal, for the territory's security and in retribution."},kw={"brill","deliah","deliah's ring","gnolls","high executor hadrec","magistrate sevren","mass grave","rot hide","silverpine","the engraved ring"},rel={"npc:magistrate-sevren","npc:high-executor-hadrec","quest:439","quest:441","quest:530","subzone:brill","zone:silverpine","topic:gnoll"},m={start="High Executor Hadrec",["end"]="Magistrate Sevren",level="16",faction="Horde",id=440},src={"The Engraved Ring"}}
E["quest:442"] = {t="quest",n="Assault on Fenris Isle",z="silverpine",s="Forsaken agents move against the Scourge on Fenris Isle. High Executor Hadrec sends them to storm Fenris Keep and take the head of Thule Ravenclaw, the necromancer commanding the island stronghold in Lake Lordamere.",h="Forsaken agents move against the Scourge on Fenris Isle.",sec={{t="Purging Lake Lordamere",b="The Forsaken hold the western roads and have established their presence at the Sepulcher, but the Scourge remain entrenched in Fenris Keep. The island lies in Lake Lordamere, east of Silverpine Forest, and its forces threaten the forest and the southern waterways leading toward the Undercity. High Executor Hadrec sees Thule Ravenclaw’s vile experiments as a danger to Forsaken control of Silverpine. Thule commands the Scourge from the keep, keeping their power close to the Forsaken shore.",sp=0},{t="The Fall of Thule Ravenclaw",b="Rot hide gnolls and shambling undead guard the path through Fenris Keep to Thule Ravenclaw. The necromancer curses his attackers and leeches their vitality to strengthen his own strikes. When he falls, his severed head proves his death. The force of the magical shockwaves reaches the Sepulcher, where Apothecary Renferrel detects them.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Why does High Executor Hadrec want Thule Ravenclaw dead?",a="Thule Ravenclaw leads the Scourge on Fenris Isle. His entrenched force threatens the Forsaken stronghold at the Sepulcher and the waterways across Lake Lordamere, so Hadrec demands his head as proof that the Scourge’s regional command is broken.",al={"why kill thule","hadrec motives","fenris isle threat"},it="motive"},{q="Where is Thule Ravenclaw located?",a="Thule Ravenclaw resides deep inside the ruined castle on Fenris Isle, in the middle of Lake Lordamere east of Silverpine Forest. He holds court in the keep’s lower communal hall, guarded by undead retainers and twisted minions.",al={"thule ravenclaw location","where is thule","find thule"},it="place",gp=true},{q="What happens when Thule Ravenclaw dies?",a="Thule’s death releases a great wave of dark necromantic energy across the region. At the Sepulcher, Apothecary Renferrel detects the unraveling magic, and High Executor Hadrec commends the strike as a strategic triumph for the Forsaken.",al={"thule death reaction","what happens after thule dies"},sp=1,it="next_step"},{q="Who controls Fenris Isle before this assault?",a="The Scourge occupy Fenris Isle. Thule Ravenclaw uses its castle as a staging ground, commanding reanimated undead and blight-twisted rot hide gnolls to terrorize Lake Lordamere’s waters.",al={"who holds fenris isle","fenris isle faction","is fenris isle scourge"},it="residents"},{q="Why was Bethor's Potion important for this mission?",a="Thule casts Hex of the Ravenclaw, a curse that weakens his opponents and magnifies his own power. Bethor Iceshard supplied counter-incantations, which Apothecary Renferrel brewed into a potion during earlier operations to neutralize the necrotic curse.",al={"hex of the ravenclaw cure","bethor potion thule","counter thule hex"},it="power",gp=true},{q="What is the strategic significance of Fenris Isle to the Forsaken?",a="Fenris Isle sits in Lake Lordamere, bordering Silverpine and the Hillsbrad foothills. Securing or neutralizing the island removes an enemy outpost that can attack Silverpine and clears a major Scourge presence from Lordaeron’s borders.",al={"why fenris isle matters","fenris isle importance"},it="conflict"},{q="What is Thule's Head for?",a="High Executor Hadrec demands Thule's Head as undeniable proof that the necromancer has finally been destroyed. Fenris Isle is a fortified Scourge stronghold, and Hadrec will not commit to claiming victory in Silverpine until he sees physical evidence that their leader's grip on the region is broken.",al={"thules head use","why take thules head","proof of thules death"},it="item",add="3fc2276d"},{q="Who is Thule Ravenclaw?",a="Thule Ravenclaw is a powerful Scourge necromancer commanding the undead forces entrenched on Fenris Isle. From the keep in the middle of Lake Lordamere, he directs the Scourge's operations throughout Silverpine Forest, posing an immediate threat to the Forsaken presence at the Sepulcher.",al={"who is thule","thule ravenclaw lore","why is thule on fenris isle"},it="target",add="8bb87601"}},ang={["race:Undead"]="For you as Forsaken, killing Thule Ravenclaw is personal retribution. Crushing Scourge outposts proves your people have broken free of the Lich King’s will.",["faction:Horde"]="As a member of the Horde, you rely on the Forsaken to stabilize Silverpine and Tirisfal against rival powers and the wandering Scourge.",["class:Mage"]="As a mage, you may share Bethor Iceshard and Apothecary Renferrel’s interest in the magical fallout of Thule’s death and the violent dispersal of his necrotic weaves."},kw={"fenris isle","hadrec","lake lordamere","scourge","sepulcher","silverpine forest","thule ravenclaw"},rel={"quest:446","subzone:fenris-isle","npc:high-executor-hadrec","subzone:sepulcher","quest:448","topic:scourge","topic:forsaken","zone:silverpine"},m={start="High Executor Hadrec",level="20",faction="Horde",id=442,ri={"Thule's Head"}},src={"Assault on Fenris Isle"}}
E["quest:443"] = {t="quest",n="Rot Hide Ichor",z="silverpine",s="High Executor Hadrec seeks Rot Hide Ichor in Silverpine Forest before the Forsaken attack Fenris Isle. He wants the fluid studied to understand the gnolls that infest the island.",h="High Executor Hadrec seeks Rot Hide Ichor in Silverpine Forest before the Forsaken attack Fenris Isle.",sec={{t="Unnatural Biology",b="Rot Hide gnolls on Fenris Isle are decaying, aggressive, and unlike ordinary wild humanoids. They hold strategic ground across Lordamere Lake. High Executor Hadrec believes the strange fluid in their veins may explain their unnatural resilience. He needs samples before committing Forsaken soldiers to a costly assault.",sp=0},{t="Apothecary Analysis",b="The Royal Apothecary Society works from the Sepulcher, where Apothecary Renferrel studies biological and chemical anomalies. Bring him samples of the putrid fluid, and the Forsaken hope to learn where the gnolls came from, who is engineering them, and what weaknesses they have in battle.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What is Rot Hide ichor?",a="Rot Hide Ichor is a putrid fluid that flows through the bodies of the Rot Hide gnolls on Fenris Isle. It sustains their undead-like, rotting state and gives them unusual resilience.",al={"what is the ichor","rot hide fluid","gnoll ichor"},it="item"},{q="Why does High Executor Hadrec want samples of the ichor?",a="High Executor Hadrec wants samples studied before the Forsaken assault Fenris Isle. Apothecary Renferrel may be able to trace who created the Rot Hides and find a weakness to exploit.",al={"why collect ichor","hadrec's goal","why hadrec wants ichor"},it="motive"},{q="Where are the Rot Hide gnolls located?",a="The Rot Hide gnolls live on Fenris Isle, east across Lordamere Lake from the Decrepit Ferry in Silverpine Forest. Rot Hide brutes, plague weavers, and other breeds overrun its shore, camps, and ruined grounds.",al={"where do i find rot hides","rot hide gnoll location","fenris gnolls"},it="place",gp=true},{q="Who is Apothecary Renferrel?",a="Apothecary Renferrel is a Royal Apothecary Society researcher stationed outside the crypt at the Sepulcher. He studies local blights, plagues, and strange biological hazards throughout Silverpine Forest for the Forsaken.",al={"who is renferrel","apothecary renferrel role"},it="identity"},{q="What happens after Renferrel receives the ichor?",a="After receiving the samples, Renferrel analyzes the fluid's chemical makeup to trace the Rot Hides' origin. His work leads into Rot Hide Origins.",al={"next quest after rot hide ichor","rot hide ichor follow up"},it="next_step"},{q="Why do the Forsaken care about gnolls?",a="The Rot Hide gnolls hold Fenris Isle, a vital stronghold in Lordamere Lake on the border of Forsaken territory. Their rotting condition and plague-like abilities suggest outside tampering and could threaten Undercity's security.",al={"why forsaken fight gnolls","gnoll threat silverpine"},it="conflict"},{q="Who are the Rot Hide gnolls on Fenris Isle?",a="The Rot Hides are an aggressive tribe of gnolls inhabiting Fenris Isle on Lordamere Lake. Unlike ordinary gnolls, they are visibly corrupted and rotting, bearing unnatural plagues and filth. The Forsaken consider them a dangerous blight right on the border of Silverpine Forest, prompting High Executor Hadrec to prepare an offensive against their stronghold.",al={"who are the rot hides","fenris isle gnolls","what are rot hide gnolls"},it="target",add="c47d3478"}},ang={["race:Undead"]="As Forsaken, you know that studying biological horrors and engineered diseases is part of survival. The Royal Apothecary Society examines the Rot Hides' fluid to learn whether the infection threatens Forsaken claims in Lordaeron.",["faction:Horde"]="As a member of the Horde, you know Fenris Isle lies on Silverpine Forest's eastern edge. Left unmonitored, it poses a tactical danger to the forces securing the surrounding lands."},kw={"apothecary renferrel","fenris isle","high executor hadrec","lordamere lake","rot hide gnolls","rot hide ichor","sepulcher","silverpine forest"},rel={"quest:439","quest:444","quest:442","npc:high-executor-hadrec","npc:apothecary-renferrel","subzone:fenris-isle","subzone:sepulcher","zone:silverpine"},m={start="High Executor Hadrec",["end"]="Apothecary Renferrel",level="17",faction="Horde",id=443,ri={"Rot Hide Ichor"}},src={"Rot Hide Ichor (quest)"}}
E["quest:445"] = {t="quest",n="Delivery to Silverpine Forest",z="silverpine",s="You carry Apothecary Johaan’s findings from Brill to Apothecary Renferrel at the Sepulcher. The Royal Apothecary Society needs them for its work on the New Plague.",h="You carry Apothecary Johaan’s findings from Brill to Apothecary Renferrel at the Sepulcher.",sec={{t="A Society Bound by Purpose",b="The Royal Apothecary Society answers directly to Lady Sylvanas Windrunner and works to concoct a New Plague that can wipe out the living and the Scourge. Its laboratories are scattered across Forsaken territory, so researchers must share their findings to keep their work moving. In Brill, Apothecary Johaan has gathered experimental results for other field researchers. You carry them south to Renferrel at the Sepulcher.",sp=0},{t="Outpost in the South",b="Silverpine Forest is the next frontier of Forsaken expansion and research. Apothecary Renferrel works from the Sepulcher, where he oversees biochemical testing amid threats from Moonrage worgen, rogue humans, and the lingering Scourge. He receives Johaan’s notes from Tirisfal Glades and folds their alchemical findings into his own local experiments, advancing the Society’s design.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Why is Apothecary Johaan sending these documents?",a="The Royal Apothecary Society expects its members to share discoveries so they can speed the creation of the New Plague. Johaan sends his latest findings from Tirisfal Glades south for other researchers to build on.",al={"why courier findings","johaan notes","why send research"},it="motive"},{q="Where is the Sepulcher located?",a="The Sepulcher is the main Forsaken outpost in Silverpine Forest. It lies south of the Tirisfal Glades border and southwest of the Undercity, along the main road through the woods.",al={"where is sepulcher","finding renferrel","sepulcher location"},it="place",gp=true},{q="Who is Apothecary Renferrel?",a="Apothecary Renferrel is a prominent member of the Royal Apothecary Society stationed at the Sepulcher. He directs field testing and studies exotic ingredients found throughout Silverpine Forest, then reports to the Society’s leaders in the Undercity.",al={"renferrel role","who is renferrel","renferrel silverpine"},it="identity"},{q="What is the New Plague mentioned by Johaan?",a="The New Plague is an alchemical contagion the Royal Apothecary Society is developing under Lady Sylvanas Windrunner’s orders. It is designed to eradicate living enemies and the undead minions of the Lich King.",al={"new plague","sylvanas plague","what plague"},it="purpose"},{q="What is the Necropolis Renferrel mentions?",a="Renferrel says he needs to send samples to “the Necropolis,” but this exchange does not identify which necropolis he means.",al={"necropolis renferrel","renferrel samples","samples to necropolis"},it="place"},{q="Why use an adventurer instead of official messengers?",a="Forsaken couriers face dangerous roads with feral worgen, aggressive wildlife, and hostile human survivors. An able-bodied adventurer can carry the delicate alchemical notes safely to the Sepulcher and lend a hand with work in the region.",al={"why me courier","why adventurer messenger"},it="why_me"}},ang={["race:Undead"]="As an Undead, carrying this research serves Lady Sylvanas and the survival of the Forsaken. It helps advance the Royal Apothecary Society’s central ambition.",["faction:Horde"]="As a member of the Horde, you help keep the northern territories secure by carrying messages along the Silverpine road, even when Forsaken alchemical research raises eyebrows among your allies."},kw={"brill","delivery to silverpine forest","johaan","new plague","renferrel","royal apothecary society","sepulcher","silverpine"},rel={"npc:apothecary-johaan","npc:apothecary-renferrel","topic:royal-apothecary-society","subzone:sepulcher","subzone:brill","zone:silverpine","zone:tirisfal","zone:undercity"},m={start="Apothecary Johaan",["end"]="Apothecary Renferrel",level="10",faction="Horde",id=445},src={"Delivery to Silverpine Forest"}}
E["quest:446"] = {t="quest",n="Thule Ravenclaw",z="silverpine",s="A courier brings strange Rot Hide ichor to Bethor Iceshard, who recognizes the work of his traitorous former colleague, Thule Ravenclaw. To help the Forsaken resist the gnolls, Bethor prepares a scroll of counter-incantations for Apothecary Renferrel.",h="A courier brings strange Rot Hide ichor to Bethor Iceshard, who recognizes the work of his traitorous former...",sec={{t="A Colleague Turned Traitor",b="At the Magic Quarter of the Undercity, Bethor Iceshard recognizes the arcane mark in a courier’s sample of Rot Hide ichor. Thule Ravenclaw made the distillation. Before the Third War, Thule was a bright young mage and Bethor’s colleague. When the Lich King rose to power, Thule betrayed his peers and swore himself to the Scourge. As Lordaeron fell, he abandoned his humanity.",sp=0},{t="The Master of Fenris Isle",b="Bethor learns that Thule survived the war and now holds Fenris Keep on Fenris Isle, in Lake Lordamere. Thule commands the Rot Hide gnolls, filling them with foul magic and sending them against Forsaken borders. Bethor draws on his close knowledge of Thule’s magic as he writes a scroll to counter the mage’s curses and wards.",sp=1},{t="Alchemical Countermeasures",b="A courier carries Bethor’s scroll back to the Sepulcher for Apothecary Renferrel of the Royal Apothecary Society. Renferrel studies the Undercity mage’s potent incantations and begins joining high sorcery with the Society’s alchemical brews. The mixture is made specifically to shatter Ravenclaw’s hexes, clearing a path for an assault on Fenris Keep.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Who is Thule Ravenclaw?",a="Before the Scourge claimed him, Thule Ravenclaw was a promising human mage trained in Dalaran who studied with Bethor Iceshard. He betrayed his brethren to serve the Scourge as the Lich King spread corruption through Lordaeron, and eventually rose to command the Rot Hide gnolls from Fenris Isle.",al={"thule lore","who is thule","thule ravenclaw backstory"},it="identity"},{q="Why does Bethor Iceshard know Thule's magic?",a="Bethor and Thule were colleagues and fellow spellcasters before Lordaeron fell. Their studies together left Bethor intimately familiar with Thule’s favored spells, magical theory, and hexes.",al={"bethor and thule","how does bethor know thule","bethor iceshard connection"},it="ties"},{q="What is Bethor's Scroll used for?",a="Bethor’s Scroll holds counter-incantations crafted to unravel Thule’s spells. Apothecary Renferrel uses them to brew a potion that shields Forsaken champions from Ravenclaw’s hexes.",al={"bethors scroll","scroll purpose","what does the scroll do"},it="item"},{q="Why are the Rot Hide gnolls a threat in Silverpine?",a="Thule Ravenclaw uses Scourge necromancy to coordinate and empower the Rot Hide gnolls. From Fenris Isle, they mount organized attacks on Forsaken settlements and patrols across Silverpine Forest.",al={"rot hide gnolls","why fight gnolls","fenris isle gnolls"},it="threat"},{q="Where does this quest take place?",a="The journey begins with Bethor Iceshard in the Undercity’s Magic Quarter and ends with Apothecary Renferrel at the Sepulcher in Silverpine Forest.",al={"thule ravenclaw turn in","where to turn in thule ravenclaw","scroll delivery location"},it="place",gp=true},{q="What happens after Renferrel receives the scroll?",a="After developing the counter-potion, Renferrel sends you to report to High Executor Hadrec before an all-out assault on Fenris Isle to eliminate Thule Ravenclaw and reclaim the island.",al={"what happens next","after thule ravenclaw quest","fenris isle attack"},sp=1,it="next_step"},{q="Why does Bethor Iceshard want the scroll delivered to Renferrel?",a="Upon inspecting the ichor, Bethor was shocked to discover that his former colleague, Thule Ravenclaw, not only survived the war but betrayed his kin to serve the Scourge and lead the Rot Hide gnolls against the Forsaken. Bethor knows Thule's magical repertoire intimately. By sending this enchanted scroll to Apothecary Renferrel, he provides the arcane incantations required to brew a potion capable of neutralizing Thule's foul hexes.",al={"why deliver bethor's scroll","bethor iceshard motive","why send scroll to renferrel"},it="motive",add="bea76ce7"}},ang={["class:Mage"]="The conflict between Bethor and Thule reveals the divide among Lordaeron’s former magi: some fell to necromancy, while others kept their arcane discipline through undeath.",["race:Undead"]="For the Forsaken, stopping Thule Ravenclaw matters because his hold on Fenris Isle threatens the Sepulcher and the western approaches to the Capital City.",["faction:Horde"]="Driving Scourge remnants from Lordaeron helps secure the Horde’s only foothold in the Eastern Kingdoms."},kw={"apothecary renferrel","bethor iceshard","fenris isle","rot hide","scourge","sepulcher","silverpine","thule ravenclaw"},rel={"quest:444","quest:448","quest:442","npc:bethor-iceshard","npc:apothecary-renferrel","subzone:fenris-isle","subzone:sepulcher","zone:silverpine"},m={start="Bethor Iceshard",["end"]="Apothecary Renferrel",level="16",faction="Horde",id=446},src={"Thule Ravenclaw (quest)"}}
E["quest:448"] = {t="quest",n="Report to Hadrec",z="silverpine",s="Apothecary Renferrel sends you to Hadrec as the Scourge threat grows. After Renferrel and Bethor Iceshard investigate the Scourge presence in Lake Lordamere, High Executor Hadrec directs Silverpine's military preparations against Fenris Isle.",h="Apothecary Renferrel sends you to Hadrec as the Scourge threat grows.",sec={{t="Escalation in Silverpine",b="Apothecary Renferrel and Bethor Iceshard have studied the danger posed by the renegade necromancer Thule Ravenclaw. But study alone cannot break the Scourge stronghold rising on Fenris Isle. Ravenclaw is binding the restless dead there, and Renferrel sees that alchemy and magic will not be enough. The Forsaken military must bring its steel and discipline to bear, so Renferrel sends you to the commander.",sp=0},{t="The High Executor's Arsenal",b="High Executor Hadrec directs Silverpine Forest's strategic operations for the Dark Lady from the Sepulcher's crypts. Bethor's warnings about Ravenclaw reach him, and Hadrec knows a necromancer entrenched on Lordamere's western shore threatens Undercity's flank. He opens the local garrison's armory to equip the vanguard before sending them against the island fortress.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who is High Executor Hadrec?",a="High Executor Hadrec commands the Forsaken forces stationed at the Sepulcher. He oversees defense and offensive operations throughout Silverpine Forest and answers to Undercity's leadership.",al={"hadrec","who is hadrec","sepulcher commander"},it="identity"},{q="Why does Apothecary Renferrel send you to Hadrec?",a="Apothecary Renferrel sends you to Hadrec because he and Bethor Iceshard found that Thule Ravenclaw has gathered a dangerous Scourge force on Fenris Isle. An entrenched necromancer calls for military strength and proper equipment, so Renferrel turns to the garrison's commander.",al={"why report to hadrec","renferrel hadrec connection"},it="motive"},{q="Where is the Sepulcher located?",a="The Sepulcher is a fortified Forsaken settlement and tomb complex in central Silverpine Forest. It is the Horde's main hub and staging ground for operations in the region.",al={"where is sepulcher","sepulcher location"},it="place",gp=true},{q="Who is Thule Ravenclaw?",a="Thule Ravenclaw is a powerful Scourge necromancer who seized Fenris Keep on Fenris Isle in Lake Lordamere. He raises the dead to build an active beachhead off Silverpine's eastern shore.",al={"thule ravenclaw","thule lore"},it="target"},{q="What happens after reporting to Hadrec?",a="Hadrec gives you supplies from the Sepulcher's armory and orders an immediate strike on Fenris Isle. The attack aims to eliminate Thule Ravenclaw and break the Scourge hold on Lake Lordamere.",al={"what next after hadrec","next quest hadrec"},it="next_step"},{q="Who is Bethor mentioned by Hadrec?",a="Bethor Iceshard is a Forsaken mage who lives in the Undercity's Magic Quarter. His magical divinations helped uncover the nature and danger of Thule Ravenclaw's rituals.",al={"who is bethor","bethor iceshard"}}},ang={["faction:Horde"]="The Sepulcher coordinates the Horde's western defense in Lordaeron. It guards the approaches to the ruins of the Capital City against Scourge outposts and human survivors.",["race:Undead"]="As Forsaken, you face Thule Ravenclaw as the Lich King's enslaving will pressing close to home. Destroying him is vital to your people's survival."},kw={"fenris","hadrec","iceshard","ravenclaw","renferrel","sepulcher","silverpine","thule"},rel={"npc:high-executor-hadrec","quest:442","quest:446","npc:apothecary-renferrel","subzone:sepulcher","subzone:fenris-isle","zone:silverpine"},m={start="Apothecary Renferrel",["end"]="High Executor Hadrec",level="16",faction="Horde",id=448},src={"Report to Hadrec"}}
E["quest:449"] = {t="quest",n="The Deathstalkers' Report",z="silverpine",s="Near the northern wilds, the Deathstalkers have found Scourge forces where the Forsaken did not expect them. You carry their report from the wounded scouts to High Executor Hadrec at the Sepulcher, bringing word that Silverpine Forest holds a greater threat than command believed.",h="Near the northern wilds, the Deathstalkers have found Scourge forces where the Forsaken did not expect them.",sec={{t="Frontline Intelligence",b="The Deathstalkers scout ahead for the Dark Lady, slipping into wild country before the main forces. Near the border of Tirisfal and Silverpine, one patrol met fierce resistance while tracking enemy movements.\n\nDeathstalker Quinn barely survived his wounds, while Erland fought his way to safety. Their patrol still gathered intelligence the Forsaken need to hold Silverpine Forest.",sp=0},{t="The Scourge Factor",b="High Executor Hadrec reads the sealed report and learns that the Scourge hold a stronger presence in Silverpine than Undercity strategists expected. Their forces are more active and aggressive than command believed.\n\nThe Forsaken had planned to secure abandoned human hamlets and drive off rogue beasts. Now the Sepulcher's command must prepare for organized Scourge opposition as it fights to claim the region.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What is the Deathstalker Report?",a="Deathstalker Rane Yorick wrote the field report for her wounded scouting cell. It records the threats they saw, including unexpected Scourge activity in northern Silverpine Forest, and brings that intelligence to the regional commander at the Sepulcher.",al={"deathstalker report","what is the report","what did yorick give me"},it="item"},{q="Who is High Executor Hadrec?",a="High Executor Hadrec commands Forsaken operations in Silverpine Forest. From the Sepulcher, he coordinates scouts, defenses, and the campaign against the Scourge and hostile humans in the region.",al={"hadrec","high executor hadrec","sepulcher commander"},it="identity"},{q="Why was the report's information a surprise to Hadrec?",a="The Forsaken leadership believed the Scourge in Silverpine was scattered and few in number beside the fighting in Tirisfal Glades and the Plaguelands. The Deathstalkers' losses and discoveries show that the Lich King's minions remain entrenched and dangerous this far south.",al={"why surprised","hadrec reaction","scourge in silverpine"},it="purpose"},{q="Who are the Deathstalkers?",a="The Deathstalkers are an elite Forsaken order of assassins, spies, and forward scouts under Lady Sylvanas Windrunner's command. They range through contested lands to find threats before the regular army advances.",al={"deathstalkers","deathstalker lore","forsaken rogues"},it="people"},{q="Where is the Sepulcher located?",a="The Sepulcher lies in central Silverpine Forest, just west of the main north-south road. It is a crypt and base camp for Forsaken forces across the province.",al={"where is sepulcher","sepulcher location"},it="place",gp=true},{q="What happens after Hadrec reads the report?",a="After reading the report, Hadrec sends you to consult specialists at the Sepulcher, beginning with Apothecary Renferrel. They will help develop ways to counter the threats in Silverpine.",al={"next quest","what now","after hadrec"},it="next_step"},{q="Why does Rane Yorick need the report delivered so quickly?",a="Rane Yorick and her companions uncovered vital intelligence regarding Scourge activity and hostile threats in the wilds of Silverpine Forest. Because this information directly impacts the Forsaken's ability to secure and hold the region, High Executor Hadrec at the Sepulcher must receive it immediately so military command can respond.",al={"why does rane yorick want this done","rane yorick motivation","why send the deathstalker report"},it="motive",add="df12075a"},{q="Why does Rane Yorick ask you to deliver the report instead of doing it herself?",a="Rane's scouting party is in no condition to travel. Her brother and fellow Deathstalker, Quinn, was severely wounded during their mission and is still slowly mending under Rane's care. With their unit immobilized and the report too urgent to delay, Rane must rely on an able-bodied traveler like you to carry the dispatch to the Sepulcher.",al={"why me rane yorick","why can't rane deliver it","why do i carry the report"},it="why_me",add="de251098"}},ang={["race:Undead"]="As an Undead, you bring intelligence that supports the Undercity's expansion. It proves your reliability to High Executor Hadrec and the Deathstalker network.",["class:Rogue"]="As a Rogue, you carry vital dispatches for the Forsaken's leading spies. Your work aligns you with the Dark Lady's shadow operatives.",["faction:Horde"]="As a member of the Horde, you help the Forsaken secure Silverpine against the Scourge. Their hold there strengthens the Horde's foothold across northern Lordaeron."},kw={"deathstalker","erland","hadrec","quinn","rane yorick","report","scourge","sepulcher","silverpine","undercity"},rel={"quest:435","npc:high-executor-hadrec","subzone:sepulcher","quest:3221","quest:1886","zone:silverpine","topic:scourge","topic:forsaken"},m={start="Rane Yorick",["end"]="High Executor Hadrec",level="11",faction="Horde",id=449},src={"The Deathstalkers' Report"}}
E["quest:452"] = {t="quest",n="Pyrewood Ambush",z="silverpine",s="Deathstalker Faerleia waits in Pyrewood Village, where Arugal's council keeps the afflicted in line. The Forsaken aim to break his hold on the town and weaken his position in Shadowfang Keep.",h="Deathstalker Faerleia waits in Pyrewood Village, where Arugal's council keeps the afflicted in line.",sec={{t="Striking the Puppets",b="Deathstalker Faerleia waits inside Pyrewood Village's town hall for the local leaders. Archmage Arugal keeps to Shadowfang Keep, tending his dark sorceries, and leaves the Pyrewood Council to maintain order among the afflicted villagers. Faerleia plans to strike the council in an ambush. Without its mediation, the Forsaken hope the worgen in the surrounding woods and village streets will break free of Arugal's control.",sp=0},{t="A Decapitation Strike",b="The ambush strikes every sitting member of Pyrewood's government, including Lord Mayor Morrison. The councilors are killed as they enter their meeting chamber, dealing a blow to the village's leadership. For the Undercity, the slaughter clears a path to taking Pyrewood Village and laying siege to Arugal in Shadowfang Keep.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Who is Deathstalker Faerleia?",a="Deathstalker Faerleia is a Forsaken operative of the Deathstalkers, the Forsaken's espionage and assassination guild. She established a foothold inside Pyrewood Village to coordinate strikes against Arugal's local support.",al={"faerleia","deathstalker faerleia","who gives pyrewood ambush"},it="identity"},{q="Why does the Forsaken want the Pyrewood Council dead?",a="Arugal relies on the council to keep the cursed human villagers compliant and under control. The Forsaken believe killing its leaders will throw Pyrewood into chaos and turn the worgen against Arugal.",al={"why kill pyrewood council","pyrewood council purpose","pyrewood council lore"},it="motive"},{q="Who leads the Pyrewood Council?",a="Lord Mayor Morrison leads the Pyrewood Council. Before the Deathstalkers' ambush, he oversees municipal matters with councilmen Smithers, Thatcher, and Brunswick.",al={"lord mayor morrison","pyrewood mayor","who runs pyrewood"},it="leader"},{q="Where does this ambush take place?",a="The ambush takes place inside Pyrewood Village's municipal town hall, in southern Silverpine Forest, just down the road from Shadowfang Keep.",al={"pyrewood ambush location","where is faerleia","town hall pyrewood"},it="place"},{q="What is the relationship between the Council and Arugal?",a="The council is Arugal's administrative mouthpiece. While he remains in Shadowfang Keep conducting dark experiments, the council manages villagers who transform into ferocious beasts under cover of night.",al={"arugal council","is council working for arugal","arugal control pyrewood"},it="ties"},{q="Does killing the council free Pyrewood from the curse?",a="No. Killing the council removes Arugal's mortal puppets but does not lift the villagers' lupine curse. The Forsaken are left to contend with a town full of hostile, uncontrolled monsters.",al={"is pyrewood cured","does ambush cure worgen","curse broken pyrewood"},sp=1,it="threat"},{q="Who are you fighting in the Pyrewood ambush?",a="You are fighting the Pyrewood Council, led by Lord Mayor Morrison alongside councilmen like Smithers, Thatcher, and Brunswick. They govern Pyrewood Village under the influence of Archmage Arugal, acting as his puppet administrators to keep the cursed, mind-addled townsfolk obedient while Arugal conducts his dark affairs inside Shadowfang Keep.",al={"pyrewood council members","who is the target pyrewood ambush","who do you fight pyrewood ambush"},it="target",add="fc270bec"},{q="Why does Deathstalker Faerleia need your help?",a="Deathstalker Faerleia is working deep behind enemy lines in hostile territory. The Council returns in waves, bringing multiple seasoned members including Lord Mayor Morrison. As skilled as Faerleia is as an assassin for the Dark Lady, she cannot take on the entire council at once without being overwhelmed, making your arrival vital to the ambush's success.",al={"why does faerleia need help","why me pyrewood ambush","why can't faerleia do it alone"},it="why_me",add="abb7a8b1"}},ang={["race:Undead"]="For the Forsaken, securing southern Silverpine helps defend the Undercity's borders. Killing Arugal's sycophants brings them closer to claiming Pyrewood.",["class:Rogue"]="As a rogue, you know the Deathstalkers' craft: infiltrate enemy strongholds, lie in wait, and eliminate commanders in their own seat of power.",["faction:Horde"]="As a member of the Horde, you weaken Arugal's network and the threat to the Horde's route through Silverpine Forest toward the southern borders."},kw={"arugal","deathstalker faerleia","faerleia","lord mayor morrison","pyrewood ambush","pyrewood council","shadowfang keep","silverpine forest"},rel={"npc:deathstalker-faerleia","npc:arugal","zone:shadowfang","zone:silverpine"},m={start="Deathstalker Faerleia",level="15",faction="Horde",id=452},src={"Pyrewood Ambush"}}
E["quest:460"] = {t="quest",n="Resting in Pieces",z="silverpine",s="On Fenris Isle, Resting in Pieces begins with Alaric's animated, severed head. He asks to be carried across Fenris Keep to an unmarked grave near the stables, where the rest of his remains lie.",h="On Fenris Isle, Resting in Pieces begins with Alaric's animated, severed head.",sec={{t="A Bodyguard Betrayed",b="Alaric once served as Thule Ravenclaw's chief servant and personal bodyguard at Fenris Keep in Silverpine Forest. Thule was a powerful mage aligned with the Scourge. When the Plague of Undeath swept through the region, he promised his sorcery would shield Alaric from it. Instead, the ward trapped Alaric in endless agony and undeath, with his awareness intact in his severed parts.",sp=0},{t="Plaything of the Rot Hides",b="Thule created the rot hide gnolls by infecting local packs with necromantic decay, then turned against his own bodyguard. He cut off Alaric's head and threw it to the savage gnolls as a diversion. The rot hides dragged Alaric's body to a shallow, hastily dug grave outside the keep's stables. They kept his speaking head as a grim plaything until an outsider intervened.",sp=0},{t="Reuniting the Pieces",b="The hastily dug grave near the stables holds Alaric's headless torso. When his severed head is brought there, his remains are reunited. Thule's curse still binds Alaric to undeath, but having his parts restored brings him a bitter measure of relief.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Who is Alaric?",a="Alaric served as Thule Ravenclaw's chief servant and personal bodyguard at Fenris Keep. Thule's spell, supposedly meant to shield him from the Plague of Undeath, instead bound him to eternal unlife.",al={"alaric","who is the talking head","talking head silverpine"},it="identity"},{q="Why was Alaric beheaded?",a="Thule Ravenclaw beheaded Alaric after completing his experiments to create the rot hide gnolls. He threw Alaric's severed, conscious head to the gnolls as a plaything.",al={"why is alaric a head","who cut off alarics head"},it="history"},{q="Where is Alaric's grave located?",a="Alaric's body lies in an unmarked, shallow grave dug in haste on Fenris Isle, in Fenris Keep's courtyard near the stable buildings.",al={"where is alarics body","shallow grave location","where is the grave fenris"},it="place",gp=true},{q="What are the rot hide gnolls?",a="The rot hide gnolls are Fenris Isle's local gnoll packs, transformed into rotting horrors touched by undeath through Thule Ravenclaw's necromantic experiments.",al={"rot hides","rot hide gnolls","fenris isle gnolls"},it="threat"},{q="Who is Thule Ravenclaw?",a="Thule Ravenclaw is a human wizard and Scourge necromancer who seized Fenris Keep in the middle of Lake Lordamere. He uses it as a laboratory to corrupt the gnolls and spread the Scourge's influence.",al={"thule","thule ravenclaw"},it="people"},{q="What happens after you find the grave?",a="After his remains are reunited, Alaric helps you find a hidden niche containing a powerful wand. You can return it to Dalaran's Magus Bethor Iceshard in the Undercity.",al={"what next resting in pieces","resting in pieces followup"},sp=1,it="next_step"},{q="Why does Alaric want his head brought to his grave?",a="Alaric is trapped in an agonizing unlife created by Thule Ravenclaw's warped protective spell. After being decapitated and tossed to the rot hide gnolls as a gruesome plaything, he fears his headless corpse was desecrated or obliterated. He wants to be returned to his makeshift grave on Fenris Isle to reunite with his remains and end his humiliating ordeal.",al={"why does the talking head need help","alaric motive","why take alaric to his grave"},it="motive",add="5dad63cd"},{q="Why does Alaric need your help to reach his grave?",a="Alaric is merely a severed, animated head. Unable to move on his own, he was left entirely helpless while being kicked around as a toy by the rot hide gnolls occupying Fenris Keep. You are the first non-gnoll he has encountered who can physically carry him past the creatures and bury him properly.",al={"why does alaric need you","why can't alaric do it himself","talking head why me"},it="why_me",add="c2c834f2"}},ang={["race:Undead"]="As a Forsaken champion, you will recognize Thule Ravenclaw's treacherous spellcasting as one of the cruel horrors Scourge-aligned sorcerers inflict across Lordaeron.",["class:Mage"]="As a mage, you can see how Thule twisted a defensive ward into an inescapable curse of severed undeath. His spell shows the harm arcane magic can suffer when necromancy corrupts it."},kw={"alaric","fenris isle","fenris keep","rot hide","shallow grave","silverpine","talking head","thule ravenclaw"},rel={"quest:461","quest:491","subzone:fenris-keep","subzone:fenris-isle","topic:gnoll","topic:plague-of-undeath","zone:silverpine","zone:tirisfal"},m={start="A Talking Head",["end"]="Shallow Grave",level="17",faction="Horde",id=460},src={"Resting in Pieces"}}
E["quest:461"] = {t="quest",n="The Hidden Niche",z="silverpine",s="Alaric's memories lead you back into Fenris Keep. His remains point toward a forgotten alcove where he seeks rest and an old relic waits.",h="Alaric's memories lead you back into Fenris Keep.",sec={{t="A Restless Request",b="Alaric remembers Fenris Keep in its better days. Horde scouts have lifted his bones from a shallow grave outside the stronghold, but he will not go quietly to the Sepulcher. He offers vital knowledge instead: a hidden niche in the keep's southwestern tower holds an item treasured by Thule Ravenclaw and his fellow mages.",sp=0},{t="Buried in the Walls",b="You carry Alaric's remains through Fenris Keep, past the Rot Hide gnolls that infest the island fortress. In the upper levels, a dusty bookshelf hides the compartment he described. Alaric asks to be sealed inside the keep's ancient masonry, where he spent the happiest days of his life, beyond the gnolls' reach.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Who is Alaric?",a="Alaric served Thule Ravenclaw as head servant and bodyguard at Fenris Keep. Thule beheaded him after creating the Rot Hide gnolls. Found in a shallow grave outside the fortress, Alaric's animated spirit guides Horde travelers in exchange for a proper resting place inside his beloved stronghold.",al={"alaric lore","who is alaric","whose bones are these"},it="identity"},{q="Where is the hidden niche located?",a="The hidden niche lies behind a dusty bookshelf on an upper floor of Fenris Keep's southwestern tower.",al={"where is dusty shelf","where is the niche","hidden niche location"},it="place",gp=true},{q="What item is hidden in the alcove?",a="The alcove holds an old wand treasured by Thule Ravenclaw and his former peers from Dalaran, along with other remnants Alaric leaves for those who helped him.",al={"what is in the niche","fenris keep treasure","thule item"},it="item"},{q="Why does Alaric want to stay inside Fenris Keep?",a="Alaric remembers his years in Fenris Keep as the happiest of his life. Resting inside its stonework brings him peace and protects his remains from the scavenger gnolls in the courtyards.",al={"why leave alaric in fenris","alaric resting place"},it="motive"},{q="What happens after finding the shelf?",a="After Alaric is sealed in the niche and you retrieve the wand, you return to the Undercity to deliver it to Bethor Iceshard.",al={"quest after hidden niche","what do i do with the wand"},sp=1,it="next_step",gp=true},{q="Why did Alaric tell you to leave his boots behind?",a="When his bones were lifted from the shallow grave, Alaric joked that his old boots never fit properly and insisted they stay in the dirt.",al={"alaric boots","leave boots behind"}},{q="Why does Alaric need you to carry his remains to the niche?",a="Alaric is nothing more than a dismembered corpse buried in a shallow grave on Fenris Isle. Having been slain and dismembered, he has no physical power to move himself back into the fortress he once called home. He relies entirely on you to exhume his scattered remains, carry him through the hostile Gnoll-infested keep, and deposit him in the secret alcove.",al={"why does alaric need help","why me alaric","why carry alaric remains"},it="why_me",add="8d31ac84"}},ang={["race:Undead"]="As a Forsaken, you know the business of speaking remains, but Alaric's wish for rest in human ruins recalls the lands your people inherited.",["class:Mage"]="The hidden alcove preserves Fenris Keep's arcane heritage, with artifacts tied to former Dalaran wizards such as Thule Ravenclaw.",["faction:Horde"]="As Horde, you recover relics from the heart of Fenris Keep, weakening Thule's foothold on Fenris Isle and aiding the Forsaken campaign to secure Silverpine Forest."},kw={"alaric","dusty shelf","fenris keep","hidden niche","rot hide","silverpine forest","thule ravenclaw"},rel={"quest:460","quest:491","zone:silverpine"},m={start="Shallow Grave",["end"]="Dusty Shelf",level="18",faction="Horde",id=461},src={"The Hidden Niche"}}
E["quest:477"] = {t="quest",n="Border Crossings",z="silverpine",s="At the Sepulcher, Shadow Priest Allister sends you to intercept Dalaran's supplies and learn why the Kirin Tor support Ambermill. The crates travel through Silverpine Forest toward a Dalaran camp near Pyrewood Village.",h="At the Sepulcher, Shadow Priest Allister sends you to intercept Dalaran's supplies and learn why the Kirin...",sec={{t="Supplies on the Frontier",b="Dalaran magi send wagons of supplies and arcane goods from the Hillsbrad Foothills through Silverpine Forest. Their shipments support outposts and staging grounds along the way. A camp just north of Pyrewood Village holds Dalaran personnel who watch the road. The human resistance at Ambermill is the main surviving stronghold in eastern Silverpine, and Dalaran has not left it to fend for itself.",sp=0},{t="The Forsaken's Suspicion",b="Shadow Priest Allister and the Forsaken leaders at the Sepulcher want to know why Dalaran commits so much to Ambermill. They suspect the Kirin Tor would not risk lives and supplies deep in Forsaken territory merely for a provincial town. A greater strategic or magical purpose may lie behind that support. Intercepting the crates can show the Forsaken what Dalaran is sending west.",sp=0},{t="Uncovering the Cargo",b="The crate Allister asks you to retrieve holds more than provisions. Inside are aged maps of Silverpine Forest and western Lordaeron, along with a magical pendant. The cargo includes arcane items and maps, but its purpose remains unclear.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Why are Dalaran wizards active in Silverpine Forest?",a="Dalaran works from Ambermill to maintain a human and Alliance presence in western Lordaeron. Shadow Priest Allister suspects the Kirin Tor have a deeper purpose than defending a rural hamlet, so the Forsaken target their supply lines.",al={"why is dalaran here","dalaran silverpine","why dalaran at ambermill"},it="why_here"},{q="Where are the Dalaran crates located?",a="The crates are at a Dalaran camp just north of Pyrewood Village, off the main road. Dalaran magi and guards keep watch there.",al={"crate location","where are the crates","pyrewood camp"},it="place",gp=true},{q="What is inside the Dalaran crate?",a="Allister does not know what Dalaran is shipping. He asks you to bring back the contents of a crate from the camp north of Pyrewood Village so he can investigate.",al={"crate contents","what is in the box"},sp=1,it="item"},{q="Who is Shadow Priest Allister?",a="Shadow Priest Allister is a prominent Forsaken leader at the Sepulcher in Silverpine Forest. He directs intelligence efforts and strikes against human holdouts and Dalaran's incursions.",al={"shadow priest allister","who gives border crossings"},it="identity"},{q="How are the supplies getting into Silverpine Forest?",a="Wagons carry the shipments from Dalaran's territory in the Hillsbrad Foothills through the border pass into Silverpine. They then reach staging camps near Ambermill and Pyrewood.",al={"dalaran supply route","hillsbrad wagons"},it="history"},{q="What follows the completion of this quest?",a="After inspecting the crate, take what you discover to Shadow Priest Allister for study in Maps and Runes.",al={"what next","follow up quest","next quest"},sp=1,it="next_step"},{q="Why does Shadow Priest Allister want this done?",a="Ambermill stands as a stubborn pocket of living human resistance in Silverpine Forest, fortified and sustained almost entirely by Dalaran's arcane backing. Shadow Priest Allister suspects the mages have a deeper, hidden agenda for investing heavily in such a backwater town. By intercepting the wagon shipments pouring into their outpost north of Pyrewood, the Forsaken hope to uncover Dalaran's true motives and eliminate a growing Alliance foothold right on the Undercity's doorstep.",al={"why does allister want the crate","shadow priest allister motive","why steal dalaran supplies"},it="motive",add="3c89d6a1"}},ang={["race:Undead"]="As an Undead, you know the Forsaken cannot tolerate an unchecked Dalaran outpost on their southern flank, especially one sending supplies under the Sepulcher's nose.",["class:Priest"]="As a Forsaken priest, you help secure the domain of the Forsaken priesthood under Shadow Priest Allister against holy and arcane rivals.",["class:Mage"]="As a Horde spellcaster, you share an interest in Dalaran's magical shipments and what they may reveal about the Kirin Tor's secrets and protective wards in Lordaeron."},kw={"ambermill","border crossings","dalaran crate","hillsbrad","pyrewood village","sepulcher","shadow priest allister","silverpine forest"},rel={"quest:478","npc:shadow-priest-allister","subzone:ambermill","subzone:pyrewood-village","subzone:dalaran","zone:silverpine","topic:lordaeron"},m={start="Shadow Priest Allister",["end"]="Dalaran Crate",level="14",faction="Horde",id=477},src={"Border Crossings"}}
E["quest:478"] = {t="quest",n="Maps and Runes",z="silverpine",s="In Silverpine Forest, maps and runes point to Dalaran's interest in Ambermill. A hidden crate holds regional charts and a rune-inscribed pendant, which adventurers recover for Shadow Priest Allister at the Sepulcher.",h="In Silverpine Forest, maps and runes point to Dalaran's interest in Ambermill.",sec={{t="A Hidden Cargo",b="Horde agents find a Dalaran crate hidden along the border routes near Ambermill. Inside are detailed regional charts and an enigmatic pendant inscribed with runes. With human sentries nearby, the scouts retrieve the artifact carefully, wary of Dalaran's arcane reach so close to their borders.",sp=0},{t="Whispers at the Sepulcher",b="At the Sepulcher, Shadow Priest Allister receives the recovered pendant. The Forsaken leadership sees that the Kirin Tor are working in Ambermill, though the purpose remains unclear. Allister cannot decipher the potent sorcery woven into the runes, so he seeks arcane experts among the undead to uncover Dalaran's plot.",sp=1}},faq={{q="What is inside the Dalaran crate?",a="The Dalaran crate contains detailed regional charts and a strange rune-inscribed pendant. The items suggest Dalaran is planning around Ambermill.",al={"what was in the crate","crate contents","dalaran crate loot"},it="item"},{q="Who is Shadow Priest Allister?",a="Shadow Priest Allister is a prominent Forsaken authority stationed at the Sepulcher. He oversees local intelligence gathering and coordinates defenses against hostile human remnants and Kirin Tor operatives in Silverpine Forest.",al={"who is allister","shadow priest allister lore"},it="identity"},{q="Why are the Forsaken concerned about Dalaran in Ambermill?",a="The Forsaken fear Dalaran's presence in Ambermill, on the border of Lordaeron lands they claim. Arcane relics or secretive troop movements could threaten the Undercity's hold over Silverpine.",al={"why ambermill matters","forsaken dalaran conflict"},it="threat"},{q="Can Shadow Priest Allister decipher the pendant?",a="No. Allister recognizes the pendant as Dalaran sorcery, but its enchantments elude his priestly craft, so he seeks deeper arcane knowledge.",al={"does allister know the runes","can allister read the pendant"}},{q="Where does this investigation lead next?",a="The investigation continues with Dalar's Analysis. The pendant goes to Dalar Dawnweaver, an arcane specialist at the Sepulcher capable of breaking down Kirin Tor magic.",al={"what is the next quest","after maps and runes"},it="next_step"},{q="What quest leads up to Maps and Runes?",a="Border Crossings leads into Maps and Runes. In Border Crossings, the Forsaken assign an operative to inspect suspicious trade crates moving into Silverpine from the borders of Dalaran.",al={"prerequisite quest","maps and runes prereq"},it="origin",gp=true}},ang={["race:Undead"]="As an Undead, you know Dalaran's surviving wizards keep outposts close to Undercity territory. Recovering their enchanted talismans helps safeguard Forsaken sovereignty in Silverpine.",["class:Mage"]="As a Mage, you know the rune-inscribed pendant bears patterns of Kirin Tor enchantment, shaped by Dalaran's tradition of shielding and arcane warding.",["class:Priest"]="As a Priest, you know that even Shadow Priest Allister's formidable shadow magic cannot unravel the intricate arcane formulas carved into the pendant.",["faction:Horde"]="As a member of the Horde, you know securing Silverpine Forest from Alliance-aligned forces like the Kirin Tor protects a vital supply corridor across northern Lordaeron."},kw={"ambermill","dalaran crate","kirin tor","maps and runes","rune-inscribed pendant","shadow priest allister","silverpine forest","the sepulcher"},rel={"quest:477","quest:481","npc:shadow-priest-allister","subzone:sepulcher","subzone:ambermill","subzone:dalaran","zone:silverpine"},m={start="Dalaran Crate",["end"]="Shadow Priest Allister",level="14",faction="Horde",id=478},src={"Maps and Runes"}}
E["quest:479"] = {t="quest",n="Ambermill Investigations",z="silverpine",s="In Ambermill, Dalaran wizards are weaving magic that threatens the Forsaken's hold on Silverpine Forest. Shadow Priest Allister sends agents from the Sepulcher to disrupt their spellwork and seize the magical foci.",h="In Ambermill, Dalaran wizards are weaving magic that threatens the Forsaken's hold on Silverpine Forest.",sec={{t="A Threat from the East",b="Ambermill is a human town in the hills of eastern Silverpine Forest, held by wizards and defenders pledged to the Kirin Tor of Dalaran. The mages are weaving magical energies in a vast ritual. At the Sepulcher, Shadow Priest Allister and his companion Dalar recognize the danger. If the Kirin Tor channel their power unchecked, the Forsaken risk being driven from Silverpine entirely.",sp=0},{t="Disrupting the Weave",b="While Dalar scries the forest and traces the flow of magic, Allister sends agents to strike the practitioners in Ambermill. Dalaran conjurers, mages, and their protectors wear enchanted pendants that focus and coordinate their arts. Taking the talismans from slain sorcerers disrupts the ritual and gives the Sepulcher time to find the ringleader directing the arcane weave.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Why is Shadow Priest Allister targeting Ambermill?",a="The Kirin Tor mages in Ambermill are channeling powerful arcane energies. Allister fears their spellcasting could cost the Forsaken control of Silverpine Forest.",al={"why attack ambermill","allister motive","ambermill threat"},it="motive"},{q="What are the Dalaran Pendants used for?",a="Dalaran conjurers, mages, and protectors wear the pendants as focuses for their craft. Taking them weakens the wizards' efforts and helps Allister study the Kirin Tor's magical progress.",al={"what are dalaran pendants","pendant purpose","why collect pendants"},it="item"},{q="Where is Ambermill located?",a="Ambermill lies in the eastern hills of Silverpine Forest. From the Sepulcher, head south along the main thoroughfare, then follow the fork east into town.",al={"ambermill location","how to get to ambermill","where is ambermill"},it="place",gp=true},{q="Who is Dalar, and how is he involved?",a="Dalar is a Forsaken practitioner at the Sepulcher with Shadow Priest Allister. He tracks and seeks to uncover the magical sources fueling the Dalaran wizards in Ambermill.",al={"who is dalar","dalar role","dalar silverpine"},it="people"},{q="What happens after recovering the pendants?",a="The pendants show that the Dalaran ritual is already well advanced, led by an adept wizard. That wizard must be confronted to halt the spellcasting entirely.",al={"what happens next","ambermill investigations follow up","after dalaran pendants"},sp=1,it="next_step"},{q="Why are Dalaran humans still in Silverpine Forest?",a="Before the Third War, Ambermill was a minor lumber town. After their kingdom was devastated, the surviving Kirin Tor took an interest in the town and still hold it against the Scourge and Forsaken.",al={"why are dalaran humans here","kirin tor in silverpine","ambermill lore"},it="why_here"},{q="Who are you sent against in Ambermill?",a="Shadow Priest Allister sends you directly against the human forces holding the fortified town of Ambermill: Dalaran conjurers, mages, and their protectors. While Dalaran itself lies further east, these wizards and guards maintain a stronghold here in Silverpine, actively channeling dangerous magic that threatens Forsaken control over the forest.",al={"who are the targets","ambermill enemies","who do i fight in ambermill"},it="target",add="fc82e396"}},ang={["race:Undead"]="The Kirin Tor remnants in Ambermill are near the Undercity's territory. Their magical work threatens Forsaken survival.",["class:Mage"]="As a mage, you know the precise coordination a large arcane ritual demands. Severing the Kirin Tor's enchanted foci disrupts their spellcraft.",["faction:Horde"]="As a member of the Horde, you know holding Silverpine Forest protects Lordaeron's western approaches from Alliance-aligned outposts loyal to Dalaran."},kw={"allister","ambermill","dalar","dalaran","kirin tor","pendant","sepulcher","silverpine"},rel={"npc:shadow-priest-allister","quest:482","subzone:ambermill","subzone:sepulcher","subzone:dalaran","zone:silverpine"},m={start="Shadow Priest Allister",level="16",faction="Horde",id=479,ri={"Dalaran Pendant"}},src={"Ambermill Investigations"}}
E["quest:480"] = {t="quest",n="The Weaver",z="silverpine",s="In Silverpine Forest, Ataeric works to awaken a dormant ley energy node for Dalaran. Shadow Priest Allister at the Sepulcher sends you to stop the archmage and take his staff, keeping Dalaran’s magic from threatening Forsaken control of the southern reaches of Lordaeron.",h="In Silverpine Forest, Ataeric works to awaken a dormant ley energy node for Dalaran.",sec={{t="Severing the Ley Thread",b="After earlier inquiries into Ambermill and Dalaran’s movements, the Forsaken learned that the wizards are trying to awaken a dormant ley energy node in Silverpine Forest. If Dalaran gains its concentrated arcane power, it could strengthen its position and threaten the Undercity’s hold over southern Lordaeron.",sp=0},{t="The Archmage's Fall",b="Shadow Priest Allister knows the operation must be stopped at its source. Archmage Ataeric directs the work, protected by wards and fellow magi. Slaying him and claiming his staff scatters the gathered magic, returns the ley energies to dormancy, and thwarts the Kirin Tor’s plans in the valley.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Who is the Weaver?",a="The Weaver is Archmage Ataeric, a powerful Dalaran spellcaster in Silverpine Forest. He is trying to weave together and awaken the latent ley energies beneath the area.",al={"who is the weaver","archmage ataeric","ataeric weaver"},it="target"},{q="Why do the Forsaken want the archmage killed?",a="The Forsaken fear that Dalaran will draw vast arcane power from the dormant ley energy node, close to the Undercity. Shadow Priest Allister sees that as a threat to Forsaken sovereignty and orders Ataeric killed before the node is fully active.",al={"why kill ataeric","forsaken dalaran conflict","why attack dalaran"},it="motive"},{q="What happens after Ataeric is defeated?",a="With Ataeric slain and his staff taken, the arcane network collapses. The gathered spells dissipate and the ley line returns to dormancy, depriving the Kirin Tor of its main foothold of arcane power in southern Silverpine.",al={"after the weaver","quest outcome","what happens to ley node"},sp=1,it="next_step"},{q="Who sends you on this quest?",a="Shadow Priest Allister, a Forsaken authority at the Sepulcher in Silverpine Forest, gives you the order after examining earlier intelligence about Dalaran’s presence around Ambermill.",al={"who gives the weaver","allister quest","quest giver weaver"},it="identity"},{q="What is the significance of Ataeric's staff?",a="Archmage Ataeric’s staff focuses and channels the regional ley energies. Taking it ensures the magic unravels completely and gives Allister an artifact he might study for the Forsaken’s own designs.",al={"ataerics staff","archmage staff purpose","why take the staff"},it="item"},{q="Where does Dalaran's presence in Silverpine come from?",a="Though Dalaran was devastated during the Third War, remnants of the Kirin Tor keep fortified enclaves, outposts, and arcane experiments in nearby territories such as Ambermill. They seek to regain control and harness vital magical reserves.",al={"dalaran in silverpine","why are dalaran mages in silverpine","ambermill dalaran"},it="place"}},ang={["race:Undead"]="As an Undead, you face Dalaran’s living magi, who dispute Forsaken control over the ruins of Lordaeron. Stopping their archmage helps secure the Sepulcher’s perimeter.",["class:Mage"]="As a Mage, you know ley lines demand deep mastery of arcane geometry. Ataeric’s fall shows how delicate such rituals become when their main conduits are lost.",["class:Priest"]="As a Priest, you see Shadow Priest Allister direct this operation through cold resolve, aiming to extinguish an arcane catalyst before it grows in power.",["faction:Horde"]="As a member of the Horde, you face Dalaran’s hostile remnants. Any growth in their arcane strength threatens Horde lands in northern Lordaeron."},kw={"allister","ambermill","ataeric","dalaran","kirin tor","ley energy","sepulcher","silverpine","weaver"},rel={"npc:shadow-priest-allister","quest:479","subzone:sepulcher","zone:silverpine","subzone:dalaran"},m={start="Shadow Priest Allister",level="22",faction="Horde",id=480,ri={"Ataeric's Staff"}},src={"The Weaver (quest)"}}
E["quest:481"] = {t="quest",n="Dalar's Analysis",z="silverpine",s="In Silverpine, Allister's report sends a Dalaran relic to Dalar for study. A rune-inscribed pendant taken from a supply crate reaches Dalar Dawnweaver at the Sepulcher. The relic shows that Dalaran's surviving mages are gathering great magical power for a hidden purpose.",h="In Silverpine, Allister's report sends a Dalaran relic to Dalar for study.",sec={{t="A Courier's Cargo",b="A supply crate from Dalaran is raided at a camp north of Pyrewood Village. Beneath old maps, Shadow Priest Allister finds a rune-inscribed pendant. Its enchantment is beyond his spiritual knowledge, so he sends it to Dalar Dawnweaver at the Sepulcher. Dalar's skill as an arcane scholar makes him better suited to read Dalaran's magical warding.",sp=0},{t="Kirin Tor Machinations",b="Dalar Dawnweaver finds the pendant is a specialized conduit once favored by high-ranking Kirin Tor wizards. It lets them channel potent magic. Many such relics are being sent straight to fortified Ambermill, a sign that the wizards are preparing an undertaking on a vast scale. Dalar probes their wards to learn their intentions.",sp=1}},faq={{q="What is the rune-inscribed pendant?",a="The pendant is an arcane conduit that senior Kirin Tor mages use to channel large amounts of magical energy safely. Found in transit, it suggests Ambermill is receiving powerful foci for high-level spellcraft.",al={"what is pendant","kirin tor pendant lore","ambermill pendant"},it="item"},{q="Why does Shadow Priest Allister send the pendant to Dalar Dawnweaver?",a="Shadow Priest Allister handles shadow magic and gathers intelligence for the Forsaken at the Sepulcher. Since the pendant is a complex arcane relic made in Dalaran, he sends it to Dalar Dawnweaver to inspect its runes and determine its purpose.",al={"why dalar","who is dalar dawnweaver","why send to sepulcher"},it="motive"},{q="Where is Ambermill and why are the Forsaken monitoring it?",a="Ambermill is a fortified human town in southeastern Silverpine Forest, maintained by Dalaran's mages. Deep in territory claimed by Lady Sylvanas Windrunner, it poses a military and magical threat to the Forsaken, who keep close watch on its borders.",al={"why watch ambermill","ambermill wizards","dalaran in silverpine"},it="place"},{q="What happens after Dalar analyzes the pendant?",a="Dalar recognizes that the Kirin Tor are gathering conduits for a major undertaking. In Dalaran's Intentions, the following task, he uses magic to scry through Ambermill's defensive shields and discover what the wizards are planning.",al={"what comes next","after dalar's analysis","dalaran intent"},sp=1,it="next_step"},{q="Where can Dalar Dawnweaver be found?",a="Dalar Dawnweaver can be found inside the crypt at the Sepulcher, the Forsaken's main stronghold in Silverpine Forest, along the main road.",al={"dalar location","where is dalar","dalar dawnweaver silverpine"},gp=true},{q="Why are the Kirin Tor operating openly in Silverpine Forest?",a="Before the Scourge devastated Lordaeron, Ambermill was a quiet lumber town. Though the capital and Dalaran fell, surviving wizards made Ambermill an active redoubt, where they constantly clash with Forsaken expansion.",al={"kirin tor silverpine","dalaran presence silverpine"},it="threat"}},ang={["class:Mage"]="As a Forsaken mage, you may recognize the Kirin Tor pendant as a traditional Dalaran spellweaving tool. Its presence suggests your old brethren are preparing an immense invocation.",["race:Undead"]="As Forsaken, you help monitor Dalaran's operations at Ambermill to guard Silverpine's borders and protect the Sepulcher from hostile sorcery.",["faction:Horde"]="As Horde, you help thwart the Kirin Tor's projects in Silverpine, keeping the Eastern Kingdoms secure from resurgent Alliance-aligned magical factions."},kw={"ambermill","dalar dawnweaver","dalaran","kirin tor","pendant","sepulcher","shadow priest allister","silverpine forest"},rel={"npc:dalar-dawnweaver","npc:shadow-priest-allister","quest:478","quest:482","subzone:ambermill","subzone:sepulcher","zone:silverpine"},m={start="Shadow Priest Allister",["end"]="Dalar Dawnweaver",level="14",faction="Horde",id=481},src={"Dalar's Analysis"}}
E["quest:482"] = {t="quest",n="Dalaran's Intentions",z="silverpine",s="Dalar Dawnweaver sends Shadow Priest Allister a warning from Silverpine Forest. A pendant bound for the Kirin Tor in Ambermill reveals their plan to awaken a dormant ley energy node beneath the town, and the Forsaken at the Sepulcher prepare to answer.",h="Dalar Dawnweaver sends Shadow Priest Allister a warning from Silverpine Forest.",sec={{t="A Dormant Spark",b="Dalar Dawnweaver studies a rune-inscribed pendant from a Dalaran supply crate and recalls an old Kirin Tor survey. Ambermill was chosen for a reason: the quiet village sits atop a dormant ley energy node. Dalar realizes the wizards intend to tap it. Awakening such a nexus takes immense magical reserves, and the enchanted pendants the wizards wear are key to channeling and catalyzing its power.",sp=0},{t="The Threat to Silverpine",b="The Forsaken cannot tolerate a fortified, power-fueled Kirin Tor outpost threatening the southern approaches to the Sepulcher and Tirisfal Glades. Whatever ritual the magi prepare, raw ley energy would give Dalaran an enormous strategic advantage in Lordaeron. Dalar urgently sends word to Shadow Priest Allister, asking him to devise a way to stall the wizards before their ritual is complete.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What is the Kirin Tor trying to do in Ambermill?",a="The wizards of Dalaran aim to awaken the dormant ley energy node beneath Ambermill. Its power would let them establish a permanent presence and pursue their wider plans in Silverpine Forest.",al={"ambermill ley line","what are dalaran wizards doing in silverpine","ambermill purpose"},it="purpose"},{q="Why does Dalar send you to Shadow Priest Allister?",a="Shadow Priest Allister holds authority over Forsaken tactics and countermeasures against Dalaran. Dalar Dawnweaver brings arcane insight and research, while Allister directs the response from the Sepulcher.",al={"why tell allister","who is allister","dalar dawnweaver allister"},it="next_step"},{q="How do the wizards' pendants tie into their plans?",a="The dormant ley node demands immense reserves of power to awaken. The wizards' enchanted pendants act as conduits and reservoirs for that magic, so taking them away would hinder the node's activation.",al={"kirin tor pendants","ambermill pendants","why collect pendants"},it="item"},{q="Why is Dalar Dawnweaver so concerned about the Kirin Tor's work in Ambermill?",a="Dalar Dawnweaver realizes that Ambermill rests upon a dormant ley energy node earmarked by the Kirin Tor. If the human wizards successfully awaken and harness that raw arcane power, it could grant Dalaran a formidable foothold right in the heart of Silverpine Forest. To secure the region for the Forsaken and eliminate a gathering magical threat, Dalar must ensure the Sepulcher's leadership takes immediate action to halt their work.",al={"why does dalar want this done","dalar dawnweaver motive","why stop kirin tor ambergrove"},it="motive",add="6acaedff"}},ang={["race:Undead"]="As an Undead, you know Dalaran's presence deep in Silverpine threatens Forsaken borders. Stopping the ley line ritual protects the roads between Tirisfal and the southern borders.",["class:Mage"]="As a Mage, you can recognize the Kirin Tor's method. Tapping dormant ley lines gives them an efficient way to establish a powerful arcane beachhead without hauling massive power sources through the wilderness.",["class:Priest"]="As a Priest, you know Shadow Priest Allister directs the Forsaken defense at the Sepulcher. He joins cold military pragmatism with the dark teachings of the Forsaken priesthood to purge living threats."},kw={"ambermill","dalar dawnweaver","dalaran's intentions","kirin tor","ley energy","sepulcher","shadow priest allister","silverpine forest"},rel={"npc:dalar-dawnweaver","npc:shadow-priest-allister","quest:481","quest:479","subzone:ambermill","subzone:sepulcher","zone:silverpine"},m={start="Dalar Dawnweaver",["end"]="Shadow Priest Allister",level="14",faction="Horde",id=482},src={"Dalaran's Intentions"}}
E["quest:516"] = {t="quest",n="Beren's Peril",z="silverpine",s="Scourge gather in a hidden cave in southern Silverpine Forest, and Shadow Priest Allister moves to stop them. The Forsaken hope to strike before the undead can begin their offensive.",h="Scourge gather in a hidden cave in southern Silverpine Forest, and Shadow Priest Allister moves to stop them.",sec={{t="A Preemptive Strike",b="Shadow Priest Allister hears that servants of the Lich King are gathering deep in southern Silverpine Forest. Their growing numbers threaten Forsaken operations across the region. Allister sends scouts to strike first and destroy the Scourge in their secluded lair before they can mobilize.",sp=0},{t="The Hidden Cave",b="A hidden cave cuts into the hills south of Ambermill, the Dalaran-aligned settlement. The rough slopes make the cavern easy to miss, and the approach lies around the hills’ southern face. Ravenclaw drudgers and guardians dwell inside, remnants of the Scourge whose destruction helps the Forsaken hold their ground in the forest.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What is Beren's Peril?",a="Beren's Peril is a secluded cave in the hills of southern Silverpine Forest, south of Ambermill. Ravenclaw undead dwell within.",al={"berens peril","where is berens peril","what is this cave"},it="place"},{q="Who assigns the mission to Beren's Peril?",a="Shadow Priest Allister, stationed at the Sepulcher in Silverpine Forest, sends Horde adventurers after learning that hostile undead are preparing an offensive from the cave.",al={"who gives berens peril","quest giver berens peril","shadow priest allister quest"},it="identity"},{q="Why are the Forsaken attacking the undead there?",a="The undead in Beren's Peril serve the Lich King as part of the Scourge. The Forsaken broke free of his control and fight to purge his lingering minions from their lands.",al={"why kill undead","why fight ravenclaw","arent forsaken undead"},it="motive"},{q="How do you find the entrance to the cave?",a="The cave lies in the hills south of Ambermill. The steep ridges make the southern face the way to reach its entrance.",al={"how to get to berens peril","cave entrance location","where is the cave entrance"},it="place",gp=true},{q="What enemies inhabit Beren's Peril?",a="Scourge thralls dwell in the cave, including Ravenclaw Drudgers and Ravenclaw Guardians. They appear to be gathering for an assault on nearby settlements.",al={"berens peril mobs","what is inside berens peril"},it="target"},{q="What role does Dalaran play in this mission?",a="Dalaran has no direct role in the mission. Human wizards from Dalaran occupy nearby Ambermill, which Allister uses as a landmark to help scouts find the hidden cave.",al={"dalaran connection","ambermill connection"},it="allies"}},ang={["race:Undead"]="For you, a Forsaken, rooting out Scourge remnants at Beren's Peril helps defend your people from the Lich King's lingering grasp.",["faction:Horde"]="For you in the Horde, clearing hidden Scourge pockets along Silverpine's borders helps stabilize northern Lordaeron.",["class:Priest"]="As a priest, you follow Shadow Priest Allister's orders and help secure the Sepulcher's authority by destroying rival undead horrors."},kw={"ambermill","beren's peril","berens peril","ravenclaw drudger","ravenclaw guardian","scourge","shadow priest allister","silverpine forest","the sepulcher"},rel={"npc:shadow-priest-allister","subzone:sepulcher","zone:silverpine","topic:scourge","topic:lich-king","subzone:ambermill","subzone:dalaran"},m={start="Shadow Priest Allister",level="21",faction="Horde",id=516,ri={"Ravenclaw Drudger","Ravenclaw Guardian"}},src={"Beren's Peril (quest)"}}
E["quest:6321"] = {t="quest",n="Supplying the Sepulcher",z="silverpine",s="At the Sepulcher, Deathguard Podrig seeks weapons for the hard-pressed garrison. He sends an order toward the Undercity as beasts, Scourge and other threats wear down its supplies.",h="At the Sepulcher, Deathguard Podrig seeks weapons for the hard-pressed garrison.",sec={{t="Arming the Front Line",b="Deathguard Podrig says the Sepulcher is fairly well stocked, yet fighting in Silverpine Forest steadily drains its gear. Feral beasts, Scourge remnants and other local threats wear down weapons and armor or leave them behind after skirmishes. Acting under Executor Hadrec's orders, Podrig writes a requisition for Gordon Wendham, a weapon dealer in the Undercity. Replacement arms and armor help the Forsaken hold their fragile footholds beyond Tirisfal Glades.",sp=0},{t="The Flight Network",b="Silverpine's roads make a slow, dangerous route for vital messages and supplies. The Forsaken send them by trained vampire bats instead. Karos Razok handles the bats at the Sepulcher, linking its soldiers to the Undercity's aerial network and the routes connecting outlying garrisons to Sylvanas's capital.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What is the purpose of Podrig's order?",a="Executor Hadrec ordered Deathguard Podrig to request weapons for the Sepulcher. Its general supplies were sufficient, but arms were needed to replace those broken or lost in fights with the Scourge and other forest threats.",al={"why podrig order","what is podrigs requisition","purpose of supplying the sepulcher"},it="purpose"},{q="Who is Gordon Wendham?",a="Gordon Wendham is a weapon merchant in the Undercity. Podrig addresses the Sepulcher's request for new arms to him.",al={"who is gordon wendham","gordon wendham undrcity"},it="people"},{q="Who is Karos Razok?",a="Karos Razok handles the bats at the Sepulcher. He oversees the dread bats that carry messengers, scouts and supplies across Lordaeron.",al={"karos razok role","who is the bat handler"},it="people"},{q="Why use bats instead of road couriers?",a="The roads through Silverpine Forest are dangerous, with hostile beasts, Scourge and other factions threatening couriers. Bat routes offer a faster, safer connection to the Undercity.",al={"why fly to undercity","why use bats"}},{q="What threats does the Sepulcher face?",a="The Sepulcher faces lingering Scourge undead, worgen, wild beasts and regional human factions. The garrison needs steady replacements to remain ready for battle.",al={"sepulcher threats","why do deathguards need weapons"},it="threat"},{q="Where does this task lead next?",a="Karos Razok can arrange flight transport to the Undercity, where the requisition is addressed to Gordon Wendham.",al={"what quest is next","next after supplying the sepulcher"},it="next_step"},{q="Why does Deathguard Podrig need this supply order delivered?",a="Deathguard Podrig conducted an inventory under Executor Hadrec's orders to ensure the Sepulcher remains fully armed. While general supplies are stable, ongoing skirmishes in Silverpine Forest against the Scourge and other prowling threats have cost the guards many of their weapons in the field. To keep the outpost from becoming defenseless, Podrig urgently needs this requisition sent to Gordon Wendham in the Undercity so replacement arms can be secured.",al={"why does podrig want this done","podrig motive","why order weapons"},it="motive",add="f1c1132b"},{q="Why does Podrig send you instead of handling the delivery himself?",a="Podrig is on active guard duty maintaining the Sepulcher's defenses alongside Executor Hadrec. With hostile Scourge roaming the surrounding woods, every Deathguard is needed to secure the perimeter and hold the camp. An able-bodied traveler provides the ideal courier to liaise with the bat master without pulling a soldier away from post.",al={"why send me","why doesnt podrig go","why rely on an adventurer"},it="why_me",add="ade30847"}},ang={["race:Undead"]="As an Undead, you help maintain Forsaken outposts like the Sepulcher, extending their reach beyond Tirisfal Glades and securing the surrounding wilderness for the Dark Lady.",["faction:Horde"]="As a member of the Horde, you rely on flight routes between garrisons and capital cities to coordinate defense across contested regions."},kw={"bat handler","deathguard","gordon wendham","hadrec","karos razok","podrig","requisition","sepulcher","silverpine","undercity"},rel={"subzone:sepulcher","npc:karos-razok","npc:gordon-wendham","zone:undercity","zone:silverpine","topic:scourge"},m={start="Deathguard Podrig",["end"]="Karos Razok",level="10",faction="Horde",id=6321},src={"Supplying the Sepulcher"}}
E["quest:91859"] = {t="quest",n="A Curious Pair",z="silverpine",s="In the Sepulcher, Trevan Rol spots an unusual pair passing through Silverpine Forest. The tauren and high elf travel under the Earthen Ring's banner, a rare sight in Horde territory that draws suspicion.",h="In the Sepulcher, Trevan Rol spots an unusual pair passing through Silverpine Forest.",sec={{t="Eyes in the Sepulcher",b="Trevan Rol sees two travelers claiming to represent the Earthen Ring pass along the road by the Sepulcher. The outpost is a grim waystation where strangers, especially those on diplomatic business, draw close scrutiny. A tauren traveling under the shamanic order's banner raises little surprise. His cloaked companion is another matter: the scout recognizes an unmistakable high elf, a sight that strikes the Forsaken as exceedingly strange.",sp=0},{t="A Peculiar Partnership",b="A high elf traveling openly beside a member of the Horde's shamanic circles raises questions among the Forsaken sentries. The Earthen Ring concerns itself with the balance of the elements, and high elves are rarely seen in Lordaeron, much less as companions to tauren envoys. To learn where the pair went and what business brought them to the forest, you are directed to Deathguard Baldren at the edge of town.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who are the two travelers mentioned in this quest?",a="Trevan Rol says the travelers presented themselves as Earthen Ring dignitaries. One is a tauren, while his cloaked companion is a high elf.",al={"who is the curious pair","who passed through sepulcher","who were the travelers"},it="people"},{q="Why is a high elf traveling with a tauren so unusual?",a="The high elves have ties to the Alliance and arcane magic, while tauren belong to the Horde and practice shamanism. Seeing them travel together through Horde-controlled Silverpine Forest under the Earthen Ring is rare and suspicious.",al={"why is high elf with tauren weird","tauren and high elf lore"},it="conflict"},{q="Who starts the quest A Curious Pair?",a="Trevan Rol gives the request in the Sepulcher, an outpost in Silverpine Forest.",al={"quest giver","where to pick up a curious pair"},gp=true},{q="Where do I find Deathguard Baldren?",a="Deathguard Baldren watches near the Sepulcher's entrance in Silverpine Forest, keeping an eye on travelers along the road.",al={"baldren location","where is baldren"},gp=true},{q="What is the Earthen Ring?",a="The Earthen Ring is an ancient shamanic organization devoted to preserving the balance of the elements and healing spiritual discord throughout the world. Its members are mostly shamans, including tauren and orcs, though its diplomats sometimes travel to distant lands.",al={"earthen ring lore","what is earthen ring"},it="identity"},{q="Is the high elf an enemy to the Forsaken?",a="Trevan Rol does not know whether the high elf is an enemy. The elf is cloaked and travels under diplomatic pretense beside a tauren, so the Forsaken question their purpose rather than attack outright.",al={"are they hostile","is elf an enemy"},it="hostile"},{q="Why does Trevan Rol want me to investigate the travelers?",a="Trevan Rol is baffled and suspicious after spotting a cloaked high elf travelling openly alongside a tauren under the banner of the Earthen Ring. Silverpine is dangerous Horde territory, and a member of the quel'dorei passing through without explanation is an extraordinary anomaly. Trevan wants to uncover what this odd pair is doing in Forsaken lands, but having exhausted what little he witnessed, he sends you to the town entrance to see what the sentries caught.",al={"why does trevan care","trevan rol motive","why investigate the travelers"},it="motive",add="f81f4edc"}},ang={["class:Shaman"]="Even experienced shamans find the Earthen Ring traveling with an elf unusual. The Ring's traditions rarely involve the quel'dorei.",["race:Tauren"]="As a tauren, you may feel conflicted seeing one of your kin travel through Lordaeron beside an elven stranger, watched closely by Forsaken sentries.",["race:Undead"]="As Forsaken, you know that outsiders passing through Silverpine Forest warrant close scrutiny, especially amid Lordaeron's fractured political climate."},kw={"curious pair","deathguard baldren","earthen ring","high elf","sepulcher","silverpine forest","tauren","trevan rol"},rel={"subzone:sepulcher","zone:silverpine","topic:tauren","topic:horde"},m={start="Trevan Rol",["end"]="Deathguard Baldren",level="22",faction="Horde",id=91859},src={"A Curious Pair"},fv=true}
E["quest:99"] = {t="quest",n="Arugal's Folly",z="silverpine",s="In Pyrewood Village, Dalar Dawnweaver seeks the magic binding its people to a curse. He needs enchanted shackles from the villagers to study Archmage Arugal's work and understand the worgen transformation.",h="In Pyrewood Village, Dalar Dawnweaver seeks the magic binding its people to a curse.",sec={{t="The Dual Lives of Pyrewood",b="South of the Sepulcher, Pyrewood Village lives two lives. In daylight, its fearful, insular residents appear to be ordinary human peasants. At twilight, their human forms tear apart and become savage Moonrage worgen, roaming the streets under Arugal's sway. Dalar Dawnweaver seeks to learn what arcane bindings cause this horror.",sp=0},{t="Shattering the Shackles",b="Dalar Dawnweaver needs enchanted Pyrewood Shackles from the transformed townsfolk to study the spell holding Pyrewood in thrall. The restraints carry the lingering sorcery of Arugal's failed wards. By examining their magic, the Forsaken mage hopes to understand the beastly transformation and find a way to bring down the rogue archmage of Shadowfang Keep.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Why do the people of Pyrewood Village turn into worgen at night?",a="Archmage Arugal's enchantments keep Pyrewood's people human by day, through an illusion or a dormant state. At night, they become Moonrage worgen under his control.",al={"pyrewood day night","pyrewood curse","why human then wolf"},it="target"},{q="What are the Pyrewood Shackles?",a="The Pyrewood Shackles are enchanted bindings worn by Pyrewood's cursed residents. Arugal used them as part of his magic over the town, and Dalar Dawnweaver studies their lingering energy to learn about the curse.",al={"pyrewood shackle","arugal shackles"},it="item"},{q="Who is Dalar Dawnweaver?",a="Dalar Dawnweaver is a Forsaken mage stationed at the Sepulcher in Silverpine Forest. He leads the Forsaken's magical study of Archmage Arugal's summoned worgen.",al={"dalar dawnweaver lore","who is quest giver sepulcher"},it="identity"},{q="Does finishing this quest cure Pyrewood Village?",a="No. The shackles give Dalar Dawnweaver insight into Arugal's magic, but Pyrewood's curse continues to hold the village in perpetual torment.",al={"can you cure pyrewood","do pyrewood people get cured"},sp=1,it="power"},{q="How does Arugal control the villagers?",a="Arugal bound the villagers to his will with reckless enchantments and enchanted shackles. They become beasts that guard the way to his domain at Shadowfang Keep.",al={"arugal pyrewood connection","how does arugal control them"},it="threat"},{q="What happens after completing the Arugal's Folly quest chain?",a="The Arugal's Folly chain ends with this assignment. What the Forsaken have learned lets them assess the threat of Shadowfang Keep and plan Arugal's downfall.",al={"after arugals folly","arugals folly finale"},sp=1,it="next_step"},{q="Why does Dalar Dawnweaver want the Pyrewood Shackles?",a="Dalar Dawnweaver is studying the bizarre enchantments that Archmage Arugal has cast across Silverpine Forest. By analyzing the magic bound within the villagers' shackles, Dalar hopes to unravel Arugal's so-called remedies, master the secrets of his wild spells, and gather the vital knowledge required to ultimately bring down the mad mage and undo his reckless sorcery.",al={"why does dalar want this","dalar dawnweaver motive","why collect pyrewood shackles"},it="motive",add="0ad90a3b"}},ang={["race:Undead"]="As Forsaken, you may see Pyrewood with cold fascination and ruthless pragmatism. Dismantling Arugal's enchantments could secure southern Silverpine.",["class:Mage"]="As a mage, you know Arugal's shackles warn how Kirin Tor sorcery can descend into madness when mixed with otherworldly summoned beasts.",["faction:Horde"]="As a member of the Horde, you help secure shackles that break Arugal's mystical stranglehold over the road south toward the Greymane Wall."},kw={"arugal","arugal's folly","dalar dawnweaver","moonrage worgen","pyrewood shackles","pyrewood village","silverpine forest","the sepulcher"},rel={"npc:dalar-dawnweaver","subzone:pyrewood-village","npc:arugal","topic:worgen","subzone:sepulcher","zone:silverpine","quest:421"},m={start="Dalar Dawnweaver",level="15",faction="Horde",id=99,ri={"Pyrewood Shackle"}},src={"Arugal's Folly (4)"}}
E["subzone:ambermill"] = {t="subzone",n="Ambermill",z="silverpine",s="Ambermill's wizards hold a fortified outpost in southeastern Silverpine Forest, southwest of Lordamere Lake. Once a quiet lumber village, it now shelters surviving wizards and apprentices from Dalaran, resisting the Forsaken on their southern borders.",h="Ambermill's wizards hold a fortified outpost in southeastern Silverpine Forest, southwest of Lordamere Lake.",sec={{t="A Bastion of Dalaran",b="Ambermill was a quiet lumber town before the Third War. After Lordaeron fell, surviving wizards of the Kirin Tor moved in and fortified the settlement. Dalaran spellscribes, conjurors, and apprentices now patrol its buildings and stables, keeping this forward redoubt against the undead.",sp=0},{t="Tapping the Ley Lines",b="Ambermill draws the Kirin Tor for more than defense. The village lies over a dormant ley line energy node. Forsaken spies and Deathstalkers watching the town have learned that Dalaran's magi are trying to awaken the nexus for large-scale arcane work. The surge could threaten the Forsaken's fragile hold on Silverpine Forest. Shadow Priest Allister and the Deathstalkers are working to stop them through sabotage, stolen Kirin Tor documents, and assassinations across the mill grounds.",sp=1,bt={"q477.3"}}},faq={{q="Why are Dalaran wizards occupying a village in Silverpine?",a="After Dalaran was devastated during the Third War, surviving Kirin Tor forces moved into Ambermill to establish an outpost of living human resistance. Forsaken agents are investigating their activities.",al={"why are wizards here","who controls ambermill","kirin tor silverpine"},it="purpose"},{q="Was Ambermill always part of Dalaran?",a="No. Before the Third War, Ambermill was a minor lumber village. Dalaran's wizards moved in and fortified it only after the Scourge overran Lordaeron.",al={"ambermill history","who owned ambermill"},it="origin"},{q="Why do the Forsaken want to attack Ambermill?",a="Ambermill is a fortified center of human opposition in Silverpine Forest. The Forsaken see its Dalaran-supported forces and secret arcane work as threats to their hold on the region.",al={"forsaken ambermill","why kill ambermill wizards"},it="conflict"},{q="What are the Deathstalkers searching for in Ambermill?",a="Forsaken Deathstalkers learned from captured human prisoners that Ambermill's wizards keep secured documents detailing Dalaran's secret plans and military intentions. The settlement is now a main target for covert infiltration and theft.",al={"ambermill documents","mennet carkad ambermill"},it="item"},{q="What is Ambermill?",a="Ambermill is a fortified human settlement nestled in the hills of southeastern Silverpine Forest, southwest of Lake Lordamere. Originally a quiet logging outpost complete with a town hall, stables, and mills, it has been repurposed into a heavily guarded military and magical encampment. Its buildings hum with arcane energy as spellcasters and guards maintain a firm perimeter against the hostile forest.",al={"what is ambermill","amber mill overview","tell me about ambermill"},it="place",add="9833b496"},{q="What happened to Ambermill?",a="Before the Third War, Ambermill was a quiet lumber town of little importance. After the Scourge ravaged the region and smashed Dalaran during the Third War, surviving Kirin Tor forces moved in and fortified the town to preserve a strategic foothold in Silverpine.",al={"ambermill history","amber mill backstory","history of ambermill"},it="history",add="c529bf0b"},{q="Who lives in Ambermill?",a="Ambermill is occupied and run entirely by Kirin Tor personnel from Dalaran. Its grounds are patrolled by Dalaran Protectors, conjured arcane serpents, apprentices, and spellscribes, while senior conjurors oversee mystical operations from within the town hall and surrounding buildings. Local service workers, like the tailor Avelina Lilly, have also provided provisions and clothing to the resident magi.",al={"who controls ambermill","ambermill residents","who is at amber mill"},it="residents",add="fc63f553"},{q="Is Ambermill dangerous?",a="Ambermill is extremely hazardous to anyone aligned with the Forsaken or the Horde. The Kirin Tor forces stationed here view the undead as an existential threat and will attack trespassers on sight. In addition to martial sentries, the settlement is guarded by skilled spellcasters who wield potent offensive magic, summoning protective arcane wards and serpent servitors to annihilate intruders.",al={"is ambermill hostile","danger in amber mill","is amber mill safe"},it="danger",add="b9a41d98"}},ang={["faction:Horde"]="As a Forsaken operative, you face one of Silverpine's few remaining pockets of living human resistance. Ambermill threatens southern logistics and harbors dangerous arcane secrets.",["class:Mage"]="As a mage, you see the Kirin Tor trying to restore their influence after the Scourge and Burning Legion devastated Dalaran."},kw={"ambermill","dalaran","kirin tor","ley line","shadow priest allister","silverpine forest"},rel={"zone:silverpine","subzone:dalaran","npc:shadow-priest-allister","quest:479","quest:482","quest:1999"},src={"Ambermill"}}
E["subzone:beren-s-peril"] = {t="subzone",n="Beren's Peril",z="silverpine",s="Scourge loyal to Thule Ravenclaw gather in the hills southwest of Ambermill, threatening the Forsaken.",h="Scourge loyal to Thule Ravenclaw gather in the hills southwest of Ambermill, threatening the Forsaken.",sec={{t="A Hidden Threat in the Hills",b="At Beren's Peril, a cave and mountain path lie high in the crags southwest of Ambermill, hidden from the main road. After the Third War, rogue Scourge undead fortified the refuge under the renegade necromancer Thule Ravenclaw. They refused to bow to the Dark Lady or flee north. Ravenclaw's regents, guardians, and drudgers gathered in secret to prepare an assault on the Forsaken base at the Sepulcher. Forsaken scouts uncovered them, and the quiet cliffs became a warzone. Horde fighters now move against the undead before they can attack.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What is Beren's Peril?",a="Beren's Peril is a cave and hillside pass southwest of Ambermill in Silverpine Forest, between the central highway and the Ambermill side road.",al={"berens peril","where is berens peril","beren's peril cave"},it="place"},{q="Who controls Beren's Peril?",a="Scourge undead loyal to Thule Ravenclaw occupy the cave, including Ravenclaw guardians, drudgers, and regents.",al={"who lives at berens peril","enemies at berens peril","ravenclaw undead"},it="residents"},{q="Why do the Forsaken care about this location?",a="Forsaken scouts found the undead gathering troops and arms for an assault on the Sepulcher. Shadow Priest Allister ordered preemptive strikes against them.",al={"allister berens peril","why attack berens peril","sepulcher threat"},it="threat"},{q="Who is Thule Ravenclaw?",a="Thule Ravenclaw is a powerful necromancer in Silverpine Forest who controlled pockets of mindless, hostile Scourge. He used places such as Beren's Peril and Fenris Keep to menace the region.",al={"thule ravenclaw","thule silverpine"},it="leader"},{q="What happened at Beren's Peril?",a="Following the Third War, this secluded cave complex in the Silverpine hills became a staging ground for renegade undead. Forsaken scouts tracking threats to the region discovered that hostile undead loyal to the rogue necromancer Thule Ravenclaw had amassed within the caverns, secretly preparing an assault against the nearby Forsaken settlement of the Sepulcher.",al={"beren's peril history","what happened at berens peril","berens peril lore"},it="history",add="896a3c65"},{q="Is Beren's Peril dangerous?",a="Yes, Beren's Peril is extremely dangerous. The hillside cave is swarming with hostile undead under the sway of Thule Ravenclaw, including Ravenclaw drudgers, guardians, and regents. Any traveler venturing into the caverns risks being overwhelmed by these organized undead before they can launch their strike against the Sepulcher.",al={"berens peril danger","how dangerous is beren's peril","is berens peril safe"},it="danger",add="25ec4175"}},ang={["race:Undead"]="As an undead, you face a bitter reminder of the Scourge's lasting grip. Ravenclaw's minions threaten the Sepulcher, and Sylvanas's loyalists must destroy them swiftly and without mercy.",["faction:Horde"]="As Horde, you must secure Silverpine Forest's rugged paths and clear rogue undead from their lairs before they can sever supply lines between the Sepulcher and the southern territories."},kw={"allister","ambermill","beren's peril","berens peril","ravenclaw drudge","scourge","sepulcher","silverpine","thule ravenclaw"},rel={"quest:516","quest:446","npc:shadow-priest-allister","zone:silverpine","subzone:sepulcher","subzone:ambermill","topic:forsaken","topic:third-war"},src={"Beren's Peril"}}
E["subzone:dawning-isles"] = {t="subzone",n="Dawning Isles",z="silverpine",s="The Dawning Isles lie blighted beneath the Vile Fin murlocs’ growing numbers. Along Silverpine Forest’s eastern edge, the islets rise from Lordamere Lake, where the Plague of Undeath has left their shores rotting.",h="The Dawning Isles lie blighted beneath the Vile Fin murlocs’ growing numbers.",sec={{t="Blight on the Lake",b="The Dawning Isles lie under the Vile Fin murlocs’ claim. Before the Third War, these keys rested amid Lordamere Lake’s calm, clear waters. When the Plague of Undeath swept across Lordaeron, corruption spread through the shallows. The vegetation turned pallid and rotting, and the islands lost their former peace. Now the Vile Fin murlocs hold the muddy shores and tangled brush. They defend their growing colonies against anyone who tries to cross the lake.",sp=0},{t="A Murloc Stronghold",b="Bog beasts once prowled the blighted Dawning Isles alongside the murlocs. The bog beasts have since vanished, leaving the Vile Fin population to swell. The murlocs now control the isles outright, making the chain of keys their stronghold on Lordamere Lake.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Where are the Dawning Isles located?",a="The Dawning Isles rise from Lordamere Lake along Silverpine Forest’s eastern boundary, just west of the Ruins of Lordaeron.",al={"dawning isles location","where is dawning isles","dawning islands map"},it="place",gp=true},{q="What creatures inhabit the Dawning Isles?",a="The Vile Fin tribe of murlocs thrives along the corrupted shores. Bog beasts once prowled the islets too, but they have since largely vanished as the murloc population has grown.",al={"mobs on dawning isles","what lives on dawning isles","dawning isle monsters"},it="residents"},{q="Why are the trees and shores rotting here?",a="The Plague of Undeath tainted the Dawning Isles when it swept across Lordaeron during the Third War. The water and soil absorbed the blight, poisoning the vegetation and leaving the islets murky, sickly, and decayed.",al={"why are dawning isles blighted","lake blight dawning isles"},it="ruin"},{q="What are the Dawning Isles?",a="The Dawning Isles are a cluster of low keys rising out of the waters of Lordamere Lake along northeastern Silverpine Forest. Once considered an idyllic and serene retreat on the lake's crystalline surface, the archipelago has since fallen into decay under the lingering blight of the Plague of Undeath.",al={"what are dawning isles","dawning isles lore","about dawning isles"},it="place",add="501d8847"},{q="What happened to the Dawning Isles?",a="Once pristine islets upon Lordamere Lake, the Dawning Isles were ruined by the spread of the Plague of Undeath, turning their vegetation sickly and rotting the shores. Murlocs and bog beasts overran the islets; the bog beasts have since vanished, and the Vile Fin murlocs have grown numerous enough to take control of the isles.",al={"dawning isles history","what happened at dawning isles"},it="history",add="425e68c2"},{q="Are the Dawning Isles dangerous?",a="Yes, they are exceptionally perilous. Beyond the lingering rot of the Plague, the isles are overrun by aggressive Vile Fin murlocs that have multiplied in great numbers and attack anyone entering their territory.",al={"is dawning isles safe","how dangerous are dawning isles","dawning isles danger"},it="danger",add="d646a662"}},ang={["race:Undead"]="The blighted Dawning Isles lie on Lordamere Lake, within sight of the Undercity’s western approaches. The Vile Fin murlocs that hold them grow more numerous each year.",["faction:Alliance"]="The blighted Dawning Isles show how far the Scourge’s corruption reached into Lordaeron’s scenic waters."},kw={"dawning isles","lordaeron","lordamere lake","silverpine forest","vile fin"},rel={"subzone:lordamere-lake","zone:silverpine","zone:ruinsoflordaeron","topic:murloc","topic:forsaken","topic:plague-of-undeath","topic:lordaeron"},src={"Dawning Isles"}}
E["subzone:dead-field"] = {t="subzone",n="Dead Field",z="silverpine",s="Forsaken assaults falter at Dead Field, a ruined farmstead in northern Silverpine Forest. Rot Hide gnolls serve the Scourge there, while the banshee Nightlash turns back those who attack.",h="Forsaken assaults falter at Dead Field, a ruined farmstead in northern Silverpine Forest.",sec={{t="A Blighted Staging Ground",b="The ruined farmstead lies in northern Silverpine Forest, its human occupants lost to the Third War. Rot Hide gnolls now use the plot as a base and willingly serve the Scourge. Deathstalker scouts passing through the region have noted signs of imminent military mobilization that threatens Forsaken supply lines and outposts. Small Forsaken assaults on the farm have repeatedly failed. Each time the gnolls are endangered, Nightlash, a wailing banshee, appears and drives the attackers back.",sp=0},{t="Ravenclaw's Ambition",b="Thule Ravenclaw directs the Rot Hide gnolls from Fenris Isle. The necromancer seeks to establish Scourge dominance over Silverpine and drive Sylvanas's forces from Lordaeron. He sends magical apparitions to the farmstead to survey his undead horde and warn Forsaken intruders.",sp=1,bt={"q437.6"}}},faq={{q="What is the Dead Field?",a="Dead Field is a ruined farmstead in northern Silverpine Forest. It was once an ordinary human farm, but has fallen into ruin and is now occupied by Rot Hide gnolls aligned with the Scourge.",al={"dead field silverpine","where is dead field","what happened to dead field"},it="place"},{q="Why are there gnolls at the farm?",a="The Rot Hide gnolls serve the Scourge and use the farmstead to gather forces and prepare attacks against Forsaken positions in northern Silverpine Forest.",al={"why rot hide gnolls","rot hides dead field","scourge gnolls"}},{q="Who is Nightlash?",a="Nightlash is a Scourge banshee who commands the Rot Hide gnolls at the farm. When Forsaken forces attack, she appears to defend her servants and repel their attempts to reclaim the land.",al={"nightlash banshee","banshee in dead field","who protects the gnolls"}},{q="Who commands the Scourge forces here?",a="Thule Ravenclaw, a powerful necromancer based on nearby Fenris Isle, commands the Scourge forces here. He coordinates the gnolls through apparitions and magical oversight to harass Forsaken expansion.",al={"who controls dead field","thule ravenclaw dead field","who is in charge"},sp=1,it="in_charge",bt={"q437.6"}},{q="What happened to the farm at the Dead Field?",a="The farm was once a homestead in northern Silverpine Forest, though the names and fates of the original farmers have been lost to the Third War. When the kingdom fell, the land fell into decrepitude, and Scourge agents moved in. Rather than cultivating crops, the Scourge turned the abandoned grounds into an outpost, rallying undead gnolls and preparing to menace nearby Forsaken holdings.",al={"dead field history","what happened at dead field","who lived at dead field"},it="history",add="8ddbb760"},{q="Who controls the Dead Field?",a="The farm is occupied by the Rot Hide gnolls, who serve the Scourge as foot soldiers. Above them lurks the banshee Nightlash, who oversees the outpost and appears whenever her minions are assaulted. The necromancer Thule Ravenclaw coordinates their movements from afar, using apparitions to direct their efforts against the Forsaken.",al={"who runs dead field","who lives at dead field","dead field residents"},it="residents",add="00a3cfa2"},{q="Why is the Dead Field abandoned?",a="Like much of northern Silverpine, the farm collapsed when the Scourge overran Lordaeron. The inhabitants were killed or driven away, and no living souls remained to tend the soil or maintain the buildings. Left untended amidst plagued soil, the decaying barns and ruined fences were quickly seized by the Scourge as a forward staging ground.",al={"why is dead field ruined","why is dead field abandoned","dead field ruin"},it="ruin",add="242af2de"},{q="Is the Dead Field dangerous?",a="It is extremely hazardous for anyone traveling alone. The Rot Hide gnolls gather here in growing numbers, pointing to imminent Scourge aggression. Repeated Forsaken raids have failed to dislodge them because Nightlash manifests swiftly to protect her servants, turning any direct confrontation into a lethal clash against both feral gnolls and ethereal wails.",al={"how dangerous is dead field","dead field threat","is dead field safe"},it="danger",add="fd654559"}},ang={["race:Undead"]="For you, the Forsaken, the Scourge foothold at Dead Field threatens the road between the Sepulcher and northern Lordaeron. It calls for swift extermination.",["class:Rogue"]="As a rogue, you know Deathstalker recon teams watch the farm closely. Infiltrating the gnoll ranks and striking their command structure is a critical tactical priority."},kw={"banshee","dead field","deathstalkers","nightlash","rot hide","silverpine forest","thule ravenclaw"},rel={"quest:437","quest:446","quest:1886","zone:silverpine","topic:gnoll","topic:scourge","topic:forsaken"},src={"Dead Field"}}
E["subzone:decrepit-ferry"] = {t="subzone",n="Decrepit Ferry",z="silverpine",s="At the Decrepit Ferry, broken docks leave Fenris Isle cut off across Lordamere Lake. The Scourge killed the ferryman and wrecked the boats, and undead and Rot Hide gnolls now overrun the shore.",h="At the Decrepit Ferry, broken docks leave Fenris Isle cut off across Lordamere Lake.",sec={{t="A Lifeline Cut Short",b="Before the Third War, daily traffic crossed Lordamere Lake from this dock. Local farmers brought fresh produce to the water and sold it to the wealthy lord of Fenris Isle and his household. For a modest fee, the ferryman carried trade goods, messengers, and visiting nobles between the mainland and the keep. That commerce ended when the Scourge swept through the kingdom. The ferryman was brutally killed, the boats were smashed, and the pier fell into decay.",sp=0},{t="A Corrupted Shoreline",b="The docks are dangerous for travelers along the lake shore. With the ferry out of service, Fenris Isle sits isolated across the water. Ghouls, skeletal warriors, and roving Rot Hide gnolls roam the ruins. The former crossing is now a dangerous stretch of Silverpine shoreline.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What was the Decrepit Ferry used for originally?",a="The ferry carried people and goods between mainland Silverpine and Fenris Isle. Farmers brought their harvest across Lordamere Lake to sell to the island's wealthy lord, and paid the ferryman a modest fee for each passage.",al={"ferry history","what was this dock","why is there a ferry here"},it="purpose"},{q="What happened to the ferry and its ferryman?",a="When the Scourge swept through Lordaeron, the ferryman was murdered and the boats were smashed. The pier fell into decay, and the crossing ended.",al={"what happened to ferryman","who broke the ferry"},it="history"},{q="What monsters lurk around the ferry docks now?",a="Ghouls and skeletal warriors roam the shore, alongside Rot Hide gnolls that prowl the nearby banks.",al={"decrepit ferry mobs","what lives at the ferry"},it="threat"},{q="Can you still take a boat to Fenris Isle from here?",a="No. The boats were smashed and the pier fell into decay, leaving Fenris Isle cut off across the lake.",al={"take boat to fenris","how to get to fenris isle","does the ferry work"},gp=true},{q="What is the Decrepit Ferry?",a="The Decrepit Ferry is the ruined remains of a once-busy dock along the eastern shore of Silverpine Forest. Before the fall of Lordaeron, it served as the vital crossing point over Lake Lordamere to Fenris Isle, ferrying local farmers, travelers, and supplies out to the island estate.",al={"what is decrepit ferry","decrepit ferry silverpine","decrepit ferry docks"},it="place",add="e48e8d6c"},{q="Why is the Decrepit Ferry ruined and abandoned?",a="When the Scourge swept through Lordaeron, the ferry service came to a violent end. The ferryman was murdered by the undead onslaught, the vessels were smashed, and the docks fell into utter neglect as monstrous predators overran the surrounding shores.",al={"why is it abandoned","why is decrepit ferry ruined","decrepit ferry destroyed"},it="ruin",add="db91f3d1"},{q="Is the Decrepit Ferry dangerous?",a="Yes, it is extremely perilous for unwary travelers. The abandoned docks and waterside are swarming with aggressive ghouls, restless skeletal warriors, and feral Rot Hide gnolls, making any attempt to linger near the landing a deadly proposition.",al={"is decrepit ferry dangerous","decrepit ferry threats","is it safe here"},it="danger",add="e3243651"},{q="Why is it called the Decrepit Ferry?",a="It earned its grim name from the shattered, rotting state left behind after the Third War. What was once a sturdy, bustling lifeline to Fenris Isle has decayed into weathered timbers, smashed debris, and waterlogged ruin.",al={"why is it called decrepit ferry","decrepit ferry name","origin of the name decrepit ferry"},it="name",add="bec7dabe"}},ang={["race:Undead"]="As an Undead, you see Lordaeron's fall in these ruins. Scourge remnants and Rot Hide gnolls now threaten Forsaken operations in eastern Silverpine."},kw={"decrepit ferry","fenris isle","ferryman","ghouls","lordamere lake","rot hide","scourge","silverpine forest"},rel={"subzone:fenris-isle","zone:silverpine","topic:gnoll","topic:scourge","topic:lordaeron","quest:438"},src={"Decrepit Ferry"}}
E["subzone:deep-elem-mine"] = {t="subzone",n="Deep Elem Mine",z="silverpine",s="Deep Elem Mine lies in central Silverpine Forest, its tunnels claimed by worgen. Once an active mine, it fell when Archmage Arugal's magic swept through the region and transformed its miners.",h="Deep Elem Mine lies in central Silverpine Forest, its tunnels claimed by worgen.",sec={{t="A Den of Beasts",b="Deep Elem Mine once supplied the living people of Lordaeron with ore. When Archmage Arugal unleashed his lupine curse across Silverpine Forest, it spread through the tunnels. The laborers succumbed and became vicious worgen, abandoning their pickaxes to claim the cavern as a lair.",sp=0},{t="Grimson and Forsaken Ambition",b="Grimson the Pale commands the pack inside the mine. Once its foreman, he kept his cunning through the transformation. The Forsaken at the Sepulcher seek to reclaim the tunnels and their ore. On orders backed by Dreadlord Varimathras, Forsaken agents mean to sever Grimson's head and purge the beasts so the Horde can secure the mine's wealth.",sp=1}},faq={{q="What is inside Deep Elem Mine?",a="Hostile worgen afflicted by Archmage Arugal's magic fill the mine. Their pack is led by Grimson the Pale, once the human foreman, who now rules deep in the tunnels.",al={"whats in deep elem mine","deep elem mine mobs","who lives in deep elem mine"},it="residents"},{q="Why do the Forsaken want Deep Elem Mine cleared?",a="The Forsaken want the mine's mineral wealth for their war efforts in Lordaeron. Dalar Dawnweaver and the Sepulcher's leaders intend to claim its resources in the name of Dreadlord Varimathras once the worgen are eradicated.",al={"forsaken mine interest","why clear deep elem mine","who wants the mine"},it="purpose"},{q="Who is Grimson the Pale?",a="Grimson the Pale was the mortal foreman of Deep Elem Mine. Arugal's feral curse transformed the workers, and Grimson became a cunning worgen alpha who kept enough intellect to command the pack in the mine.",al={"who is grimson","grimson the pale lore","deep elem mine boss"},it="leader"},{q="How did the worgen get into the mine?",a="The worgen began as the mine's own laborers. Archmage Arugal's curse spread across Silverpine Forest and transformed them where they worked.",al={"why are there worgen in the mine","worgen origin deep elem mine","how did miners turn"},it="history"},{q="What is Deep Elem Mine?",a="Deep Elem Mine is an old mining site carved into the hills of central Silverpine Forest. Once a regular working excavation under human overseers, it has ceased ordinary operations and fallen under the control of feral worgen spawned by Archmage Arugal's dark sorcery.",al={"deep elem mine","what is deep elem","deep elem mine silverpine"},it="place",add="1f4b67a8"},{q="Why was Deep Elem Mine abandoned?",a="The mine fell when Archmage Arugal's fell sorcery spread across the hills of Silverpine. Rather than simply being overrun from without, the mine collapsed from within when its own foreman, Grimson the Pale, succumbed to the worgen curse and turned the site into a den for feral beasts.",al={"why is deep elem mine abandoned","deep elem mine ruined","what ruined deep elem mine"},it="ruin",add="3a795aef"},{q="Is Deep Elem Mine dangerous?",a="Deep Elem Mine is extremely perilous to wander into unprepared. Its dark tunnels are swarming with savage worgen driven by predatory instincts, all united under the ruthless command of their former overseer, Grimson the Pale.",al={"deep elem mine danger","is deep elem mine safe","threats in deep elem mine"},it="danger",add="ee2e1c55"}},ang={["race:Undead"]="For the Forsaken, securing the mine brings economic gain and answers the Sepulcher's order to break Arugal's grip on central Silverpine.",["profession:Mining"]="The feral pack makes mining dangerous, but Deep Elem Mine holds one of Silverpine's richest underground mineral deposits."},kw={"arugal","dalar dawnweaver","deep elem mine","grimson the pale","silverpine forest","varimathras","worgen"},rel={"npc:arugal","quest:99","npc:dalar-dawnweaver","topic:worgen","zone:silverpine","topic:forsaken","npc:varimathras"},src={"Deep Elem Mine"}}
E["subzone:fenris-isle"] = {t="subzone",n="Fenris Isle",z="silverpine",s="Rot Hide gnolls and a rogue Scourge necromancer hold Fenris Isle in Lordamere Lake, off Silverpine Forest.",h="Rot Hide gnolls and a rogue Scourge necromancer hold Fenris Isle in Lordamere Lake, off Silverpine Forest.",sec={{t="A Fallen Stronghold on the Lake",b="Fenris Keep once anchored Lordaeron’s military outpost on Fenris Isle. When the Scourge swept through northern Lordaeron, the garrison was slaughtered or fled into exile, leaving the island to the dead. Since then, Rot Hide gnolls have made it their stronghold, spreading a crude empire across the lake’s shores. The Forsaken of Silverpine Forest watch the island closely, fearing its entrenched inhabitants threaten their northern territories.",sp=0},{t="The Master of Fenris Keep",b="Thule Ravenclaw commands Fenris Keep from its crumbling stone halls. Once aligned with the Kirin Tor, the necromancer turned to the Scourge’s dark arts and bent the native gnolls to his will. His sorcery raises their fallen kin and fortifies the island against intrusion. From this isolated sanctuary, Thule oversees the lake’s ferry crossings. Forsaken scouts and Horde forces strike ahead of any greater threat, seeking to break his hold on the archipelago.",sp=1,bt={"q437.6"}}},faq={{q="What is Fenris Isle?",a="Fenris Isle lies in Lordamere Lake, off Silverpine Forest’s eastern coast. Before the Third War, it served as a fortress for the Kingdom of Lordaeron; now plague-ridden gnolls and Scourge servants infest it.",al={"where is fenris isle","fenris isle lore","what is this island"},it="place"},{q="Who controls Fenris Isle right now?",a="Rot Hide gnolls occupy Fenris Isle and hold Fenris Keep as their stronghold. Forsaken investigators seek to uncover the source of the growing threat.",al={"who runs fenris isle","fenris isle bosses","who lives on fenris isle"},it="residents"},{q="What happened to the humans who used to live here?",a="When the Scourge overran Lordaeron during the Third War, Fenris Keep’s human defenders and inhabitants were murdered or driven away. The fortress lay in ruins until gnolls and necromancers claimed its empty ramparts.",al={"what happened to fenris keep humans","who built fenris keep"},it="history"},{q="Why is the Horde interested in attacking the island?",a="The Forsaken see the entrenched Rot Hide gnolls as a threat to Silverpine Forest and the nearby ferry crossing. Their agents seek help investigating and disrupting the island’s hostile forces.",al={"assault on fenris isle lore","why do horde attack fenris isle","forsaken fenris isle"},it="threat"},{q="Why is Fenris Keep in ruins?",a="Fenris Keep once served as a thriving military stronghold for the kingdom of Lordaeron. When the Scourge swept across the northern realms during the Third War, the fortress fell. Its defenders and inhabitants were slaughtered or driven into flight, leaving the outpost abandoned to decay until Thule Ravenclaw and his gnolls claimed the wreckage.",al={"why is fenris isle abandoned","fenris keep ruined","what ruined fenris keep"},it="ruin",add="5a4e2fe3"},{q="Is Fenris Isle dangerous?",a="Fenris Isle is extremely perilous. The island is thoroughly infested by the Rot Hide gnolls and ruled by the rogue wizard Thule Ravenclaw. Surrounded by the murky waters of Lordamere Lake, any explorer who crosses to the island faces aggressive, diseased beasts and dark spellcasting within the dilapidated keep.",al={"is fenris isle safe","fenris isle dangers","threats on fenris isle"},it="danger",add="115572ef"}},ang={["race:Undead"]="As Forsaken, you see Fenris Isle as an intolerable Scourge bastion in your own backyard. Relentless strikes are needed to keep Thule Ravenclaw’s Rot Hide gnolls from overrunning Silverpine’s eastern waters.",["faction:Horde"]="As Horde, you can help Forsaken agents investigate the Rot Hide gnolls and strike their stronghold across Lordamere Lake."},kw={"fenris isle","fenris keep","lordamere lake","rot hide","silverpine forest","thule ravenclaw"},rel={"subzone:fenris-keep","subzone:lordamere-lake","zone:silverpine","quest:442","quest:446","quest:439","subzone:decrepit-ferry","topic:scourge"},src={"Fenris Isle"}}
E["subzone:fenris-keep"] = {t="subzone",n="Fenris Keep",z="silverpine",s="On Fenris Isle, isolated in the heart of Lordamere Lake, Fenris Keep now belongs to the Scourge. Thule Ravenclaw holds the stone fortress that once sheltered Lordaeron troops.",h="On Fenris Isle, isolated in the heart of Lordamere Lake, Fenris Keep now belongs to the Scourge.",sec={{t="The Scourge on Lordamere",b="Thule Ravenclaw rules Fenris Keep and threatens the Forsaken in Silverpine Forest. From the fortress, he sends Rot Hide gnolls to attack anyone who sets foot on the isle. Fenris Isle lies only miles across the water from the Tirisfal border. So the Forsaken at the Sepulcher and Undercity send champions to break the keep's defenses and end the rogue necromancer's rule.",sp=1,bt={"q437.6"}},{t="A Fallen Bastion of Lordaeron",b="Before the Third War, Fenris Keep guarded Lordamere Lake for the Kingdom of Lordaeron. A sizable force of troops held the island fortress. When the Scourge swept across the land, the keep fell with the rest of the realm.\n\nThule Ravenclaw, a former Kirin Tor wizard who betrayed his order, seized the fortress. He joined the Scourge and used necromancy to subdue the island's gnolls, making them the ravenous Rot Hide pack. Now he is entrenched deep within the keep's stone halls.",sp=1,bt={"q437.6"}}},faq={{q="What is Fenris Keep?",a="Fenris Keep is an isolated stone fortress on Fenris Isle in Lordamere Lake. Once a military stronghold for the fallen kingdom of Lordaeron, it is now held by the undead Scourge.",al={"fenris keep lore","what is fenris keep","fenris castle"},it="place"},{q="Who rules Fenris Keep right now?",a="Thule Ravenclaw rules Fenris Keep. The former Kirin Tor mage betrayed the living to serve the Scourge, and commands undead-tainted Rot Hide gnolls from within the fortress.",al={"who controls fenris keep","fenris keep boss","master of fenris isle"},sp=1,it="residents",bt={"q437.6"}},{q="Why are there gnolls inside Fenris Keep?",a="Thule Ravenclaw subdued the local gnolls with dark magic and disease, twisting them into Rot Hide gnolls. They guard the castle and surrounding island as his loyal shock troops.",al={"rot hide gnolls fenris","why gnolls in keep","fenris gnolls"},sp=1,bt={"q437.6"}},{q="Why do the Forsaken care about Fenris Keep?",a="Fenris Keep gives the Scourge a defensible base on Lordamere Lake. It threatens Forsaken movements through eastern Silverpine Forest and Tirisfal Glades, so Sylvanas's forces cannot leave a Scourge commander unchecked so close to their borders.",al={"why forsaken attack fenris","forsaken fenris keep","undercity fenris"},it="motive"},{q="What happened to Fenris Keep?",a="Fenris Keep once held immense strategic value, housing a sizable garrison of the Kingdom of Lordaeron's military amidst the waters of Lordamere Lake. When the Third War swept the land, the Scourge overran the fortress. Rather than being cleansed, it fell into the hands of Thule Ravenclaw, a renegade Kirin Tor mage who allied with the Lich King and transformed the local gnoll tribes into ravenous undead minions.",al={"fenris keep history","what happened at fenris keep","fenris keep lore"},it="history",add="c58313a0"},{q="Why is Fenris Keep ruined?",a="Fenris Keep fell to ruin when the Scourge decimated Lordaeron's defenses during the Third War. The military garrison that once maintained the fortress was slaughtered, leaving the structures untended and rotting. Today, it stands as a decaying stronghold dominated by necromantic magic and feral, flesh-eating gnolls.",al={"why is fenris keep abandoned","who destroyed fenris keep","fenris keep ruins"},it="ruin",add="07ecc870"},{q="Is Fenris Keep dangerous?",a="It is exceptionally dangerous. The fortress and surrounding island crawl with the Rot Hide gnolls, who hungrily attack anyone setting foot on their shores. Within the keep itself resides Thule Ravenclaw, a dangerous necromancer wielding dark magic over his monstrous servants.",al={"fenris keep danger","is fenris keep safe","how dangerous is fenris keep"},it="danger",add="6ae37309"}},ang={["faction:Horde"]="For the Horde, and especially the Forsaken, Fenris Keep is a lingering Scourge stronghold. They must eradicate it to safeguard Silverpine Forest and Lordamere Lake's waterways.",["class:Mage"]="As a mage, you can see Thule Ravenclaw's betrayal of the Kirin Tor's teachings. He turned Dalaran's arcane knowledge to the Scourge's dark arts."},kw={"fenris isle","fenris keep","lordaeron","lordamere lake","rot hide","scourge","silverpine forest","thule ravenclaw"},rel={"subzone:fenris-isle","quest:446","subzone:lordamere-lake","zone:silverpine","topic:scourge","topic:forsaken","topic:gnoll","quest:366"},src={"Fenris Keep"}}
E["subzone:greymane-wall"] = {t="subzone",n="Greymane Wall",z="silverpine",s="At Silverpine’s southern edge, Greymane Wall bars the way into Gilneas. King Genn Greymane raised the stone barrier after the Second War, and its gates remain locked against the outside world.",h="At Silverpine’s southern edge, Greymane Wall bars the way into Gilneas.",sec={{t="A Monument to Isolation",b="King Genn Greymane turned from the Alliance after the Second War, resentful of its demands, especially the taxes for the orc internment camps. He believed Gilneas had paid enough in coin and blood for troubles beyond its borders. Greymane withdrew the kingdom from the Alliance and ordered a vast barrier built across the head of the peninsula. When the Third War brought the Plague of Undeath and desperate refugees to the wall, its gates stayed shut.",sp=0},{t="The Price of Seclusion",b="The wall kept the Scourge from overrunning the peninsula, but Silverpine beyond it found no such safety. Archmage Arugal of Dalaran summoned feral worgen to fight the undead. The beasts could not be controlled, and now prowl the forest beneath the silent wall. What lies behind the gates remains unknown to the outside world.",sp=1}},faq={{q="What lies beyond the Greymane Wall?",a="The peninsula kingdom of Gilneas lies beyond the wall, ruled by King Genn Greymane. Before the Third War, Gilneas cut itself off from Lordaeron and the rest of the world, closing all commerce and communication.",al={"what is behind the wall","where does greymane wall lead","what kingdom is behind the wall"},it="place"},{q="Can you open the gates of the Greymane Wall?",a="No. The portcullis and iron-banded doors are barred from the southern side. Gilneas has severed all contact with the outside world, and nothing enters or leaves.",al={"how to get past greymane wall","can you open greymane wall","open the gate"},gp=true},{q="Why was the wall built here instead of farther south?",a="No record explains the wall’s exact course. It crosses Silverpine’s southern edge at the head of the Gilnean peninsula, leaving villages such as Pyrewood and Ambermill to its north.",al={"why did they build it here","why cut off pyrewood","crowley lands cut off"},it="origin"},{q="What happened to the refugees who fled here during the Third War?",a="When the Scourge ravaged Lordaeron, crowds of human refugees gathered outside the wall and begged to enter. King Greymane refused to open the gates to protect his kingdom, and the undead eventually slaughtered the desperate refugees outside.",al={"scourge refugees wall","refugees outside greymane wall"},it="history"},{q="What is the Greymane Wall?",a="The Greymane Wall is a colossal stone bulwark spanning the southern frontier of Silverpine Forest. Commissioned by King Genn Greymane after the Second War, it seals the kingdom of Gilneas away from Lordaeron and the rest of the world behind massive, impenetrable gates.",al={"what is greymane wall","greymane wall","giant wall in silverpine"},it="place",add="29630d52"},{q="Why is it called the Greymane Wall?",a="It is named after King Genn Greymane, the ruler of Gilneas who ordered its construction. Chafing at high taxes to support the Alliance's orc internment camps and weary of foreign wars, Greymane erected the colossal barrier to isolate his nation completely.",al={"why is it called greymane wall","who named greymane wall","greymane name origin"},it="name",add="18f5ff7d"},{q="Who controls the Greymane Wall?",a="The wall belongs entirely to the isolationist kingdom of Gilneas, ruled by King Genn Greymane. While Gilnean sentries keep watch from the safe side of the great ramparts, the outside perimeter is utterly abandoned to the wilderness and whatever shadows wander Silverpine.",al={"who controls greymane wall","who guards the wall","who lives at greymane wall"},it="residents",add="e1e9af4d"},{q="Is the Greymane Wall dangerous?",a="The wall itself is an impassable stone barrier, but the lands outside its gate are perilous. Silverpine Forest is overrun with feral worgen, vengeful spirits, and hostile beasts that prey upon any traveler who lingers too close to the silent, barred entrance.",al={"is greymane wall safe","is it dangerous near the wall","threats at greymane wall"},it="danger",add="6b007fab"}},ang={["faction:Alliance"]="For the Alliance, Greymane Wall recalls Gilneas’s abandonment of its former allies. When the Scourge took Lordaeron, Greymane ignored their pleas and left them outside his gates.",["faction:Horde"]="For the Forsaken, who now claim Silverpine Forest, Greymane Wall marks an impassable southern border. It seals away a human kingdom whose intentions and strength remain unknown."},kw={"arugal","genn greymane","gilneas","greymane wall","pyrewood","silverpine"},rel={"zone:silverpine","subzone:pyrewood-village","subzone:ambermill","topic:worgen","npc:arugal","topic:alliance-of-lordaeron","topic:scourge"},src={"Greymane Wall"}}
E["subzone:ivar-patch"] = {t="subzone",n="Ivar Patch",z="silverpine",s="At Ivar Patch in northern Silverpine Forest, a ruined harvest hides the fate of its farmhands.",h="At Ivar Patch in northern Silverpine Forest, a ruined harvest hides the fate of its farmhands.",sec={{t="A Ruined Harvest",b="Before the Third War, Ivar's pumpkin farm was a prosperous homestead in Lordaeron. Ivar employed lively farmhands and servants, but the Scourge spread the Plague of Undeath across the countryside and consumed the farm. Ivar, his family, and his laborers rose again as rotting, feral ghouls, bound to prowl the ruined soil without their minds. Unlike the Forsaken, they have no free will.",sp=0},{t="The Deathstalker Ambush",b="Three Deathstalkers—Rane Yorick, Quinn Yorick, and Erland McKree—scouted northern Silverpine for the Forsaken, seeking to judge the region's threats. As they passed through the Dead Field, the ghouls at Ivar Patch ambushed them. Ivar, now called Ivar the Foul, badly mauled Quinn. With Quinn gravely wounded, Rane and Quinn fortified themselves inside the farm's ruined house, while McKree continued alone toward Malden's Orchard.",sp=1}},faq={{q="What happened to the farm and its owner?",a="The Plague of Undeath struck the farm during the Third War. Ivar, his family, and his workers succumbed and rose as rotting, feral ghouls under the Scourge's lingering sway.",al={"ivar patch history","who was ivar","what happened to ivar"},it="history"},{q="Why are there Deathstalkers hiding inside the house?",a="Deathstalkers Rane and Quinn Yorick were scouting Silverpine Forest to gauge regional threats. Ghouls ambushed them as they passed through, and Ivar the Foul severely injured Quinn, forcing them to shelter inside the ruined farmhouse.",al={"deathstalkers at ivar patch","why are forsaken here","quinn yorick farmhouse"},it="people"},{q="Are the ghouls here part of the Forsaken?",a="No. The ghouls roaming the pumpkin fields are mindless Scourge remnants created by the Plague of Undeath. They lack free will and attack living travelers and Forsaken on sight.",al={"are these ghouls forsaken","scourge in ivar patch","why are ghouls hostile"},it="hostile"},{q="Where is the Ivar Patch located?",a="Ivar Patch lies in northern Silverpine Forest, north of the Dead Field and just south of the road toward Malden's Orchard.",al={"ivar patch location","where is ivar patch"},it="place",gp=true},{q="What is the Ivar Patch?",a="The Ivar Patch was once a prosperous pumpkin farm in northern Silverpine Forest, filled with busy fields, farmhands, and servants. Today, it lies ruined and overgrown, its fertile soil spoiled by the Third War and overrun by feral undead.",al={"what is ivar patch","ivar patch lore","ivar farm"},it="place",add="b4d2b280"},{q="Why is it called the Ivar Patch?",a="The land takes its name from its former owner, Ivar. He once managed the estate and employed numerous servants to tend the pumpkins, but during the Third War he fell to the plague, rising as the foul ghoul who now haunts the grounds.",al={"who was ivar","why called ivar patch","ivar name origin"},it="name",add="ef89f0e6"},{q="Is the Ivar Patch dangerous?",a="It is extremely hazardous. Mindless, ravenous ghouls wander the blighted pumpkins, attacking any living or undead travelers who trespass. Even trained Forsaken scouts like the Deathstalkers were ambushed and badly wounded trying to pass through.",al={"ivar patch danger","is ivar patch safe","threats at ivar patch"},it="danger",add="a1ef5b14"}},ang={["race:Undead"]="As an undead, you see in the ruined farm a reminder of the Plague of Undeath that tore Lordaeron apart, and of the mindless fate the Forsaken narrowly escaped.",["faction:Horde"]="As a member of the Horde, you help secure the northern roadway between Silverpine Forest and the safety of Undercity by culling the ravenous ghouls at the patch."},kw={"deathstalkers","ghouls","ivar patch","ivar the foul","pumpkin patch","quinn yorick","rane yorick","silverpine forest"},rel={"quest:425","quest:1886","npc:quinn-yorick","zone:silverpine","subzone:dead-field","subzone:malden-s-orchard","topic:plague-of-undeath","topic:scourge"},src={"Ivar Patch"}}
E["subzone:malden-s-orchard"] = {t="subzone",n="Malden's Orchard",z="silverpine",s="Black worgs prowl Malden's Orchard in northern Silverpine Forest. The ruined farmstead takes its name from Malden, the human farmer who fled during the Scourge invasion of Lordaeron. Its dark evergreen trees grow wild, and a crumbling cottage once sheltered a Forsaken scout cut off from his unit.",h="Black worgs prowl Malden's Orchard in northern Silverpine Forest.",sec={{t="A Blighted Harvest",b="Malden's Orchard once sent fresh fruit to the towns of Lordaeron. Malden, a human farmer, tended the land before the Third War. When the Scourge swept through the kingdom, he abandoned the farm and fled the plague. Since then, Silverpine's dark mists have closed over the orchard. Its evergreen trees go unpruned, and fruit rots on blighted boughs. Wild predators have claimed the plot.",sp=0},{t="Trapped in the Cottage",b="Black worgs hunt through the overgrown orchard and make the route through northern Silverpine dangerous. Erland McKree, a scout sent to survey the area for the Deathstalkers, was overwhelmed by the beasts. He remained trapped for days in Malden's dilapidated cottage. Forsaken reinforcements finally broke through the pack and escorted him back to his fellow scouts at the Ivar Patch.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Who was Malden?",a="Malden was a human farmer who lived here before Lordaeron fell. When the Scourge invaded during the Third War, he abandoned the orchard and fled for his life.",al={"malden lore","who owned the orchard","who is malden"},it="identity"},{q="Why is the orchard full of worgs?",a="Wild black worgs from Silverpine Forest claimed the dense grove and abandoned yard as pack territory after no living tenders remained to defend the farmstead.",al={"why are there worgs here","malden orchard dogs","worg infestation"},it="threat"},{q="Who is trapped inside the cottage?",a="Deathstalker Erland McKree was trapped inside the cottage. Sent to survey the area for the Forsaken, he was ambushed by the orchard's worgs and stayed inside until aid arrived.",al={"cottage scout","who is in the house","deathstalker in the cabin"},it="people"},{q="Does anyone harvest fruit from this orchard now?",a="No one tends the dark trees, and their fruit rots on the branches amid the decay spreading through Silverpine Forest.",al={"is the fruit edible","malden's orchard harvest","can you pick fruit"},it="today"},{q="What is Malden's Orchard?",a="Malden's Orchard is an overgrown fruit grove and homestead nestled in northern Silverpine Forest. Once a quiet farmstead tended by living human hands, its dark, evergreen trees now stand neglected, their unpicked fruit left to rot amid the gloom of the woods.",al={"what is maldens orchard","maldens orchard silverpine","about maldens orchard"},it="place",add="b372998e"},{q="What happened to Malden's Orchard?",a="When the Scourge swept across Lordaeron, its original owner was forced to abandon the cottage and flee for his life. The farmstead fell into silent disrepair until vicious black worgs overran the grove, turning the once-peaceful orchard into a savage den.",al={"history of maldens orchard","maldens orchard lore","what happened here maldens orchard"},it="history",add="ad803607"},{q="Why was Malden's Orchard abandoned?",a="The farm was abandoned during the Third War when the Plague of Undeath and the Scourge invaded Lordaeron, forcing its master to flee. Left without caretakers, the wilderness reclaimed the land and hungry predators moved in to claim the grounds.",al={"why is maldens orchard ruined","why was it abandoned maldens orchard","who ruined maldens orchard"},it="ruin",add="87e05548"},{q="Is Malden's Orchard dangerous?",a="Yes. A dense pack of ravenous black worgs has completely overrun the orchard. Their presence is lethal enough that even a trained Forsaken Deathstalker was pinned down inside the lone cottage for days, unable to step outside without facing certain death.",al={"maldens orchard danger","is it safe at maldens orchard","threats at maldens orchard"},it="danger",add="a9b40d5a"},{q="Why is it called Malden's Orchard?",a="The orchard is named after its former human owner, Malden, who tended the trees and lived in the small homestead here before the Scourge tore through the kingdom.",al={"why is it called maldens orchard","maldens orchard name origin","who named maldens orchard"},it="name",add="a14ed0b8"}},ang={["race:Undead"]="For you, the orchard recalls human ruin. Deathstalker scouts must secure this contested part of northern Silverpine against feral beasts.",["faction:Horde"]="If you travel south from the Sepulcher or the Tirisfal border, tread carefully near the orchard. Aggressive worg packs make their home on the farm."},kw={"cottage","erland mckree","ivar patch","malden","malden's orchard","maldens orchard","silverpine","worgs"},rel={"zone:silverpine","subzone:ivar-patch","npc:quinn-yorick","quest:1886","topic:forsaken","topic:scourge","topic:lordaeron","topic:plague-of-undeath"},src={"Malden's Orchard"}}
E["subzone:north-tide-s-hollow"] = {t="subzone",n="North Tide's Hollow",z="silverpine",s="Moonrage worgen haunt North Tide's Hollow, a clearing just north of the Sepulcher in Silverpine Forest. Loyal to the rogue Archmage Arugal, they use it as a base to stalk the coastal woods.",h="Moonrage worgen haunt North Tide's Hollow, a clearing just north of the Sepulcher in Silverpine Forest.",sec={{t="A Feral Foothold",b="North Tide's Hollow lies in dense timber north of the Forsaken settlement of the Sepulcher. The savage Moonrage pack holds the hollow, worgen brought into Lordaeron by Archmage Arugal's reckless sorcery. Crude shelters scattered through the hollow offer the hardy beasts little more than bare necessities, yet give them a forward staging ground close to Forsaken travel routes.",sp=0},{t="Under Shadowfang's Shadow",b="The Moonrage worgen answer to a sinister will from Shadowfang Keep, unlike ordinary wilderness predators. Near the western shoreline and Silverpine's main road, they menace Forsaken couriers and patrols moving through the region.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Where is North Tide's Hollow?",a="North Tide's Hollow lies in western Silverpine Forest, just north of the Forsaken outpost of the Sepulcher and near the coastal bluffs.",al={"north tides hollow location","where is north tides hollow","hollow location"},gp=true},{q="What creatures inhabit North Tide's Hollow?",a="Moonrage worgen, supernatural wolf-beasts bound to Archmage Arugal's madness, inhabit the hollow.",al={"who lives here","north tides hollow enemies","mobs in north tides hollow"},it="residents"},{q="Why do the worgen live in crude camps here?",a="Though vicious and wild, the Moonrage pack is cunning enough to organize basic camps. The worgen are resilient and hardened, needing only primitive shelters and necessities to endure Lordaeron's wilderness.",al={"worgen camps","why do worgen have tents"}},{q="Who controls the worgen in this area?",a="The Moonrage worgen in North Tide's Hollow serve Archmage Arugal, who summoned worgen into Lordaeron and commands them from Shadowfang Keep.",al={"who leads the worgen","worgen master"},it="in_charge"},{q="What is North Tide's Hollow?",a="North Tide's Hollow is a rugged wilderness hollow located in Silverpine Forest, situated just north of the Sepulcher. It is known primarily as a wild encampment and haunting ground for the ferocious Moonrage worgen that roam the pine woods under the influence of Archmage Arugal.",al={"what is north tides hollow","north tide hollow info","tell me about north tides hollow"},it="place",add="8d98927f"},{q="Is North Tide's Hollow dangerous?",a="Yes, it is extremely dangerous for lone travelers. The hollow is overrun by savage Moonrage worgen who attack any interlopers on sight. These feral beasts have established crude camps throughout the area, making the hollow a perilous threshold for anyone journeying north of the Sepulcher.",al={"is north tides hollow safe","how dangerous is north tides hollow","north tide hollow threats"},it="danger",add="ebea75f3"}},ang={["race:Undead"]="Near the Sepulcher, the Moonrage pack in North Tide's Hollow threatens Forsaken sovereignty and logistical lines in Silverpine."},kw={"arugal","moonrage","north tide's hollow","sepulcher","silverpine forest","worgen"},rel={"zone:silverpine","subzone:sepulcher","topic:worgen","npc:arugal"},src={"North Tide's Hollow"}}
E["subzone:north-tide-s-run"] = {t="subzone",n="North Tide's Run",z="silverpine",s="Cold surf breaks along North Tide's Run, Silverpine Forest's northwestern shore. A half-sunken ship marks the strand, where young tauren druids come to test themselves in the sea.",h="Cold surf breaks along North Tide's Run, Silverpine Forest's northwestern shore.",sec={{t="A Lonely Coast",b="North Tide's Run follows Silverpine Forest's northwestern edge beside the Great Sea. Cold sand meets pounding surf, and a partly sunken ship rests tilted in the shallows near the beach.",sp=0},{t="Waters of the Sea Lion",b="Young tauren druids come to North Tide's Run on pilgrimage along the path of Cenarius. They dive for relics lost to the waves, testing their breath and endurance as they seek the blessing of the aquatic form.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What is North Tide's Run?",a="North Tide's Run is Silverpine Forest's northwestern shore, along the Great Sea. Its quiet strand is marked by a half-sunken ship and tidal waters.",al={"north tides run","where is north tides run","what is this beach"},it="place"},{q="Why do druids come to North Tide's Run?",a="Young tauren druids come to North Tide's Run on pilgrimage. They brave the depths to recover lost pendant fragments and earn the power to take aquatic form.",al={"druid quest silverpine beach","aquatic form silverpine","why tauren here"},it="purpose"},{q="What is the sunken ship in the water?",a="A partly sunken vessel rests in the shallows just off the sand. Travelers along the coast can use it as a landmark.",al={"shipwreck north tides run","sunken boat silverpine beach","ship wreck"},it="history"},{q="Is North Tide's Run dangerous?",a="North Tide's Run is relatively quiet compared to the haunted heartlands of Silverpine, but it is far from harmless. The cold waters of the Great Sea conceal hidden depths and dangerous marine life, while wandering beasts roam the desolate shoreline. You will find no friendly shelter here, leaving travelers largely exposed to the perils of the northern coast.",al={"is north tides run safe","north tides run danger","threats north tides run"},it="danger",add="7c1c9724"}},ang={["class:Druid"]="As a tauren druid, you face a rite of passage on this cold coast, where submerged relics form part of your trial to master the sea lion form.",["race:Tauren"]="As a young tauren, you travel far from Mulgore's warm plains to North Tide's Run, one of the few places in Lordaeron on your early spiritual journey."},kw={"aquatic form","druid trial","great sea","north tide's run","shipwreck","silverpine forest"},rel={"zone:silverpine","quest:31","topic:druid","topic:tauren","topic:horde"},src={"North Tide's Run"}}
E["subzone:olsen-s-farthing"] = {t="subzone",n="Olsen's Farthing",z="silverpine",s="Olsen's Farthing lies in ruin beside Silverpine Forest's main trade road. Since the Third War, reanimated thralls have overrun its fields.",h="Olsen's Farthing lies in ruin beside Silverpine Forest's main trade road.",sec={{t="A Blighted Homestead",b="Olsen's Farthing once worked the fields beside Silverpine's main trade road. Now weeds choke the farmland, and broken buildings mark the loss of the farmstead. Undead thralls roam the grounds, bound to serve and raid under Thule Ravenclaw. Travelers who stray too close risk being slaughtered.",sp=0},{t="The Grasp of Ravenclaw",b="Thule Ravenclaw commands the undead haunting Olsen's Farthing. The powerful necromancer works from Fenris Isle, at the center of Lake Lordamere, where dark sorcery lets him raise and enslave the dead from the surrounding countryside. His servants reach across Olsen's Farthing and threaten the Forsaken as they seek to secure northern Silverpine Forest.",sp=1,bt={"q437.6"}}},faq={{q="What was Olsen's Farthing before the Third War?",a="Before the Third War, Olsen's Farthing was a productive farm beside Silverpine Forest's main trade road. It supported local commerce and fed Lordaeron's settlements before the kingdom fell to the Scourge.",al={"olsens farthing history","what was this place","who lived at olsens farthing"},it="history"},{q="Why is the farm infested with undead?",a="The farm was destroyed during the Third War, and Thule Ravenclaw seized its remains. He raised the dead as thralls and raiders to terrorize travelers along the road.",al={"why are there undead here","who controls the undead at olsens farthing","ravenclaw slaves silverpine"},it="ruin"},{q="Who is Thule Ravenclaw?",a="Thule Ravenclaw is a dangerous necromancer aligned with the Scourge. From his stronghold on Fenris Isle, he directs undead incursions across Silverpine Forest.",al={"who is thule ravenclaw","thule ravenclaw lore","who commands ravenclaw raiders"},sp=1,bt={"q437.6"}},{q="Does the Horde or Forsaken hold any presence here?",a="Hostile undead loyal to Thule Ravenclaw overrun Olsen's Farthing. Forsaken scouts and Horde travelers alike face hostile ground there.",al={"is olsens farthing horde","do forsaken live at olsens farthing","is there a quest hub here"},it="today"},{q="What is Olsen's Farthing?",a="Olsen's Farthing is a ruined farmstead situated along the trade road running through Silverpine Forest. Once a thriving piece of rural farmland, it has fallen into decay and ruin following the devastation of the Third War.",al={"what is olsens farthing","olsens farthing silverpine","olsen farmstead"},it="place",add="332ece8e"},{q="Who lives at Olsen's Farthing?",a="No living farmers remain. Instead, the grounds are inhabited and overrun by the Ravenclaw undead—slaves and raiders serving the necromancer Thule Ravenclaw, who commands them from nearby Fenris Isle.",al={"who controls olsens farthing","who is at olsen farthing","olsens farthing inhabitants"},it="residents",add="1623e0db"},{q="Is Olsen's Farthing dangerous?",a="Yes. The farmstead poses a severe hazard to any travelers along the road. The undead bound to Thule Ravenclaw ravenously assault anyone who steps into the ruined fields and crumbling farm buildings.",al={"is olsens farthing safe","olsens farthing danger","threats at olsens farthing"},it="danger",add="60f4df25"}},ang={["race:Undead"]="For the Forsaken, Olsen's Farthing recalls the Scourge threat that still seeks to enslave the dead instead of freeing them.",["faction:Horde"]="Clearing the raiders from Olsen's Farthing helps secure the supply road from the Sepulcher northward and the road toward Tirisfal Glades."},kw={"fenris isle","lordaeron farm","olsen's farthing","olsens farthing","ravenclaw raiders","ravenclaw slaves","silverpine forest","thule ravenclaw"},rel={"quest:446","zone:silverpine","subzone:fenris-isle","topic:forsaken","topic:horde","topic:third-war"},src={"Olsen's Farthing"}}
E["subzone:pyrewood-village"] = {t="subzone",n="Pyrewood Village",z="silverpine",s="Isolated Pyrewood Village lies beneath Shadowfang Keep in southern Silverpine Forest. Once part of Gilneas, the settlement was stranded outside the Greymane Wall, and Arugal's curse now haunts its living residents.",h="Isolated Pyrewood Village lies beneath Shadowfang Keep in southern Silverpine Forest.",sec={{t="A Town Severed",b="Pyrewood was once a prosperous Gilnean settlement. After the Second War, King Genn Greymane sealed Gilneas behind the massive Greymane Wall, leaving Pyrewood on the wrong side. Cut off from their homeland, the townsfolk were entirely defenseless as the Scourge crossed Lordaeron during the Third War. They survived the first wave of undead, but their nightmare began when the mage Arugal took refuge in the fortress above.",sp=0},{t="The Moonrage Curse",b="Archmage Arugal unleashed otherworldly beasts from Shadowfang Keep and cursed Pyrewood's living residents. By day, they look like ordinary human villagers and keep their normal faculties as they tend the town hall, blacksmith, and chapel. The village merchants even trade with visiting Alliance travelers. When the sun sets, every resident becomes a savage, bloodthirsty worgen of the Moonrage pack. Anyone left within the village walls is attacked.",sp=1,bt={"q421.5"}}},faq={{q="Why does Pyrewood Village attack me at night?",a="Archmage Arugal of Shadowfang Keep cursed Pyrewood's villagers. By day, they keep their human forms and normal faculties, but each night they become ravenous Moonrage worgen and attack outsiders on sight.",al={"pyrewood hostile at night","pyrewood worgen shift","why are they worgen"},sp=1,it="danger",bt={"q421.5"}},{q="Why is Pyrewood outside the Greymane Wall?",a="King Genn Greymane ordered the Greymane Wall built to seal Gilneas away from the outside world after the Second War. Pyrewood ended up on the wrong side, leaving its residents to fend for themselves.",al={"why outside the wall","is pyrewood gilnean"},it="origin"},{q="Can Alliance players visit Pyrewood safely?",a="Yes, Alliance travelers can visit and trade with the village merchants during daylight. After dark, the entire village transforms into hostile worgen, whatever your faction.",al={"alliance pyrewood friendly","can alliance go to pyrewood","pyrewood vendors"},sp=1,it="ties",bt={"q421.5"}},{q="How does the Horde view Pyrewood?",a="The Forsaken see Pyrewood as an intolerable threat on their southern border. Under agents such as Deathstalker Faerleia, the Horde seeks to assassinate the village's council and sever Pyrewood's ties to Arugal.",al={"forsaken pyrewood","horde hostile pyrewood","deathstalker faerleia pyrewood"},it="conflict"},{q="What is Pyrewood Village?",a="Pyrewood Village is a human settlement nestled in southern Silverpine Forest, situated just outside the Greymane Wall and beneath Shadowfang Keep. Originally part of Gilneas, it was cut off from its homeland when King Greymane sealed the borders. The village miraculously survived the Scourge during the Third War, maintaining its town hall, chapel, and blacksmith. By day, its hardy human inhabitants carry on their daily lives and welcome friendly Alliance travelers, even as dark magic looms over them from the keep above.",al={"what is pyrewood","pyrewood village lore","pyrewood info"},it="place",add="be6317a5"},{q="What happened to Pyrewood Village?",a="Pyrewood was stranded when King Genn Greymane built his massive wall, leaving the village outside Gilneas. During the Third War, the village endured the onslaught of the Scourge, standing as one of the few surviving human enclaves in Lordaeron. However, true tragedy struck when Archmage Arugal unleashed his summoned worgen upon Baron Silverlaine's nearby keep. After claiming the stronghold, Arugal placed a terrible curse upon Pyrewood's surviving villagers, binding their fates to his mad experiments.",al={"history of pyrewood","what happened at pyrewood","pyrewood history"},it="history",add="9ba6a911"},{q="Who lives in Pyrewood Village?",a="Pyrewood is inhabited by its surviving Gilnean townsfolk and governed by a local ruling council. Cut off from Gilneas when the Wall closed, the villagers now govern themselves under desperate circumstances. Tragically, their true master is Archmage Arugal, who watches from Shadowfang Keep. By day, craftsmen, guards, and councilors run the town in human guise, but come nightfall, they all succumb to the worgen curse.",al={"who leads pyrewood","pyrewood residents","who controls pyrewood village"},it="residents",add="fda3e589"}},ang={["faction:Alliance"]="Pyrewood is a tragic remnant of living humanity in Lordaeron. Its people trade with travelers by day, then succumb to a horrific curse each night.",["faction:Horde"]="The Forsaken see Pyrewood as a lingering pocket of hostile humans and monstrous worgen serving Archmage Arugal on the border of their lands."},kw={"arugal","greymane wall","moonrage","pyrewood","pyrewood village","shadowfang","silverpine"},rel={"zone:shadowfang","npc:arugal","zone:silverpine","subzone:greymane-wall","subzone:ambermill","topic:worgen","quest:452","npc:deathstalker-faerleia"},src={"Pyrewood Village"}}
E["subzone:sepulcher"] = {t="subzone",n="Sepulcher",z="silverpine",s="The Forsaken hold the Sepulcher above Silverpine Forest’s western coast. Once a Lordaeron graveyard and burial crypt, it is now a fortified Horde refuge amid threats from across the region.",h="The Forsaken hold the Sepulcher above Silverpine Forest’s western coast.",sec={{t="A Sanctum in the Fog",b="The Sepulcher crowns the hills above Lordaeron’s western coast. You find an old cemetery and stone crypt beside the western road, now held by the Forsaken. Since the Third War, they have made its grounds and ancient vault a vital outpost. Danger presses from every side: feral worgen stalk the south, Scourge remnants wander east, and Kirin Tor wizards watch from Ambermill. For travelers crossing Silverpine, the Sepulcher offers shelter, supplies, and a place of command.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What was the Sepulcher before the Forsaken moved in?",a="Before the Third War and Lordaeron’s fall, the Sepulcher was a roadside cemetery and stone crypt where local villagers buried their dead.",al={"sepulcher history","what was the sepulcher","who built the sepulcher"},it="history"},{q="Why is the Sepulcher so vital to the Forsaken?",a="The Sepulcher is the Forsaken’s only fortified hub in Silverpine Forest. From there, their scouts and commanders watch for Dalaran mages, Scourge holdouts, and worgen spreading near Shadowfang Keep.",al={"why is sepulcher important","forsaken in silverpine","role of the sepulcher"},it="purpose"},{q="Are travelers belonging to other Horde races welcome here?",a="Yes. Forsaken deathguards, merchants, and apothecaries manage and inhabit the base, but it is an official Horde refuge where orcs, trolls, and tauren can rest and trade as they pass through the region.",al={"can orcs go to sepulcher","is the sepulcher horde friendly","horde at sepulcher"},it="residents"},{q="What threats surround the Sepulcher?",a="Hostile forces surround the Sepulcher. Scourge roam to the east, the Kirin Tor hold Ambermill to the southeast, and fierce worgen stalk the woods to the south.",al={"threats to sepulcher","enemies in silverpine","what attacks sepulcher"},it="threat"},{q="What is the Sepulcher?",a="The Sepulcher is the primary Forsaken settlement and stronghold in Silverpine Forest. Nestled in the hills overlooking the western Lordaeronian coastline, it serves as the operational hub for Horde efforts throughout the region, offering a safe harbor complete with scouts, merchants, and trainers.",al={"what is sepulcher","sepulcher silverpine","what is the sepulcher"},it="place",add="70fd5666"},{q="Why is it called the Sepulcher?",a="Before the Forsaken fortified it as an outpost, the site was simply a graveyard and crypt alongside the Silverpine road. A sepulcher is a tomb or burial vault, and the Forsaken kept the fitting name when they converted the ancient crypt into their military base.",al={"why is it called sepulcher","sepulcher name meaning","why called sepulcher"},it="name",add="2b930170"},{q="Is the Sepulcher dangerous?",a="Within its perimeter, the Sepulcher is a secure haven guarded by Forsaken sentries. Outside its boundaries, however, the area is perilous. Hostile worgen prowl to the south, Scourge lurk to the east, and Kirin Tor agents watch from the southeast, making the outpost an isolated refuge in hostile territory.",al={"is the sepulcher safe","danger sepulcher","is sepulcher safe"},it="danger",add="d7b2f06c"}},ang={["race:Undead"]="The Sepulcher directs the Forsaken’s struggle to pacify Silverpine Forest, including operations against lingering Scourge loyalists, Kirin Tor remnants, and feral worgen.",["faction:Horde"]="If you travel south from Tirisfal Glades, the Sepulcher is the only reliable Horde refuge, repair stop, and flight hub for miles."},kw={"crypt","deathguard","forsaken outpost","graveyard","sepulcher","silverpine forest","silverpine sepulcher"},rel={"zone:silverpine","topic:forsaken","topic:horde","topic:scourge","topic:worgen","topic:third-war","quest:446"},src={"Sepulcher"}}
E["subzone:shadowfang-keep"] = {t="subzone",n="Shadowfang Keep",z="silverpine",s="On a rugged bluff above Pyrewood Village, Shadowfang Keep broods over southern Silverpine Forest. Once Silverlaine Keep, it fell to worgen summoned during the Third War and became the lair of the mad Archmage Arugal, haunted by slain nobles and overrun by wolf-beasts.",h="On a rugged bluff above Pyrewood Village, Shadowfang Keep broods over southern Silverpine Forest.",sec={{t="Fall of the Silverlaines",b="Before the Third War, Baron Silverlaine ruled nearby Pyrewood Village from his ancestral seat, Silverlaine Keep. When the Scourge swept through Lordaeron, desperate wizards sought forbidden means to stem the undead tide. Drawing on Dalaran mage Ur's dimensional research, Archmage Arugal summoned worgen from beyond this world. The savage beasts tore through the Scourge, then escaped control. They rampaged across southern Silverpine and besieged the keep, killing Baron Silverlaine, his family, and the defenders under Commander Springvale. Guilt and grief broke Arugal's sanity. He claimed the fortress, renamed it Shadowfang Keep, and called the monstrous predators his children.",sp=0},{t="A Haunted Bastion",b="Shadowfang Keep is the heart of a growing wolf curse in Silverpine Forest. Arugal dwells in the highest observatory, surrounded by ravenous worgen of the Moonrage and Shadowfang packs. Sinister beasts also prowl the keep, including his massive pet wolf, Fenrus. Below Arugal's sanctum, the restless ghosts of the keep's former lords and household remain trapped in torment. Baron Silverlaine and Commander Springvale are among them, cursed to defend the halls they failed to protect in life. From the walls, Arugal's influence reaches Pyrewood Village and the surrounding woodlands, threatening the neighboring Forsaken who seek to purge the forest of his madness.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What was Shadowfang Keep called before Arugal took over?",a="Before Arugal took it, the fortress was called Silverlaine Keep. It was Baron Silverlaine's ancestral seat, and he governed Pyrewood Village and the surrounding lands.",al={"original name","who used to own shadowfang","silverlaine keep"},it="origin"},{q="Why did Arugal summon the worgen here?",a="During the Third War, the Scourge crushed Dalaran's forces and raised slain wizards into undeath. Despite the Kirin Tor's warnings, Archmage Arugal used the wizard Ur's research to summon worgen from beyond this world. They tore through the Scourge, then turned on the living and ran wild across Silverpine.",al={"why did arugal summon worgen","arugal backstory","how did worgen get here"},it="motive"},{q="Who rules Shadowfang Keep right now?",a="Archmage Arugal holds Shadowfang Keep. Mad with guilt over releasing the monsters, he embraced the worgen as his children and rules from the fortress heights beside his deadly pack.",al={"current master of shadowfang","who lives in shadowfang keep","arugal keep"},it="in_charge"},{q="Why are there ghosts in Shadowfang Keep?",a="The ghosts are Baron Silverlaine, Commander Springvale, and members of the keep's former household. When the worgen swarmed the keep and slaughtered its inhabitants, their spirits remained bound to the stone, cursed to wander its ruined corridors.",al={"silverlaine ghost","commander springvale ghost","undead inside shadowfang"},it="threat"},{q="What connection does Pyrewood Village have to the keep?",a="Pyrewood Village lies in the keep's shadow and was governed by Baron Silverlaine. Under Arugal's creeping influence, villagers were afflicted with the worgen curse: they appeared human by day and became rabid beasts beneath the night sky.",al={"pyrewood and shadowfang","pyrewood village curse"},sp=1,it="ties",bt={"q421.5"}},{q="What is Shadowfang Keep?",a="Shadowfang Keep is a haunted stronghold perched high on a rocky bluff in southern Silverpine Forest, looming directly over Pyrewood Village near the Greymane Wall. Originally the ancestral seat of Baron Silverlaine, the fortress was overrun by feral worgen summoned during the Third War. Today, it stands as the secluded lair of the mad Archmage Arugal, guarded by ravenous beastmen, spectral defenders, and twisted sorcery.",al={"what is shadowfang keep","shadowfang keep lore","shadowfang castle"},it="place",add="b733cd78"},{q="What happened at Shadowfang Keep?",a="During the Third War, Archmage Arugal sought to repel the Scourge by using the research of Ur to summon extra-dimensional worgen into Azeroth. Though the beasts slaughtered the undead, they quickly ran rampant across Silverpine and laid siege to Baron Silverlaine's stronghold. The worgen butchered the baron, his family, and his garrison. Driven mad by guilt and horror, Arugal embraced the beasts as his own 'children,' claimed the fallen keep, and renamed it Shadowfang.",al={"shadowfang keep history","what happened to silverlaine keep","fall of shadowfang"},it="history",add="cc8ad05a"},{q="Why is Shadowfang Keep ruined?",a="The fortress fell into ruin when Arugal's rampaging worgen besieged and overwhelmed its defenders, slaughtering Baron Silverlaine and his entire household. Rather than restoring the noble estate, the deranged archmage allowed the halls to crumble into darkness, filling the courtyard and ramparts with savage beasts and the tormented ghosts of the slain nobles who perished during the massacre.",al={"why is shadowfang keep ruined","shadowfang keep destroyed","why is it abandoned"},it="ruin",add="ee32dcde"},{q="Is Shadowfang Keep dangerous?",a="Shadowfang Keep is exceptionally lethal. Behind its iron gates lurk packs of ferocious worgen, Arugal's colossal pet wolf Fenrus, and bloodthirsty cultists. In addition to the living beasts, the restless, vengeful spirits of Baron Silverlaine and his slain soldiers haunt the halls, while Archmage Arugal commands deadly arcane curses from atop the castle ramparts.",al={"is shadowfang dangerous","shadowfang keep dangers","how dangerous is shadowfang"},it="danger",add="5c468b05"},{q="Why is it called Shadowfang Keep?",a="Originally known as Silverlaine Keep after its ruling noble, the fortress was renamed Shadowfang Keep by Archmage Arugal after his summoned worgen overran it. He bestowed the name in honor of the savage, shadowy wolf-beasts he adopted as his beloved children and the dark packs that now stalk its halls.",al={"shadowfang keep name","why is it named shadowfang","how did shadowfang get its name"},it="name",add="26793205"}},ang={["faction:Horde"]="For the Forsaken, Arugal's worgen are an unpredictable menace on the doorstep of the Undercity's outer territory in Silverpine, and demand swift extermination.",["class:Mage"]="As a mage, Shadowfang Keep is a grim reminder of Kirin Tor arrogance and the disaster of delving into extra-dimensional summoning without restraint."},kw={"arugal","fenrus","pyrewood","shadowfang","silverlaine","silverpine","springvale","worgen"},rel={"npc:arugal","zone:silverpine","npc:baron-silverlaine","npc:commander-springvale","subzone:pyrewood-village","topic:worgen","quest:1014","subzone:greymane-wall"},src={"Shadowfang Keep"}}
E["subzone:shining-strand"] = {t="subzone",n="Shining Strand",z="silverpine",s="Along eastern Silverpine, Shining Strand follows Lordamere Lake south from the Ruins of Lordaeron toward Alterac's rugged foothills. Vile Fin murlocs hold settlements in its shallows, making the shore dangerous for unseasoned travelers.",h="Along eastern Silverpine, Shining Strand follows Lordamere Lake south from the Ruins of Lordaeron toward...",sec={{t="A Contested Coastline",b="Shining Strand follows Silverpine Forest's eastern edge beside the misty waters of Lordamere Lake. Several aggressive Vile Fin murloc settlements line the shallows, threatening anyone who travels the lake road. Feral worgen roam the deep woods behind the shore.",sp=0},{t="Alchemical Harvest",b="Royal Apothecary Society attention reached Shining Strand and its neighboring waters. The late Apothecary Berard recorded unusual hardened tumors harvested from local Vile Fin murlocs. He theorized their corrupted anatomy could make the tumors a valuable catalyst for concocting a new plague for Sylvanas Windrunner's fledgling nation.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Where is the Shining Strand located?",a="Shining Strand runs along Silverpine Forest's eastern shore, beside Lordamere Lake. It stretches south from the Ruins of Lordaeron to the rugged hills separating Silverpine from the Alterac Mountains.",al={"shining strand location","where is shining strand","silverpine coast"},it="place",gp=true},{q="What threats are found along the Shining Strand?",a="Vile Fin murlocs hold several settlements along the shore and attack unwary travelers. Feral worgen prowl the Silverpine woods beyond the strand.",al={"shining strand monsters","what is on shining strand","shining strand enemies"},it="threat"},{q="Why is the Royal Apothecary Society interested in this area?",a="The Royal Apothecary Society is interested because the late Apothecary Berard documented hardened tumors in local Vile Fin murlocs, with unique physiological traits. He theorized the growths could serve as a catalyst for concocting a new plague.",al={"apothecary berard","shining strand plague","new plague tumor"},it="purpose"},{q="Who are the Vile Fin?",a="The Vile Fin are the murloc tribe whose settlements line Shining Strand, making the lakeshore dangerous for unseasoned travelers.",al={"where are murlocs silverpine","vile fin location","shining strand murlocs"},it="residents"},{q="What is the Shining Strand?",a="The Shining Strand is the eastern shoreline of Silverpine Forest along the waters of Lordamere Lake. It extends southward from the outskirts of the Ruins of Lordaeron down to the jagged hills separating Silverpine from the Alterac Mountains.",al={"what is shining strand","shining strand lore","where is the strand"},it="place",add="1e20c8b8"},{q="What happened at the Shining Strand?",a="The shoreline is dominated by settlements of the Vile Fin murloc tribe, making it a treacherous stretch for travelers, while feral worgen prowl the woods of Silverpine beyond it.",al={"shining strand history","what happened at the strand"},it="history",add="59cd2470"},{q="Is the Shining Strand dangerous?",a="Yes. Aggressive Vile Fin murlocs hold settlements along the shore and raid anyone who strays near the water, and feral worgen roam the nearby woods.",al={"is shining strand dangerous","shining strand dangers"},it="danger",add="6739e2d5"}},ang={["race:Undead"]="The Royal Apothecary Society studies the Vile Fin murlocs of Shining Strand in hopes of concocting a new plague.",["faction:Horde"]="Lordamere Lake's shore links Silverpine's northern approaches with passages toward the Alterac Mountains, though the strand is perilous."},kw={"apothecary berard","dawning isles","lordamere lake","shining strand","silverpine forest","vile fin","worgen"},rel={"zone:silverpine","subzone:lordamere-lake","subzone:dawning-isles","quest:367","topic:forsaken","topic:murloc","topic:worgen","zone:alterac"},src={"Shining Strand"}}
E["subzone:skittering-dark"] = {t="subzone",n="Skittering Dark",z="silverpine",s="In western Silverpine, Skittering Dark lies abandoned beneath a web of danger. Giant spiders fill the mine and nearby woods, hunting unwary beasts and travelers.",h="In western Silverpine, Skittering Dark lies abandoned beneath a web of danger.",sec={{t="A Webbed Hollow",b="The Skittering Dark lies east of North Tide's Run, where the western coast meets the hills. Once a working mine, its shafts now lie choked with cobwebs and serve as a sprawling nest for giant spiders. Krethis haunts the shadowed woods outside, while the spiders hunt anything that strays too close.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What is the Skittering Dark?",a="Skittering Dark is an abandoned mine in western Silverpine Forest, overrun by giant spiders. Webbing and predatory spiders fill the cavern network and the surrounding trees.",al={"skittering dark mine","what is this mine","spider cave silverpine"},it="place"},{q="Who leads the spiders in the mine?",a="No single ruler of the brood is known. Krethis Shadowspinner is the most feared spider, a rare and dangerous weaver that prowls in and around the mine.",al={"spider boss","skittering dark boss","matriarch"},it="leader"},{q="Where is the Skittering Dark located?",a="Skittering Dark lies in western Silverpine Forest, against the hills just east of North Tide's Run.",al={"skittering dark location","how to find skittering dark"},it="place",gp=true},{q="Who lives in the Skittering Dark?",a="The mine and surrounding hollow are overrun by giant spiders. They lurk in dark crevices and spin thick webs across the rocky slopes and tunnels. A formidable rare spider named Krethis Shadowspinner is also known to prowl in and around the mine.",al={"who lives in skittering dark","skittering dark inhabitants","what creatures live in skittering dark"},it="residents",add="958edcba"},{q="Is the Skittering Dark dangerous?",a="Extremely dangerous. The aggressive spiders will ambush anyone foolish enough to draw near their nests, dragging unwary prey into their webs deep inside the old mine shafts.",al={"how dangerous is skittering dark","is skittering dark dangerous","danger of skittering dark"},it="danger",add="040a6057"},{q="Why is the mine in the Skittering Dark abandoned?",a="The mine was once worked before the plague and war devastated Lordaeron, but whatever mortal enterprise once extracted ore here collapsed long ago. Left completely unattended during the kingdom's fall, the subterranean shafts and shadowed tunnels offered a fertile, secluded breeding ground for monstrous arachnids, completely driving out any lingering industry.",al={"why is skittering dark abandoned","who mined skittering dark","why did miners leave skittering dark"},it="ruin",add="ecb7b94e"},{q="Why is it called the Skittering Dark?",a="The name reflects both the grim nature of the abandoned shaft and the ceaseless rustle of the swarm within. Beneath the perpetual gloom of Silverpine's shadowed hills and cavern walls, the only constant sound is the chittering and scuttling of thousands of spider legs moving through the dark.",al={"why is it called skittering dark","skittering dark name origin","how did skittering dark get its name"},it="name",add="0b1ef10a"}},ang={["faction:Horde"]="As a Horde traveler in Silverpine, watch for spiders that ambush unwary prey straying from the surrounding woods into their webbed dens."},kw={"krethis","mine","north tide's run","silverpine","skittering dark","spider"},rel={"zone:silverpine","subzone:north-tide-s-run","topic:worgen","topic:forsaken"},src={"Skittering Dark"}}
E["subzone:south-tide-s-run"] = {t="subzone",n="South Tide's Run",z="silverpine",s="South Tide's Run follows Silverpine Forest's southwestern edge beside the cold Great Sea. These damp shores border the forested interior and form the southern counterpart to North Tide's Run.",h="South Tide's Run follows Silverpine Forest's southwestern edge beside the cold Great Sea.",sec={{t="The Western Shore",b="Along Silverpine Forest's southwestern edge, the Great Sea meets a desolate shore. The eastern roads lead toward the Greymane Wall under the forest's protection, but this open coastline takes the western tides. The bleak stretch remains largely untouched by the settlements inland.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Where is South Tide's Run located?",a="South Tide's Run runs along Silverpine Forest's southwestern coast beside the open Great Sea.",al={"where is south tides run","south tides run location","south tide run map"},it="place",gp=true},{q="How does South Tide's Run differ from North Tide's Run?",a="Both beaches trace Silverpine Forest's western shore. South Tide's Run covers the southern coast, while North Tide's Run follows the northwest near the border with Tirisfal Glades.",al={"north tides run vs south tides run","difference between tide runs"}},{q="Are there any settlements along South Tide's Run?",a="No major towns or outposts stand along the beach. Most Forsaken activity stays inland near the main thoroughfares, leaving the shoreline isolated.",al={"towns in south tides run","who lives in south tides run"},it="residents"},{q="What is South Tide's Run?",a="South Tide's Run is the southwestern coastal stretch of Silverpine Forest, running alongside the waters of the Great Sea. Together with North Tide's Run to the north, it forms the western shoreline of the region.",al={"what is south tides run","south tides run info","south tide run"},it="place",add="c53efa4c"},{q="Why is it called South Tide's Run?",a="It takes its name from its position along Silverpine Forest's coast, serving as the southern counterpart to North Tide's Run along the edge of the Great Sea.",al={"why south tides run","south tides run name meaning","south tide run name"},it="name",add="d867ddea"}},ang={["race:Undead"]="As an Undead, you stand on a wild southwestern coast far from the Sepulcher's protection, an empty frontier the Forsaken rarely tread."},kw={"great sea","silverpine coast","silverpine forest","south tide's run","south tides run"},rel={"subzone:north-tide-s-run","zone:silverpine"},src={"South Tide's Run"}}
E["subzone:valgan-s-field"] = {t="subzone",n="Valgan's Field",z="silverpine",s="Worgen roam Valgan's Field, a ruined farm overlooking Lordamere Lake in northern Silverpine Forest. Archmage Arugal unleashed the Moonrage pack, and the Forsaken now seek his abandoned research there.",h="Worgen roam Valgan's Field, a ruined farm overlooking Lordamere Lake in northern Silverpine Forest.",sec={{t="A Ruined Homestead",b="Valgan's Field lies west of the Shining Strand and north of the nearby river, with Lordamere Lake beyond its ruined farmstead. The wheat farm once prospered, until the Scourge swept through Lordaeron and forced its owner, Valgan, to flee or die. Left untended, the buildings fell to feral Moonrage worgen prowling down from Shadowfang Keep. Before the Third War, Arugal spent time here and left remnants of his arcane research, which now draw the Forsaken's attention.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who was Valgan?",a="Valgan was the human farmer who owned and worked the homestead before the Third War. When the Scourge swept across northern Lordaeron, Valgan either died or fled into exile, leaving the farm to ruin.",al={"valgan","who is valgan","valgans field history"},it="name"},{q="Why are worgen roaming Valgan's Field?",a="Archmage Arugal summoned the feral Moonrage pack into Silverpine Forest and unleashed the beasts against the Scourge. He quickly lost control as they spread through the forest, and guilt drove him mad.",al={"why are there worgen here","moonrage worgen valgan","who brought the worgen"},it="residents"},{q="Why are the Forsaken interested in this farm?",a="Archmage Arugal lived at the farm before the war and left valuable spellbooks behind. The Forsaken seek the lost writings to understand and counter his terrifying magic.",al={"valgans field quest","why forsaken care about valgans field","arugal spellbook farm"},it="purpose"},{q="What rare threats appear near the farm?",a="Moonrage worgen packs are the farm's chief menace. No other notable threat is known to haunt its fields.",al={"nightlash","rare spawn valgans field","monsters at valgan"},it="threat"},{q="What is Valgan's Field?",a="Valgan's Field is a desolate, abandoned wheat farm situated in northern Silverpine Forest, resting just west of the Shining Strand and east of the main road. Before the plague tore through Lordaeron, it was a peaceful homestead overlooking Lordamere Lake. Today, like much of the forest, it lies overgrown, unkempt, and haunted by deadly predators.",al={"what is valgans field","valgan farm","valgans field silverpine"},it="place",add="5ca486da"},{q="What happened at Valgan's Field?",a="Before the Third War, the archmage Arugal spent time here, leaving behind remnants of his arcane research. When the Scourge swept through Silverpine, the homestead fell into ruin as its owner was driven off or slaughtered. Later, when Arugal unleashed the worgen upon the region from Shadowfang Keep, feral Moonrage worgen overran the fields, claiming the broken farm as their territory.",al={"valgans field history","what happened to valgan farm"},it="history",add="1c9d9eee"},{q="Why is Valgan's Field ruined?",a="The farm was abandoned when the Scourge marched across northern Lordaeron, devastating the rural settlements. Any hope of reclaiming the land vanished when Arugal summoned the otherworldly worgen, whose Moonrage pack infested the fields and made human habitation impossible.",al={"why is valgans field abandoned","why is valgan farm ruined","ruin of valgans field"},it="ruin",add="d73dae69"},{q="Is Valgan's Field dangerous?",a="It is extremely hazardous for lone travelers. The abandoned farmstead is prowled by vicious Moonrage worgen spawned from Arugal's dark magic, and the ravenous pack attacks anyone who strays into the fields.",al={"how dangerous is valgans field","valgans field threats"},it="danger",add="93e0efce"}},ang={["race:Undead"]="For the Forsaken, clearing Valgan's Field is essential to securing the road through Silverpine and recovering Arugal's notes before his monstrous pets spread farther north.",["class:Mage"]="Arugal's abandoned research at the farm warns of the catastrophic perils of unchecked summoning and extraplanar magic."},kw={"arugal","moonrage","shining strand","silverpine forest","valgan","valgan's field","worgen"},rel={"npc:arugal","quest:99","topic:worgen","zone:silverpine","subzone:shining-strand","subzone:lordamere-lake","topic:forsaken","topic:scourge"},src={"Valgan's Field"}}
E["zone:silverpine"] = {t="zone",n="Silverpine Forest",z="silverpine",s="Silverpine Forest lies under Forsaken rule and threat from rival forces along Lordaeron's western coast. The Scourge's plague scars the woods, where worgen, diseased gnolls, and hostile human enclaves endanger travelers.",h="Silverpine Forest lies under Forsaken rule and threat from rival forces along Lordaeron's western coast.",sec={{t="A Haunted Frontier",b="Silverpine Forest lies between Tirisfal Glades and the sealed Greymane Wall. Once a lush wonder of Lordaeron, it has withered since the Third War. Ghostly fog moves among dying, silver-barked pines, and ruined farmsteads lie abandoned to the wilderness. Tirisfal Glades borders the forest to the north, and Lordamere Lake lies along its eastern shore. To the south, the Greymane Wall shuts Gilneas away from the chaos beyond. The Forsaken hold their central outpost at the Sepulcher and struggle to secure the woods from enemies on every side.",sp=0},{t="Rival Enclaves and the Scourge",b="The Forsaken's claim to Silverpine faces challenges from living and undead factions. On Fenris Isle to the east, Thule Ravenclaw leads Scourge remnants and commands plague-addled Rot Hide gnolls that trouble the northern farmlands. In the south, human mages from Dalaran hold the fortified settlement of Ambermill, where they conduct mystical research and oppose Forsaken expansion. At the Sepulcher, the Royal Apothecary Society and High Executor Hadrec wage a brutal campaign against these threats while testing virulent new plagues.",sp=1,bt={"q437.6"}},{t="The Worgen and Shadowfang",b="Shadowfang Keep looms above Silverpine's southwest woods, held by the mad Dalaran archmage Arugal. The keep was once Baron Silverlaine's seat. During the Third War, Arugal summoned wolf-beasts from another dimension to repel the Scourge. The beasts turned on their summoners and spread a lycanthropic curse through the southern woods. By daylight, human villagers in Pyrewood Village appear ordinary and go about their chores. Beneath the night sky, they transform into savage worgen.",sp=1,bt={"q421.5"}}},faq={{q="What is the Greymane Wall at the southern border?",a="The Greymane Wall is a massive stone barrier built by King Genn Greymane to isolate Gilneas from the rest of Lordaeron. When the Scourge ravaged the continent during the Third War, Gilneas shut its gates and refused outside aid, leaving lands north of the wall, including southern Silverpine, to fend for themselves.",al={"why is there a giant wall","greymane wall lore","gate to gilneas"},it="place"},{q="Why do the villagers of Pyrewood Village attack at night?",a="Archmage Arugal's worgen curse afflicts the inhabitants of Pyrewood Village. By day, they keep human form and their daily routines, remaining friendly to the Alliance. When the moon rises, the curse transforms the villagers into savage, bloodthirsty worgen who attack anyone nearby.",al={"pyrewood village mystery","pyrewood worgen","why are pyrewood humans hostile at night"},sp=1,it="conflict",bt={"q421.5"}},{q="Who is Thule Ravenclaw?",a="Thule Ravenclaw is a powerful necromancer serving the Scourge. From Fenris Keep on Fenris Isle in Lordamere Lake, he commands legions of undead and influences the diseased Rot Hide gnolls across eastern Silverpine, threatening the Forsaken's eastern flank.",al={"who leads fenris isle","thule ravenclaw lore","scourge on fenris isle"},sp=1,it="threat",bt={"q437.6"}},{q="Why is Dalaran occupying Ambermill?",a="Wizards of Dalaran led by Archmage Ataeric hold Ambermill. From the village, these human mages monitor Forsaken movements, study the forest's magical afflictions, and seek to contain the nearby worgen outbreak spreading from Shadowfang Keep.",al={"ambermill mages","why is the alliance in ambermill","dalaran in silverpine"},it="threat"},{q="What is the Sepulcher?",a="The Sepulcher is the Forsaken's main military outpost and travel hub in Silverpine Forest. Under High Executor Hadrec, it is the base for Deathguard patrols, Deathstalker scouts, and the Royal Apothecary Society as they fight to secure the forest.",al={"horde town in silverpine","where is the flight path","sepulcher lore"},it="place",nx={14,15}},{q="Can Alliance players quest in Silverpine Forest?",a="Silverpine Forest has no Alliance gathering places or friendly towns; local work is for the Horde alone. Alliance adventurers usually enter the forest while traveling from Southshore to explore Shadowfang Keep or fight hostile Forsaken forces.",al={"is silverpine horde only","alliance quests in silverpine","can alliance go to silverpine"},gp=true},{q="What is Silverpine Forest?",a="Silverpine Forest is a vast, ancient woodland along the rugged western coast of Lordaeron, directly south of Tirisfal Glades and bounded on the east by Lordamere Lake. Once a lush and verdant wood protected by the Alliance, it is now shrouded in ghostly mists, sickly pale pines, and eerie silence broken only by distant howling. The Forsaken hold sway over the north from the Sepulcher, but their claim is constantly contested by Scourge remnants, savage Rot Hide gnolls, Dalaran wizards, and the cursed worgen of Shadowfang Keep.",al={"what is silverpine","tell me about silverpine","silverpine forest lore"},it="place",add="21fc6836",nx={9,10}},{q="What happened at Silverpine Forest?",a="Silverpine once resembled the pristine wilderness of the Hinterlands, but the Third War ruined it. When the Lich King's Scourge swept south, undead armies torched farmsteads, slaughtered the rural population, and tainted the land with the plague of undeath. King Genn Greymane sealed Gilneas behind his massive wall, abandoning northern lands like Pyrewood and Ambermill. To repel the Scourge, Archmage Arugal unleashed savage worgen, but the curse spread out of control. With Lordaeron shattered, the blighted woods became a contested battleground.",al={"silverpine history","what happened here silverpine","fall of silverpine"},it="history",add="01503e92"},{q="Who used to live here before the Forsaken?",a="Before the Third War, Silverpine was inhabited by human farmers, miners, and soldiers of Lordaeron and Gilneas. Southern settlements such as Pyrewood Village and Ambermill were left outside when Gilneas sealed itself behind the Greymane Wall. Fenris Isle housed a bustling Lordaeron military garrison at Fenris Keep. Most of these former inhabitants perished during the Scourge invasion, fled south to the sealed wall, or succumbed to undeath and the worgen curse.",al={"who lived in silverpine before","silverpine former residents","past inhabitants of silverpine"},it="people",add="b9edb2aa"},{q="Why is the forest so dead looking?",a="The forest bears the deep, lingering scars of the Third War. Silverpine marks the southernmost extent where the Scourge's plague of undeath visibly corrupted the flora, draining the vitality from the soil and leaving the ancient silver-barked pines pale, sickly, and shedding blighted needles. With Lordaeron destroyed and Gilneas walled off, no caretakers remained to heal the ravaged groves or tend the scorched cropland, leaving cold mists and rot to settle over the woods.",al={"why is silverpine dying","why does silverpine look dead","blighted trees silverpine"},it="ruin",add="5b2addb4"},{q="Is Silverpine Forest dangerous?",a="Extremely dangerous. Wild predators like blighted bears, giant spiders, and ferocious worgs prowl beneath the trees. Plague-ridden Rot Hide gnolls violently slaughter travelers along the roads, while human mages from Dalaran fortify Ambermill against Horde intrusion. To the south, the feral Moonrage worgen terrorize the valleys under the sway of Archmage Arugal. Outside the fortified sanctuary of the Sepulcher, survival requires constant vigilance.",al={"how dangerous is silverpine","threats in silverpine","is it safe here"},it="danger",add="67376895"},{q="Why did the Horde send me to Silverpine?",a="You were sent south from Tirisfal Glades to reinforce the Forsaken frontier. The Undercity considers Silverpine vital to securing its southern border, but its hold is fragile and stretched thin. High Executor Hadrec and the Deathguard require capable champions to drive back encroaching Scourge necromancers, eliminate hostile gnolls, monitor Dalaran's covert maneuvers, and contain the bloodthirsty worgen threatening to overrun the woodlands.",al={"why am i in silverpine","horde silverpine arrival","why send me here"},it="arrival",add="6dcc337b",nx={13}},{q="Is this still Forsaken land?",a="The Forsaken claim Silverpine as sovereign territory of the Undercity, but their control is heavily contested. While they maintain firm dominion over northern Silverpine and the fortified haven of the Sepulcher, they do not hold undisputed sway over the entire forest. Hostile Rot Hide gnolls rule the eastern waters, Dalaran wizards occupy Ambermill, and Arugal's feral worgen dominate the southwestern reaches.",al={"does forsaken own silverpine","who controls silverpine","forsaken territory silverpine"},it="today",add="ab9ff98b"},{q="Who built the Sepulcher?",a="Before the Third War, the Sepulcher was simply a large, quiet human graveyard and roadside crypt built by the people of Lordaeron to inter their dead along the western highway. Following Lordaeron's fall, the surviving Forsaken seized the burial grounds and refitted the crypt into a fortified military outpost, caravan station, and logistical headquarters for their southern operations.",al={"who made the sepulcher","sepulcher origin","history of the sepulcher"},it="origin",add="858ebaa5"},{q="Why are the Forsaken based at the Sepulcher?",a="Nestled defensibly in the western hills, the Sepulcher offers the Forsaken a natural vantage overlooking the coast and the main road. Positioned between the Scourge in the east, Dalaran to the southeast, and feral worgen to the south, it serves as the only secure outpost where Deathguard patrols and Royal Apothecary researchers can coordinate defenses and protect the route to Tirisfal.",al={"why are forsaken at sepulcher","sepulcher forsaken base why","importance of sepulcher"},it="purpose",add="f51f7d3d"},{q="Who is High Executor Hadrec?",a="High Executor Hadrec is the military commander of Forsaken operations in Silverpine Forest, stationed at the Sepulcher. Stern and pragmatic, he directs the Deathguard and Deathstalker scouts in pacifying the wilderness, uncovering hidden threats, and orchestrating strikes against hostile forces such as Thule Ravenclaw and the Rot Hide gnolls.",al={"hadrec","who is hadrec","high executor hadrec silverpine"},it="in_charge",add="0581536d",nx={17}},{q="Who does High Executor Hadrec answer to?",a="Hadrec answers directly to Lady Sylvanas Windrunner, the Banshee Queen of the Forsaken, and her high command in the Undercity. As a senior officer of the Deathguard, his mandate is to secure the borders of her newborn kingdom and eliminate any power that could compromise Forsaken sovereignty.",al={"who is hadrec's boss","hadrec superior","who does hadrec report to"},it="leader",add="ff53d58c"},{q="Who are the Rot Hide gnolls and why are they here?",a="The Rot Hides are a vicious clan of gnolls inhabiting Silverpine Forest, operating primarily out of Fenris Isle and prowling the shores of Lordamere Lake. Unlike common gnolls, they are afflicted by the plague of undeath, bearing patchy gray fur and rheumy, yellow eyes. They wage a brutal guerrilla war against the Forsaken, scavenge battlefields, and fiercely assault anyone who nears their camps.",al={"rot hide gnolls","why are gnolls in silverpine","rothide gnoll silverpine"},it="threat",add="6c73f41e",nx={19}},{q="Who is controlling the Rot Hide gnolls?",a="The Rot Hide gnolls are under the thrall of Thule Ravenclaw, a treacherous necromancer aligned with the Scourge. From his stronghold on Fenris Isle, Thule uses dark magic to manipulate these blighted beasts, sending them to exhumed battlefields to harvest fresh corpses for his growing legions of undead.",al={"who commands rot hides","rot hide master","who leads the rothides"},sp=1,it="threat",add="ad054bc9",bt={"q437.6"}},{q="What is the Dead Fields?",a="The Dead Field is a blighted expanse of farmland in central Silverpine, along the road leading toward Lordamere Lake. Once a peaceful agricultural homestead, it became a mass killing ground during the Third War when the Scourge overran Lordaeron. Today, it is an open graveyard littered with shallow graves and disturbed earth.",al={"dead fields silverpine","the dead field","what are the dead fields"},it="place",add="97f89d60",nx={21}},{q="Why are the gnolls digging in the Dead Fields?",a="The Rot Hide gnolls are excavating the Dead Field to unearth the human corpses buried there during the Third War. Acting on the orders of Thule Ravenclaw, they dig up bodies and preserved remains to supply the necromancer with raw material for constructing Scourge constructs and reinforcing his undead army on Fenris Isle.",al={"why are rothides digging","gnolls dead fields why","gnoll digging corpses"},sp=1,it="motive",add="d487a8f2",bt={"q437.6"}},{q="What's on Fenris Isle?",a="Fenris Isle is a large island situated within Lordamere Lake off Silverpine's eastern shore. It is dominated by Fenris Keep, a former military fortress of Lordaeron that has fallen into dark disrepair. Today, the island serves as a heavily fortified redoubt swarming with Rot Hide gnolls and the undead minions of Thule Ravenclaw.",al={"fenris isle","what is on fenris isle","fenris keep"},it="place",add="3bca491d",nx={23}},{q="Why does Hadrec want Fenris Isle attacked?",a="Hadrec recognizes Fenris Isle as the beating heart of the Scourge threat in eastern Silverpine. Leaving Thule Ravenclaw entrenched in Fenris Keep gives the Scourge an unassailable staging ground to raise undead gnolls, raid supply caravans, and threaten the eastern approach to Tirisfal. Striking the island is crucial to breaking Thule's power and securing the lake.",al={"why attack fenris isle","hadrec fenris isle motive","assault on fenris isle reason"},sp=1,it="motive",add="bd044bca",bt={"q437.6"}},{q="Are the Dalaran wizards in Ambermill working with the Alliance?",a="Yes. While Dalaran focuses heavily on rebuilding its devastated city, the Kirin Tor forces stationed at Ambermill remain openly friendly to the Alliance and fiercely hostile to the Horde. Dalaran frequently dispatches aid to Silverpine's surviving human enclaves, opposing Forsaken expansion and working closely with southern remnants.",al={"ambermill dalaran alliance","is dalaran with alliance here","kirin tor alliance silverpine"},it="allies",add="574e415e"},{q="Who is Arugal and what is 'Arugal's Folly'?",a="Archmage Arugal was a Dalaran wizard who, in desperation to defend against the Scourge during the Third War, turned to forbidden magic and summoned monstrous wolf-beasts known as worgen. However, the feral beasts turned on the Kirin Tor wizards and innocent locals alike, spreading a ravenous lycanthropic curse across southern Silverpine. Driven mad by guilt and horror at what he had unleashed, Arugal retreated into Shadowfang Keep, adopting the worgen as his 'children.'",al={"arugal","arugals folly","who was arugal","archmage arugal lore"},it="history",add="fd7851b2",nx={26,27}},{q="Where did the worgen come from?",a="The worgen are otherworldly wolf-beasts pulled across dimensions by Archmage Arugal. Seeking a weapon to bolster Dalaran against the Scourge during the Third War, Arugal conjured these creatures into Silverpine, where they quickly turned on their summoners and spread a transformative curse.",al={"where did worgen come from","worgen origin silverpine","how did worgen get here"},it="origin",add="f38b73fd"},{q="Is Arugal still alive?",a="Yes, Archmage Arugal is very much alive. Shrouded in madness, he resides high atop the towers of Shadowfang Keep, overlooking Pyrewood Village. From his fortress, he directs his pack of Shadowfang worgen and guards his twisted lupine domain from anyone bold enough to breach his gates.",al={"is arugal alive","where is arugal now","arugal status"},it="threat",add="fc903f13"},{q="What is Pyrewood Village?",a="Pyrewood Village is a human settlement nestled in southwestern Silverpine, directly beneath the imposing cliffs of Shadowfang Keep. It was left outside when Gilneas sealed the Greymane Wall before the Third War. Its surviving inhabitants struggle to maintain a semblance of normal life by day, though an ancient darkness consumes them once the sun sets.",al={"pyrewood village lore","what is pyrewood","pyrewood town"},it="place",add="5dc043c6"},{q="Where does all this lead after Silverpine?",a="Once you have stabilized Silverpine by confronting Thule Ravenclaw and purging Arugal in Shadowfang Keep, your journey typically leads east across the mountains into the Hillsbrad Foothills to support the Forsaken at Tarren Mill. Alternatively, many Horde travelers take a zeppelin to Kalimdor to campaign through the vast plains of the Barrens.",al={"where to after silverpine","next zone after silverpine","silverpine next step"},it="next_step",add="20eec241"},{q="How did I end up in Silverpine Forest?",a="You likely followed the southbound road out of Tirisfal Glades, passing through the mountain pass southwest of the Undercity ruins. Forsaken characters finish securing their northern home in Tirisfal and naturally press south into Silverpine to expand the fledgling empire. Alternatively, Horde travelers from other continents arrive via zeppelin outside Undercity before walking down the coast, while rare adventurers coming from the south might cross through Hillsbrad Foothills to reach these blighted woodlands.",al={"how did i get here","how do i reach silverpine","path to silverpine forest"},it="arrival",add="da147569"},{q="What am I supposed to be doing in Silverpine Forest?",a="You are here to help the Forsaken secure their southern frontier against mounting perils. Reporting to High Executor Hadrec and the Deathstalkers at the Sepulcher, you must counter the diseased Rot Hide gnolls raiding from the Dead Fields and Fenris Isle, root out Scourge necromancers like Thule Ravenclaw, and keep close watch on Dalaran's wizards entrenched at Ambermill. Farther south, you will also investigate the ravenous wolf-beasts terrorizing Pyrewood Village and the shadow cast by Shadowfang Keep.",al={"what is my mission here","why was i sent to silverpine","what are we doing in silverpine forest"},it="purpose",add="97a9302a"}},ang={["race:Undead"]="Silverpine is the Forsaken's front line south of Tirisfal Glades. The Royal Apothecary Society tests new concoctions here, while the Deathguard battles lingering Scourge agents.",["faction:Alliance"]="Alliance explorers find a hostile forest, with only a fragile Dalaran garrison at Ambermill and the cursed villagers of Pyrewood Village.",["class:Mage"]="Ambermill and the fall of Archmage Arugal into lupine madness make Silverpine a grim warning of Kirin Tor magic gone disastrously astray."},kw={"ambermill","arugal","fenris isle","greymane wall","pyrewood","rot hide","sepulcher","shadowfang","silverpine","silverpine forest"},rel={"zone:shadowfang","subzone:sepulcher","subzone:pyrewood-village","subzone:ambermill","subzone:fenris-isle","subzone:greymane-wall","quest:1014","zone:tirisfal"},m={levels="10-20"},src={"Silverpine Forest (Classic)","Silverpine Forest"}}
